    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61349&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Irrigation Technician",
      "description": "Job Title Irrigation Technician Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61349 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Learn more about The Ringling at https://www.ringling.org/about-ringling/careers/ . Responsibilities This position is responsible for pump repairs and maintenance, skill in working with variable frequency drives (VFDs), and hands-on experience with irrigation systems and troubleshooting. Monitors, adjusts, and repairs irrigation systems throughout campus for optimal performance. Reports issues to the Associate Director of Facilities & Grounds and makes recommendations for corrective measures. Performs preventive maintenance on irrigation systems. Diagnoses and troubleshoots system issues, including leaks, electrical faults, and pump malfunctions. Identifies and resolves problems with irrigation controls, wiring, piping, and sprinkler heads. Repairs, overhauls, and replaces defective parts on irrigation systems. Establish and monitor irrigation schedules to meet landscaping needs while prioritizing water conservation using equipment related to the trade including variable frequency drives (VFDs). Maintains tools and equipment to keep in clean, proper working order. Operates and maintains power tools, hand tools, and trenching equipment. Operates, maintains, manipulates, and extracts data from central irrigation system. Conduct regular inspections to ensure system efficiency and compliance with local water regulations. Completes work orders and submits paperwork in a timely manner. Maintains accurate records of irrigation schedules, repairs, water usage, and inventory. Orders parts and supplies for irrigation system maintenance and repairs. Maintains an accurate inventory of irrigation parts. Prepares water usage/consumption reports. Collaborates with the groundskeeping team to support plant health, landscape aesthetics, and grounds maintenance. Works with and trains grounds employees in irrigation system repair, modification procedures, and techniques. Maintains trees, plants, shrubs, flowers, and grass through pruning, mowing, trimming, planting, watering, leaf blowing, raking, and mulching. Fertilizes plants, shrubs, trees, and grass on a seasonal basis. Plants and transplants plants, trees, shrubs, and flowers. Monitors for disease, insect damage, and weeds; reports and treats as directed. Operates landscaping equipment (string trimmers, hedge trimmers, mowers, edgers, sod cutters, chainsaws). Designs and installs irrigation systems. Plans and installs manual and automatic irrigation systems (battery-operated, hydraulic, electrical). Performs trenching, backfilling, and other excavation activities required for irrigation installation. Provides information about the plants to visitors and responds to questions. Drives motorized vehicles to traverse campus. Performs other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations, including performing grounds work or general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum. Qualifications High school diploma and two years' experience. Relevant Technical or Vocational degree may substitute for experience. Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position including the ability to lift 50 pounds, walk long distances, and work in extreme weather conditions. Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of: Pump repairs and maintenance, skill in working with variable frequency drives (VFDs), and hands-on experience with irrigation systems and troubleshooting. The practices and the ability to perform skilled carpentry, painting, plumbing, electrical, HVAC, or other related trades work. Landscaping and groundskeeping techniques. Ability to: Perform groundskeeping work to include the transplanting, cultivation, pruning, and trimming of plants, shrubs, and trees. Safely operate machinery, tools, equipment and various types of motorized vehicles including but not limited to dump trucks, tractors, forklifts, pallet trucks, front-end loaders, and golf-carts. Identify safety hazards and take necessary safety precautions to establish a safe work environment Establish and maintain effective working relationships. Perform assigned responsibilities with minimal to moderate supervision. Understand and follow written and oral instructions. Prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously Troubleshoot, diagnose, maintain and repair a variety of equipment and machinery used in area of work. Contact Info For more information, technical assistance, or should you require accommodations for the application or interview processes, please contact Ringling Human Resources at 941-358-2773 or employment@ringling.org. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position has a salary range beginning at $40,000 + with final offer amount based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. Working Hours The primary working hours for this position are between 6:30 AM and 3:00 PM (with a 30 minute meal period) Monday - Friday. This role may be required to work a flexible schedule including nights, weekends and special events based on the needs of The Ringling. This position is eligible to receive on-call pay. The position incumbent is required to be accessible and available to return to work during off-duty hours as scheduled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63691&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Museum Custodian",
      "description": "Job Title Museum Custodian Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63691 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities This role serves as a member of the General Museum Housekeeping Team, performing custodial tasks such as floor maintenance, public restrooms cleaning and stocking, mopping, dusting, etc. Cleans and sanitizes all public spaces and restrooms throughout the Sarasota Campus Complex during the day. Restocks tissue, towels, and hand soap supplies. Completes assigned daily tasks in campus venue to include prepare the campus to open, cleaning glass, dusting, sweeping, mopping, and emptying wastebaskets. Respond to service calls. Clean special event areas as needed: clearing refuse and using appropriate tools to remove stains and scrub hard surfaces. Complete assigned work orders and stock custodial closets according to supply request sheets or as needed. Drives custodial golf carts to traverse the 66 acre campus to deliver supplies and carry equipment. Clear trash from Sarasota Campus Complex grounds and clean exterior surfaces. Empty and transport recycling. Performs custodial maintenance projects. Completes other duties and projects as assigned that support museum operations and provides general assistance for the Facilities department at the museum, which may include supporting events and general assistance as needed. Qualifications Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire Due to the need to drive golf carts in this role, applicants must be 18 years of age or older. 9th-grade education or higher Ability to meet physical requirements as determined by position, to include moving objects up to 45lbs, working with chemicals, climbing and descending stairs, standing and walking for extended periods. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to maintaining high standards of cleanliness and organization. Ability to: Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Work independently while contributing positively to a team environment. Recognize workplace safety hazards and implement appropriate safety precautions. Knowledge of the safe operation of custodial equipment, machinery, tools, and cleaning materials. Problem-solving skills with the ability to identify issues and take appropriate corrective action. Verbal fluency in additional language(s) besides English. Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2773. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $33,408 or higher annually. Final offer amount will be determined based on the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. This position is based in Sarasota, FL. Employees are required to wear the standard issue uniform while at work. This role is designated as essential and may be required to work before, during, or after an emergency museum closure. Working Hours Friday to Tuesday from 10:00 AM to 6:30 PM with a half hour meal period. Weekends, weekdays, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63694&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Postdoctoral Scholar - Webster",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Postdoctoral Scholar - Webster Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63694 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Postdoctoral Researcher in Genetics, Genomics, and Bioinformatics The Webster Lab in the Department of Biological Science at Florida State University invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher. Our lab investigates individual variation: we seek to understand why genetically identical individuals in a shared environment vary for both molecular and organismal phenotypes, and we then determine how genotype and environment can regulate this variation. We combine computational genomics, molecular biology, and experiments in Caenorhabditis elegans to address these questions. The successful candidate will help shape a project aligned with their interests and career goals. Projects may be fully computational or may combine bioinformatics with laboratory experiments. Funding for the position will be provided through either our lab's NSF CAREER award or startup funds, depending on the planned project. Responsibilities The postdoctoral researcher will analyze large genomic datasets, develop reproducible analysis pipelines, contribute to manuscripts and presentations, and collaborate with other members of the lab. The position requires thoughtful and efficient use of modern coding assistants as part of computational work, together with careful validation, documentation, and version control. Depending on the project and the candidate’s interests, responsibilities may also include designing and conducting experiments with C. elegans, mentoring junior researchers, and contributing to grant proposals. The position may be fully computational, or may be a split between computational and wetlab work; in either case, proficiency with bioinformatic analysis is a must. Qualifications A Ph.D. completed by the position’s start date in genetics, genomics, bioinformatics, molecular biology, evolutionary biology, or a closely related field Experience analyzing high-throughput sequencing data using bioinformatics Proficiency in at least one relevant programming language, such as R or Python Ability to work independently and collaboratively and to communicate research effectively Preferred Qualifications Experience working with C. elegans Experience with transcriptomic, epigenomic, or population-genomic sequencing data Experience developing reproducible computational workflows Interest in combining computational analysis with molecular or organismal experiments Helpful The lab is committed to supportive, individualized mentoring. The postdoctoral researcher and principal investigator will establish a mentoring plan and revisit it regularly through one-on-one meetings. Mentoring will include support for research independence, publishing, conference participation, fellowship and grant applications. Postdoctoral scholars have access to career-development programs, networking, travel awards, and other resources through FSU’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs . They may participate in the FSU Postdoctoral Association . Candidates interested in teaching may also pursue opportunities to serve as an instructor of record for a course, subject to departmental need and approval. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Amy Webster . Additional information about the lab is available here . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Compensation, mentoring, and professional development Salary will be commensurate with relevant postdoctoral experience and aligned with the current NIH NRSA postdoctoral stipend scale . The position also includes applicable FSU employee benefits. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applicants should submit (1) a cover letter describing their research experience, interests, and career goals; (2) a curriculum vitae; and (3) contact information for two references. Review of applications will begin October 26 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is flexible, but ideally will be between January and July 2027. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
