    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63473&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Admissions & Workflows Analyst",
      "description": "Job Title Admissions & Workflows Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63473 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Division of Enrollment Management - Technology Operations Unit Responsibilities The Division of Enrollment Management is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar , Office of Financial Aid , and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management’s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the students’ development and progression in their academic experience – from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families as well as to campus partners across the University. The Technology Operations Unit within Enrollment Management provides technology support, technology-based solutions, systems configuration, identity and data management, and analysis across the division. The unit works closely with subject matter experts in Admissions, Registrar, and Financial Aid to meet the operational and reporting needs of various stockholders across campus. Works collaboratively with Admissions staff and campus stakeholders to develop scalable solutions that improve data integrity, application processing, communication delivery, and student experience. Develops and maintains Slate workflows, forms, queries, rules, communications, and related system functionality. Analyzes business processes and operational requirements to identify opportunities for automation, efficiency, and process improvement through Slate. Develops and maintains advanced reporting tools to guide decision-making and improve recruitment effectiveness. Stays current on Slate capabilities and best practices and actively engages with peer institutions to share ideas and improve processes. Evaluates new feature requests and assesses their potential impact and feasibility. Serves as liaison and Slate support resource for designated talent-based admissions programs and populations, including but not limited to Music, Dance, Theatre, Studio Art, and Film. Collaborates with program staff and campus partners to develop and maintain application and review processes that support program objectives. Coordinates with departmental stakeholders to reconcile data, identify process issues, send communications to prospective students, and improve applicant experiences. Supports the day-to-day operations of the undergraduate Slate system by maintaining documentation, ensuring data integrity, and providing responsive support to internal and external users. Contributes to the Admissions knowledgebase and delivers training to new users to promote consistent and effective use of Slate. Participates in special events hosted by the Office of Admissions. Assists other sections during peak times in support of the goals of Enrollment Management. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications The ability to prioritize and organize multiple work assignments simultaneously. Experience with data management as well as using Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook or comparable software. Demonstrable technical experience to include handling configuration changes, modifications, enhancements and/or workarounds related to an application. Applicants should be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships and be able to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Preferred applicants should have a strong understanding of University admissions and recruitment processes. Previous work experience with admissions CRMs (Slate). Candidates with a strong sense of initiative and the demonstrated ability to manage multiple responsibilities concurrently are preferred. The ability to make sound judgments while working in a deadline-driven environment is essential. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $47,660, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62665&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Business Analyst - UBA Central Office",
      "description": "Job Title Business Analyst - UBA Central Office Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62665 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators Responsibilities Responsible for analyzing data, business processes, and systems to support operational efficiency and decision-making within the University Business Administrators (UBA) and for the Asst Vice President of Administrative Services. Performs advanced analytical work involving business process evaluation, data analysis and visualization, and reporting to support organizational goals. Provides advanced support on finance and administrative tasks and manages special projects for client sites. Develops statistical analysis methods for strategic planning within the University Business Administrators (UBA). Utilizes SQL, Snowflake, and data reporting tools to optimize queries, dashboards, and reports. Designs and maintains databases and dashboards and creates financial and statistical reporting systems. Reviews and analyzes UBA site reports and data to identify trends, formulate recommendations for process improvement and resource allocation, and implements solutions. Manages assigned projects and serves as a liaison to departments to review and communicate recommended solutions effectively both verbally and in writing. Evaluates, manages, and maintains specific reports, databases, and dashboards. Validates integrated data from multiple sources to ensure accuracy and business integrity. Provides leadership, advanced support, research, development and guidance on Finance and Administration related tasks for client sites. Serves in the absence of UBA senior staff and with varying operational project assignments. Responsible for working with UBA staff and the Deans, Directors, and Department Heads of assigned client sites to create reporting tools and put systems in place to implement and maintain operational efficiencies. Recommends policies and procedures to client site leadership to ensure compliance with federal, state, and university regulations and ensures proper internal controls. Independently maintains and troubleshoots core business applications. Uses in-depth knowledge of university system modules to extract, analyze, and interpret data to identify trends, opportunities, and improve processes. Successfully incorporates the use of university-approved AI systems to streamline data analysis and visualization. Contributes to requirement specifications, data mapping, diagrams, and flowcharts. Resolves complex issues, escalating to the Director when necessary. Collects and analyzes data, provides summary analysis, and investigates compliance matters. Acts as a liaison with internal stakeholders and F&A central offices for data reporting compliance. Develops and updates training resources, including work samples and presentations. Guides department representatives to resolve technical questions. Coordinates system overview trainings and other one-on-one trainings as needed. Creates technical manuals and job aids for the department. Serves as the Information Security Manager (ISM) and the SeminoleSecure Business Impact and Disaster Recovery Coordinator for the department. Ensures data is stored correctly and maintains emergency plans. Oversees the UBA website, technical tools, and form repository. Manages system permissions and documents position procedures. Works directly with the Director on any assigned special projects. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63264&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "College Life Coach (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Job Title College Life Coach (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63264 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Advising First – Division of Undergraduate Studies Coach Life Coaching Responsibilities Responsible for building trusting relationships with assigned roster of students. Provide coaching services that are personalized, constructive, engaging, motivating, and informative. Prioritizes and executes appropriate coaching actions to remove roadblocks to students’ success. Basic understanding of available technology that supports the college life coaching functions. Completes all corresponding administrative tasks associated with the position by the given deadlines. Responsible for maintaining appropriate documentation as it pertains to the goals of The Center for College Life Coaching. Takes a proactive approach to college life coaching by outreaching to assigned roster of students to invite them to engage in coaching, consistently outreaching to non-responding students, and sending meeting reminders. Responsible for seeking contact with students who are late to appointments and rescheduling as needed. Participates in trainings necessary to perform duties of a college life coach. Continues to improve coaching skills by pinpointing key areas of growth and actively participates in professional development. Participates in initiatives established by The Center for College Life Coaching, Advising First, and Undergraduate Studies. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Master's degree. Knowledge of University rules and regulations. Experience student advising, counseling, or experience working one-on-one with people in a professional or academic setting. Creative problem-solving skills. Prior student advising, counseling, or experience working one-on-one with people in a professional or academic setting. Computer skills to include experience with Microsoft Office and web-based applications. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously with minimal to moderate supervision. Prior customer service experience and/or experience working with students in an educational setting. Ability to deal with people in a calm, confident manner and with complete objectivity. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. Will have access to student data which is covered under the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act. Position requires a high level of discretion and knowledge of legal issues in relation to confidentiality of data. Ability to extract complex academic information from various sources and maintain confidentiality. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $44,184, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
