    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63066&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Event Logistics Assistant (OPS/Part-Time)",
      "description": "Job Title Event Logistics Assistant (OPS/Part-Time) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63066 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities This role provides logistical setup of venues for events, both large and small. Responsibilities include: Carrying & moving tables, chairs, lighting, and other event-related equipment around the Ringling's 66-acre campus. Setting up and operating A/V equipment. Ensuring logistical setups are completed prior to event start time and cleared promptly at the close of the event. Assisting with oversight of vendor load-ins and load-outs. Interfacing with clients, vendors, guests, and Museum staff with a focus on customer service. Enforcing established rules and policies for sound, guests, and vendor conduct. Maintaining the safety of property, in conjunction with the security department. Attending weekly planning meetings and maintaining event equipment and supplies. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid Florida driver’s license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Preferred Qualifications Experience with: Event logistics A/V equipment Customer service Ability to: Respond calmly to urgent situations Effectively communicate and problem-solve Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $16.22 per hour (20 hours per week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to adhere to the business dress standards. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours This role has a dynamic schedule that is determined by planned events at The Ringling. Events are scheduled at a minimum of 2 weeks in advance of an event. Events are scheduled at various times, including days, evenings (as late as 1:00 AM), weekends, and holidays. Additional support is often needed during high season each year between October and May. Weekends, days, evenings, or holidays may be required as needed by Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63690&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Media Specialist- Public Affairs (National High Magnetic Field Lab)",
      "description": "Job Title Media Specialist- Public Affairs (National High Magnetic Field Lab) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63690 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU). FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities This position supports the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory’s public affairs and outreach efforts through the creation of digital, print, and multimedia communications. The position develops content and visual materials that promote the Lab's research, education, events, and community engagement initiatives, while supporting communications across web, social media, print, and other outreach channels for audiences at all three MagLab sites. Key Responsibilities: Conceptualize, design, and produce visually compelling print and digital marketing collateral, including brochures, reports, infographics, newsletters, promotional items, and other communication materials. Ensure consistency with MagLab branding and visual identity standards across communication products and platforms. Collaborate with the Public Affairs team to write, edit, and produce content that reaches and engages the Lab's audience map. Coordinate the Public Affairs team's community outreach portfolio, including Science Nights at the Library. Develop new hands-on experiences, cultivate and manage community partnerships, and expand outreach opportunities. Play a strong role in organizing, developing, and executing new visitor and community engagement experiences at MagLab Open House and other public-facing events. Implement creative communication strategies that advance the Lab's goals, strengthen stakeholder relationships, and build deeper trust with internal and external audiences. Support the Public Affairs Director and broader Public Affairs team with departmental initiatives, including proofreading, editing, Open House planning and execution, tours, special projects, and other communications needs as assigned. Support internal communication efforts through strategic and timely contributions to channels including the MagBLAB newsletter and the MagNET intranet. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience in graphic design & brand management Experience in email campaign marketing Experience in content creation Adobe Creative Suite proficiency, including Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign. Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Caroline McNiel . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
