      "title": "Program Manager for Learning & Development of The Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project (ROTA)",
      "description": "Job Title Program Manager for Learning & Development of The Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project (ROTA) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63680 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Stoops Center for Communities, Families, and Children The CFC Center was created by the Stoops Family Foundation, Inc. to generate and sustain translational knowledge development for effective policies, services, and usable research for the promotion of communities, families, and the children of Florida, the nation, and across the globe. Responsibilities Leads the design, development, implementation, and improvement of ROTA training curricula, webinars, e-learning modules, blended learning courses, and related educational resources. Provides curriculum development and instructional design support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Manages ROTA educational content and functionality within the online learning platform and content repository. Oversees the organization, accessibility, quality, and maintenance of digital learning resources. Provides learning platform, digital content, and resource development support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Manages ROTA certification programs and processes for trainer preparation, instructional consistency, and fidelity monitoring. Oversees training standards and quality across learning activities. Provides certification, trainer preparation, and training quality support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Develops and oversees ROTA technical assistance for participants and rural organizations, including implementation coaching, virtual support, and other learning-focused assistance. Provides technical assistance, implementation support, and learning-focused consultation for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Reviews ROTA participant data, evaluations, feedback, and training outcomes and uses findings to guide improvements to curricula, resources, certification activities, and technical assistance. Provides training evaluation and continuous improvement support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Provides learning and development expertise and supports training, technical assistance, and related activities for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and special initiatives as assigned based on organizational needs and priorities. Performs special projects and related duties that support Stoops CFC Center programmatic and organizational goals. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience in a related science or research services field or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience (Note: combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
