      "title": "Program Manager for Operations of The Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project (ROTA)",
      "description": "Job Title Program Manager for Operations of The Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project (ROTA) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63679 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Stoops Center for Communities, Families, and Children The CFC Center was created by the Stoops Family Foundation, Inc. to generate and sustain translational knowledge development for effective policies, services, and usable research for the promotion of communities, families, and the children of Florida, the nation, and across the globe. Responsibilities The Program Operations Manager will manage the day-to-day administrative and programmatic operations of the Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project across all five project goals. The position will coordinate project implementation, administrative processes, timelines, logistics, and reporting requirements to ensure project goals and deliverables are met. The position will also support other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned based on organizational needs and priorities. Manages administrative scheduling and logistical coordination for ROTA webinars, in-person trainings, certification courses, Consortium meetings, and project events. Maintains project calendars and coordinates schedules, materials, communications, and other administrative requirements in collaboration with project staff. Provides administrative, training, meeting, and event coordination for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Manages administrative and operational activities associated with the ROTA annual needs assessment, including focus group scheduling, survey distribution logistics, records, and activity tracking. Coordinates administrative communication among project leadership, staff, Consortium members, and partners. Provides needs assessment, project coordination, communication, and activity-tracking support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Coordinates ROTA reporting processes and deadlines and works with project leadership and staff to collect, organize, and prepare information and documentation required for SAMHSA reporting and other project requirements. Provides reporting, documentation, and compliance support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Supports other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, special initiatives, and administrative activities as assigned based on organizational needs and priorities. Performs special projects and related duties that support Stoops CFC Center programmatic and operational goals. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience in a related science or research services field or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
