    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63677&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Manager for Outreach of The Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project (ROTA)",
      "description": "Job Title Program Manager for Outreach of The Rural Opioid Technical Assistance Regional Project (ROTA) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63677 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Stoops Center for Communities, Families, and Children The CFC Center was created by the Stoops Family Foundation, Inc. to generate and sustain translational knowledge development for effective policies, services, and usable research for the promotion of communities, families, and the children of Florida, the nation, and across the globe. Responsibilities Develops and implements ROTA outreach strategies to engage rural communities throughout Southeast Region. Build relationships with community- and faith-based organizations, recovery groups, consumers, family members, and other stakeholders. Travels throughout Southeast Region to support community engagement, partner meetings, outreach activities, and events. Provides community outreach and engagement support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Develops and adapts ROTA outreach messages, materials, and communication strategies for rural audiences. Promotes ROTA resources and opportunities and connects community members and organizations with relevant programs, services, and resources. Provides outreach communications and resource promotion support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Coordinates ROTA community outreach, recruitment, application activities, onboarding, engagement, and ongoing communication for the State Ambassador Program. Maintains relationships with ambassadors and supports their participation in project outreach activities. Provides ambassador, stakeholder, and community engagement coordination for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Coordinates ROTA community-facing activities associated with the traveling library exhibit, including outreach to potential sites, site relationships, scheduling, promotion, and coordination with state library offices and project partners. Provides coordination and support for community-facing activities and initiatives for other Stoops CFC Center programs and projects as assigned. Develops and maintains relationships with state, regional, and national partners to support ROTA activities and initiatives. Recruits community participation in the annual needs assessment, symposium, and other ROTA activities. Provides partnership development and community participation support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Coordinates with ROTA project leadership and staff to share outreach information, participation updates, and other documentation needed to support project implementation and reporting. Provides communication, coordination, and documentation support for other Stoops CFC Center programs, projects, and initiatives as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience related to administrative services or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63685&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Training Specialist, SLP - Florida Center for Interactive Media",
      "description": "Job Title Training Specialist, SLP - Florida Center for Interactive Media Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63685 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Center for Interactive Media Responsibilities Produce and/or review technical assistance materials that support the development and implementation of quality services for students. Maintain current knowledge on appropriate practices related to speech/langauge impaired, deaf/hard of hearing, and visually impaired. Utilize available resources to provide assistance in other areas related to students. Research, analyze, and recommend guidance, policies and procedures related to federal and state requirements, curriculum, and instruction for students. Provide technical assistance through workshops, presentations, meetings, etc. to FDOE and constituents to support quality services for students. Perform other duties assigned related to the development and implementation of quality services for students. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires the successful completion of a Level 2 Background Check by the Florida Department of Education. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
