    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63609&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Digital Humanities Librarian, 12 Month Salaried",
      "description": "Job Title Digital Humanities Librarian, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63609 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Libraries Responsibilities The Digital Humanities Librarian serves as the advanced technical lead for CreateFSU, the Libraries' academic web-hosting service, providing expert consultation and technical support for faculty and student digital scholarship initiatives. This position collaborates closely with the DRS team, the AI and Data Lab, and campus partners to advance digital research methodologies, expand access to emerging technologies, and support the university's mission of research excellence and student success. The successful candidate will help empower researchers and students to explore, create, and share new forms of scholarship while contributing to a vibrant and growing digital humanities community at FSU. Support Digital Scholarship and Research Innovation Serve as the advanced technical lead for CreateFSU and related web-hosting platforms, providing consultation, troubleshooting, and support for complex digital scholarship projects. Assist faculty, graduate students, and researchers in developing and sustaining digital humanities projects using a variety of publishing and web-based platforms. Develop and maintain technical documentation, tutorials, and user guides that support digital research and publishing initiatives. Advance Student Learning and Research Skills Collaborate with DRS colleagues to design and deliver workshops, instructional programming, and technical training through initiatives such as the Digital Research Incubator. Provide instruction in digital research methods, programming, data analysis, and related technologies, helping students and researchers build practical skills that support academic and professional success. Partner with faculty to integrate digital humanities tools, methodologies, and assignments into undergraduate and graduate curricula. Build Campus Partnerships Consult with faculty, students, and staff on digital research projects, scholarly communication, and emerging technologies. Foster collaborative relationships with partner units, including the Research Computing Center and the Interdisciplinary Data Humanities Initiative. Serve as a resource for campus digital scholarship efforts and contribute to strategic initiatives that enhance research capabilities across disciplines. Contribute to Professional Excellence Engage in ongoing professional development and scholarly activities related to digital humanities, digital scholarship, and academic librarianship. Participate in library, university, and professional service activities. Stay informed of emerging trends, technologies, and best practices that advance digital research and scholarship. Qualifications Master's degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program; or Master's degree in a humanities discipline, digital humanities, or a closely related field with relevant technical experience. Demonstrated ability to independently learn and apply new technologies, software applications, programming languages, and web-based tools. Understanding of current research trends, emerging technologies, and methodological shifts in the digital humanities. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to public service and user-centered support. Strong collaborative mindset and adaptability in a fast-paced, evolving organizational environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing technical support, debugging, or administration for web-hosting platforms (e.g., WordPress, Reclaim Hosting). Proficiency in programming languages common to humanistic research, such as Python or R. Familiarity with web development technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) for site customization and troubleshooting. Demonstrated experience designing and delivering technical instruction, workshops, or academic presentations. Ph.D. in a humanities or related digital studies field. Other Information University Libraries seeks a collaborative and technically skilled Digital Humanities Librarian to help shape the future of digital scholarship, research innovation, and student learning. Located within the Office of Digital Research and Scholarship (DRS), this position provides an exciting opportunity to partner with faculty, researchers, and students on innovative digital humanities projects while helping develop technical skills and research capabilities that support academic success. Join us in advancing discovery, scholarship, and student success through the power of digital humanities and emerging technologies. At FSU Libraries, you will have the opportunity to: Collaborate with innovative faculty, researchers, and students on impactful digital scholarship projects. Help prepare students with the digital research and analytical skills needed for academic and career success. Work in a collaborative environment that values creativity, innovation, continuous learning, and professional growth. Contact Info Dr. Aaron Rodriguez , Director of Digital Research and Scholarship University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63666&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Enrollment Management Specialist (Student Affairs/Admissions - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Job Title Enrollment Management Specialist (Student Affairs/Admissions - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63666 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Student Affairs/Admissions - College of Medicine Responsibilities Manages academic and administrative processes for enrollment within the Division of Student Affairs and Admissions (DSAA) at the College of Medicine. Manages all aspects of the electronic student files to include maintaining the security of student records, uploading all applicable documentation, processing acceptance documents, tracking enrollment requirements and posting all final degrees to the official student record. Acts as primary point of contact for all admitted students and enrolled students in the Bridge, MD, and PA degree programs. Counsels and corresponds with all incoming and currently enrolled students, providing information on guidelines and policies for University and college enrollment requirements. Manages scheduling courses and registration for all Bridge, MD, and PA courses each semester. Supports enrollment responsibilities as needed for Genetic Counseling degree program. Assists with managing student information and different academic calendars for all the cohorts for MD and PA. Assists Enrollment Manager with tasks related to graduation, degree certifications, licensure requirements, data reporting, and related tasks. Assists the division staff with student functions such as Orientation, Graduation, White Coat ceremony, actively participating as part of the DSAA team. Requires driving to transport sensitive documents on campus. Qualifications Bachelor's degree or higher and two years of experience. Valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Melinda McDaniel Program Manager Enrollment Services University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary: mid $40,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . May require occasional evening and weekend hours. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63688&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Facilities Supervisor",
      "description": "Job Title Facilities Supervisor Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63688 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Custodial Services Department Responsibilities Works along with staff to ensure the overall cleanliness (interior & exterior) of the Union complex, Askew Student Life Center, Students Services Building, & Circus. Implements cleaning and training procedures. Responsible for planning & scheduling work assignments to the designated zone staff. Conducts a walk through inspection of areas in each zone (Inspects custodial closets, storage rooms & custodial equipment to ensure that it is being properly secured & maintained.) Works closely with Assistant Custodial Supervisor to provide consistent cleaning procedures and services for day & night shifts. Responds to requests for spills, cleanups and trash/recyclable collection. Works with Building Services Administration/Human Resources/Director on all administrative personnel matters, i.e. time sheets, appointments, Employee Performance Appraisals, overtime requests, special events manpower & equipment needs. Communicates facility & equipment repairs needed in complex. Assists with the development and enforcement of policy & procedures, & work standards. Ensures that university departmental rules are followed (regarding dress code, leave, authorized breaks, work hours, sanitation, etc.). Communicates to others: rules, policies, procedures, & standards of the department and the university, reviews leave requests. Other duties assigned but not limited to: Replaces and recycles light bulbs per University standards. Assists with setups for banquets and special events including but not limited to moving furniture, equipment, and setting up stages. Monitors and reports all unusual conditions that arise throughout the complex Coordinator of Physical Plant and other through hand-held radio. Hand-held radio must be worn at all times. Coordinates and performs the recycling program and hazardous waste. Maintains MSDS & Hazardous Materials management Program. Disposes trash in dumpsters. Collects and coordinates the collecting of recyclable products (plastics, glass, aluminum) from the recycling bins in the Oglesby Union. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years' experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Relevant training may substitute for experience. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Ten (10) hour workday, Sunday though Wednesday. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63661&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "IT Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Title IT Services Coordinator Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63661 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU’s Department of Information Technology Services (ITS) Responsibilities This position serves as a member of the Information Technology Services (ITS) Service Desk, which is first point-of-contact for the university community. The Service Desk provides support associated with support and service requests submitted by faculty, staff, students, and affiliates, ensuring timely resolution of technical issues and service requests while maintaining consistent, high-quality customer experience. The role is responsible for managing customer interactions across multiple channels, including phone, chat, web, and the FSU Service Center case management system. Responsibilities include real-time intake, triage, and troubleshooting of technical issues; fulfillment of service requests; and comprehensive case documentation from initiation through resolution or escalation. The position is expected to exercise independent judgment in diagnosing issues, determining appropriate resolutions, and identifying when escalation is required. Collaborates within a team environment to ensure the timely processing of service and support requests for ITS services. Responsible for data integrity and quality control for order processing system from order receipt, translation of user needs into standard telecommunications language using appropriate order forms, coordination of all resources (internal and external) to meet timely fulfillment, order status, accurate billing information, and ensuring customer follow-up and satisfaction. Uses reporting tools (predefined and custom reports in order system) to identify and correct billing, order routing, and informational errors. Designs, maintains and generates management reports to support all functions. Conducts regular on-site customer visits, training and follow-up for clarification of service and support requests of all ITS products and services. Makes recommendations and coordinates additions, changes and enhancements based on customer contact, and oversees implementation, if necessary. Works with colleagues on special promotions and events, as necessary, and maintain strong customer relationships by utilizing a team approach for the distribution of workload and ensure quality control through customer contact. Acts as a team leader or team member, either independently or with other areas of ITS/FSU on special projects to implement or enhance ITS's products and service. Performs and completes multiple tasks and projects simultaneously in a time-sensitive manner. Liaison to a multitude of outside vendors, campus departments, and internal/external customers to ensure customer satisfaction and appropriate turnaround times for fulfillment of all requests to ensure smooth operations for all activities. This position may require the use of a University or state vehicle, golf cart, and utility vehicle may be needed to reach site premises, a valid driver's license will be needed to operate a vehicle. Performs duties in compliance with ITS policies, guidelines, and processes pertaining to support requests, work orders, project management, change management, and incident management. Appropriately utilizes associated tools in accordance with ITS standards. May be required to carry a university cell phone during normal working business hours (8 AM - 5 PM). Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and four years' experience or a combination of post high school or education and experience equal to four years. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in CRM systems and AiM Work Order Management. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? A professional who has really great time management skills and exceptional customer service skills. What is a typical day in this position? Interacting with external vendors, service providers and departmental budget managers and IT Professionals. What can I expect in the first 60-90 days? A complete understanding of the FSU Service Portfolio and support workflows. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63657&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering-Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering-Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63657 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for teaching faculty positions in the field of Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in graduate courses and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to teach graduate-level classes (in-person and online), and have a strong interest in using technology in engineering education. Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 200+ graduate students, ~1000 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $27M. We are starting our graduate programs (MS-Aero and MS-Mechanical) at the FSU Panama City (PC) campus. We expect the candidates to be part of our faculty at the FSU PC campus and to collaborate with our existing faculty at the Tallahassee campus. Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint university is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Unnikrishnan Sasidharan Nair, Search Committee Chairperson, usasidharannair@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page teaching statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed teaching plan will connect with existing courses in the department and universities. A 1-page research statement (optional) Two selected publications for review (optional) The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information We are interested in candidates with backgrounds in Mechanical & Aerospace engineering who can teach graduate-level courses, including but not limited to Aerodynamics, Fluid Dynamics, Aerospace Propulsion, Aerospace Structures, Dynamics & Controls, and Mechanics & Materials. Other areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering will also be considered, particularly if they complement the department's existing strengths. The positions are at the Teaching Faculty I level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered for a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on January 4, 2027. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63361&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Travel Assistant (Herbert Wertheim College of Business)",
      "description": "Job Title Travel Assistant (Herbert Wertheim College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63361 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Originates travel requests, cash advances, travel, and expense reimbursements to Wertheim College of Business students through Concur. Works directly with students traveling on behalf of the Wertheim College for student professional development opportunities, including travel requests, expense reports, and other methods that adhere to University policies and procedures. Holds a Travel Card. Responsible for reconciling monthly financial statements for Wertheim College travel and student professional funds. Works with the Senior Travel Administrator to monitor area travel budgets and report to the Dean’s office. Ensures that expense reports are flowing correctly and check payments have been reconciled or redistributed as needed. Communicates and interprets University policies and procedures with the appropriate directors, department chairs, faculty, staff, and students. Assists the Assistant Director for Finance and Administration and Assistant Dean for Finance and Administration to develop controls to ensure compliance with the University policies and procedures. Partners with Wertheim College Business Analyst to support and maintain reporting system for students with eligible professional development funds. Partners with the Wertheim College’s Student Engagement team and Business Career Services office to promote professional development opportunities to students. Educates students on proper utilization of funds. Assists the Senior Travel Administrator in processing other travel transactions during peak periods. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of relevant experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Contact Info Nicole Folkert Senior Travel Administrator University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63579&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Warren and Margot Coville Photography Internship - Spring 2027 (Part-Time/OPS)",
      "description": "Job Title Warren and Margot Coville Photography Internship - Spring 2027 (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63579 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University. Responsibilities The Warren and Margot Coville Photography Intern will: Work with the Curator of Photography and New Media to research objects in The Ringling's photography collection in order to update or correct catalog records. Assist in research and create bibliographies and summary reports on selected artists and/or photographs. Locates applicable resources onsite in the Ringling Museum's Art Library or identifies potential loans from other institutions. Assist the curator with the weekly survey of the paper storage vault on-site to view, assess, and research photographs. Assist in the planning and research for upcoming exhibitions. Qualifications Applicant must be currently enrolled in an undergraduate program at a college. Knowledge and skill using Microsoft Office Suite/Microsoft 365. Ability to lift boxes or books up to 15lbs. Preferred Qualifications Robust organizational and time management skills. Proficiency in Adobe Acrobat. Skill in online and library-based research. Ability to take direction and work independently. Experience compiling bibliographies in Chicago or MLA style. Students majoring or minoring in art, art history, or the humanities, especially with an interest in photography or the history of photography. Helpful Learning Outcomes Develop art history research skills Gain a better understanding of the history of photography Understand best practices for safe handling, care, and storage of photographic objects Develop skills in curatorship within a professional museum environment Length of Internship The internship will be during the Spring 2027 semester. The start date is flexible beginning January/early February 2027 and ending early May 2027 (maximum of 16 weeks). Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.45 per hour (8 to 10 hours per week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Your application is not considered complete without the following items attached: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcripts Considerations This is an OPS/Part-Time job This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. Work Location: Sarasota, FL Please note this will be an in-person internship experience, not remote. Employees are required to adhere to the business dress standards. Working Hours 8 to 10 hours per week on weekdays, with a flexible schedule. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63662&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) - FSU Health Lifestyle Medicine Clinic",
      "description": "Job Title Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) - FSU Health Lifestyle Medicine Clinic Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63662 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The first clinic of its kind, the FSU Health Lifestyle Medicine Clinic combines the holistic approach of functional medicine with the expertise of nursing faculty. Our clinic comprises of nurse practitioners and faculty members of the FSU College of Nursing . Together, these practitioners can address the root causes of many illnesses and provide a unique approach to care that combines standard medicine with lifestyle habits to treat and prevent chronic illness. Responsibilities Provide high-quality, patient-centered Primary and Lifestyle Medicine care that aligns with the clinic's focus, goals, and objectives while adhering to current standards of care. Performs comprehensive physical examinations and evaluates patients presenting with health concerns across FSU Health clinics and other assigned clinical practice locations. In accordance with applicable Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) protocols, scope of practice, and clinic policies, assesses and diagnoses illnesses and injuries and develops appropriate plans of care. Orders and interprets diagnostic laboratory tests, imaging studies, and other procedures as medically indicated. Initiates evidence-based treatments, interventions, referrals, and follow-up care consistent with established clinical protocols and current standards of practice. Incorporates Primary and Lifestyle Medicine principles, including prevention, health promotion, chronic disease management, and patient education, into the delivery of patient-centered care. Maintains professional, respectful, and responsive communication with patients, families, clinic staff, healthcare partners, and other external parties. Documents the patient history, physical and emotional state, diagnostic findings and treatment in the patient’s medical record/EMR. Reviews and discusses with patient the results of laboratory, x-ray, and other procedures. Makes indicated referrals to other specialists/consultants as necessary. Collaborates with the physician and/or APRN’s regarding patient management as clinically appropriate. Provides medication refills and addresses other clinical needs for clinic patients, including coverage for other nurse practitioners when they are unavailable, to ensure continuity of care and timely response to patient needs. May perform indicated minor surgical and non-invasive diagnostic procedures. Qualifications Graduate from an accredited Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioner program. Valid Florida licensure as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (in accordance with Chapter 464, Florida Statutes). Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification or the ability to obtain one within 30 days of hire. Within 30 days of hire, the candidate must provide: Documentation of Tetanus immunization within 10 years. Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician, reporting negative results. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63667&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Job Title Custodial Worker (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63667 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Custodial Services Responsibilities Cleans blinds, baseboards, windowsills in parlor and office; dusts, polishes furniture and vacuum carpet. Cleans all bathroom areas by scrubbing and disinfecting toilets, showers and lavatories, empties and cleans sanitary cans, tissues boxes and waste baskets; cleans student kitchens; sweeps entrance walks and building entrances. Dust mops floors and stairwells; cleans trash chute rooms; dust walls, doors, ceiling, baseboards and transoms in entire building. Collects trash from trash barrels on each floor to be picked up by the city collectors. Mops, waxes, and buffs floors in areas assigned. Checks reports and replace light bulbs that need replacing and cleans trash containers regularly. Apply disinfectants, deodorizes and other chemicals by spray method for sanitation purposes; performs other duties as assigned by supervisor. Qualifications 9th Grade Education Preferred Qualifications Preferred experience in custodial work. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63649&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Foundations (Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried), Medical Education - College of Medicine",
      "description": "Job Title Director of Clinical Foundations (Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried), Medical Education - College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63649 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Medical Education - College of Medicine Responsibilities Florida State University College of Medicine (FSU MED) invites applications for the position of Director of Clinical Foundations within the Office of Medical Education. This faculty leadership position provides strategic and operational leadership for the implementation, management, assessment, and continuous improvement of the first two years of the undergraduate medical education curriculum. The Director is responsible for supporting academic excellence, curricular integration, educational innovation, and the successful transition of medical students from the pre-clerkship curriculum to their clinical education. This is a faculty position reporting to the Associate Dean for Undergraduate Medical Education, with responsibility for leading the implementation, management, assessment, and continuous improvement of the M1 and M2 curriculum. The Director works collaboratively with course directors, faculty, staff, and medical education leadership to promote academic excellence, curricular integration and innovation, and alignment with the College's educational program objectives, mission, and applicable Liaison Committee on Medical Education (LCME) accreditation standards. The Director oversees the planning, delivery, and evaluation of the pre-clerkship curriculum, including curricular activities, educational assessments, course and examination processes, and student learning outcomes. The Director serves as Chair of the Year 1 & 2 Subcommittee of the Curriculum Committee and as an ex-officio member of the Year 3 & 4 Subcommittee and Curriculum Committee, providing leadership for course review, curricular evaluation, outcomes assessment, continuous quality improvement, and accreditation activities. Responsibilities also include oversight and analysis of National Board of Medical Examiners (NBME) examinations, the Comprehensive Basic Science Examination (CBSE), and USMLE (United States Medical Licensing Examination) Step 1 preparation and outcomes. The Director will also oversee the College of Medicine Course Master Schedule with support from MED Administrative Services, as needed. The Director provides leadership and supervision for Office of Medical Education staff supporting the pre-clerkship curriculum and supports the development of course directors and faculty. Working with medical education leadership and other College programs, the Director contributes to strategic planning and integration of the four-year undergraduate medical education curriculum, supports students' successful transition to the clinical years, and represents the College on appropriate committees and initiatives related to medical education. The successful candidate will be considered for appointment at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor level, with academic rank determined based on qualifications and experience and in accordance with College and University criteria. Qualifications Ph.D., M.D., D.O., M.D./Ph.D., or other appropriate terminal degree from an accredited university in a discipline relevant to medical education and the responsibilities of the position. For physician candidates, board certification or board eligibility and eligibility for medical licensure in the State of Florida, as applicable. Demonstrated record in undergraduate medical education, including experience with curriculum development, course leadership, educational assessment, program administration, or related medical education activities. Demonstrated leadership experience within a school of medicine, academic health center, or comparable academic environment. Strong organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with demonstrated ability to manage multiple complex academic initiatives and priorities. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to academic excellence, professional development, collaboration, stakeholder engagement, and fostering an educational environment that supports the College of Medicine's mission. Previous experience as a medical school course director, curriculum director, or in another significant leadership role within undergraduate medical education. Demonstrated record of teaching, educational scholarship, scholarly activity, and/or service appropriate to the academic rank sought. Knowledge of LCME accreditation standards and experience supporting accreditation, continuous quality improvement, or institutional medical education program evaluation. Experience with educational program evaluation, assessment of learner outcomes, and continuous quality improvement. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, academic leaders, and other stakeholders across organizational and disciplinary boundaries. Experience with competency-based medical education, curricular mapping, educational program objectives, and horizontal and vertical curriculum integration. Experience with NBME examinations, CBSE, USMLE Step 1 outcomes, or other medical student assessment programs. Experience leading multidisciplinary teams and supervising professional staff in an academic or medical education environment. Contact Info Linda Netherton University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position is Non-Tenured and Non-Tenure Earning. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63660&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Immigration Advisor",
      "description": "Job Title Immigration Advisor Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63660 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Center for Global Engagement Responsibilities This position will provide immigration-related services and advise international students enrolled in F-1 status. Serve as a Department of Homeland Security Designated School Official regularly submitting updates to the federal immigration (SEVIS) database to comply with regulatory reporting responsibilities and to authorize or recommend immigration benefits. Interpret and apply federal immigration regulations to support students in their maintenance of lawful F-1 status. Effectively use the Sunapsis database to ensure accurate immigration-related records. Assist and guide students with solving problems and identifying resources. Work closely with academic departments, university Human Resources, and other units throughout FSU. Engage in extensive and frequent communication by phone, Teams/Zoom, email and in-person with enrolled international students in F-1 status, other CGE team members, FSU faculty and staff, community, employers, and representatives of government agencies on issues related to federal F-1 immigration regulations (e.g. enrollment, graduation, transfer/change of level, employment authorization, extension of stay, etc.), general immigration laws that impact students in F-1 status (e.g. registration documentation, address reporting, international travel, change of status, etc.), and other state and federal policies. Help create supportive environment for international students. Work closely with academic departments, Admissions, Registrar, Student Finance, Division of Student Affairs departments, and other partners across campus. Hold multiple roles in FSU databases, with access to input and change visa codes, place and remove holds, view basic admissions information, student account information, student addresses, and student enrollment information, etc. Participate in the development and testing of new electronic forms developed by the Program Director for Data and Compliance, recommend updates to current forms and form communication, and provide feedback on data feed and data extract issues. Access daily the federal government immigration (SEVIS) database and Sunapsis to enter determinations regarding continuing eligibility for F-1 status, process employment authorizations (Curricular Practical Training) or recommendations (Optional Practical Training), update academic program changes, transfer immigration records to other U.S. institutions, and submit other required updates within regulatory reporting periods. Maintain accurate background information and documentation in Sunapsis to support the submitted SEVIS updates as required by regulations. Monitor daily auto-assigned cases in Sunapsis to identify immigration status issues and to review and process submitted electronic forms. Use Sunapsis communication tools to contact students regarding their cases to ensure consistent advising. Deliver regular Optional Practical Training workshops in person and via Zoom in rotation with other CGE advisors. Participate in new international student orientations each semester by giving presentations, checking students in, and/or guiding short tours. Play a role in the semesterly ACIREMA interactive simulation activity for the university community. Assist with developing and providing additional presentations and workshops for international students and the FSU community. Attend trainings offered by Undergraduate Advising, Human Resources, Research Compliance, and other areas. Contribute to CGE assessment efforts as needed. Participate in major CGE events and programs. Serve on DSA and/or CGE committees as needed. Provide back-up support to other advisors and to front desk. Participate in professional associations for international educators. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Applicant must be a U.S. citizen or permanent resident due to federal SEVIS database requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in international affairs, higher education, or closely related field. Experience as a Designated School Official and/or Alternate Responsible Officer using SEVIS regularly. Experience using Sunapsis, Terra Dotta, or other case management software. Ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and efficiency. Experience presenting information in one-on-one, small group, and large group settings both in-person and online. Evidence of strong professional writing skills and ability to analyze complex information. Experience living, studying, or working abroad and knowledge of a second language. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting in the high $40,000’s to low $50,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applicants must upload a cover letter when completing the online application. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applicants will begin on October 16, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61585&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain, College of Business)",
      "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain, College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61585 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain | College of Business Responsibilities The Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems, and Supply Chain (BAISSC) at Florida State University’s Herbert Wertheim College of Business invites applications for a teaching faculty position (non-tenured track, 9 months salaried). The start date is August 2027. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in the areas of Business Analytics and Information Systems. Possible graduate level and/or additional course offerings may be available depending on qualifications. Qualifications An earned doctorate or other terminal degree from an accredited institution in a field closely related to Business Analytics or Information Systems is required. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience in areas such as Operations Management, Business Analytics, and/or Management Information Systems. Contact Info For inquiries regarding this position, please contact: Dr. Noyan Ilk Department Chair Department of Business Analytics, Information Systems & Supply Chain University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application materials include: 1) A letter of interest 2) Curriculum vitae 3) Three letters of reference This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will remain open until January 15, 2027. For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 15, 2026, when application reviews will begin. Applications received after this date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63560&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist (The Collegiate School at Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Job Title Administrative Specialist (The Collegiate School at Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63560 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Collegiate School | Panama City The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City is a developmental research laboratory charter school associated with the College of Education, Health and Human Sciences (Anne’s College) at Florida State University. In this capacity, TCS serves as a center for innovative instructional programming, research and program evaluation, and professional development solutions for the educational community. TCS will begin its fourth year of operation in August 2026, with grades 9-12. The mission of The Collegiate School at Florida State University, Panama City, is to provide rigorous academic studies and career development for students who aspire to meet the ever- changing and complex workplace demands of the 21st century. Resources and expertise available through Florida State University and the local community will prepare students to thrive in the competitive global market as they identify and pursue career goals through academic and career training. Responsibilities Assists the Business Manager with reconciliations. Monitors information maintained in the internal accounting system for accuracy and compliance. Serve as the primary contact for procurement, purchasing, and contract management. Oversees revenue collection, deposits, and accounts receivable activities. Assists the Business Manager with data collection and reporting for TCS School Board Financial meetings and annual financial audit. Serves as P-card proxy and Procurement Representative to ensure the propriety of the payments, compliance with prompt payment and other applicable laws, policies, and procedures of the State of Florida and FSU. Creates ePRFs when applicable for vendor payments. Serves as the school HR and Payroll Representative, ensuring proper approval of and payment of personnel in accordance with university, state, and federal requirements. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Experience with managing budgets, procurement, contracts, or office operations. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Proficiency with Mircosoft Office Suite. Familiarity with university policies, Foundation operations, or event coordination. Proficiency with content management systems and/or Adobe Creative Suite Helpful The Collegiate School at Florida State University, Panama City (TCS) seeks a compelling, innovative, engaging, and enthusiastic Administrative Specialist. We invite applications for this full-time position, starting this fall. This Administrative Specialist will join The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City, in its fourth year of operation, with the mission of providing collegiate studies and career readiness to students in the Bay County area. Contact Info Debbi Whitaker , Director - The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $40,910, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. The position will begin in Fall 2026. This position will be on campus at FSU Panama City in Panama City, Florida. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63650&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, 12 Month Salaried - The Graduate School",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, 12 Month Salaried - The Graduate School Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63650 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Graduate School Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs serves as a member of the Graduate School's senior leadership team and provides strategic leadership for graduate academic affairs, policy development, academic quality, student success initiatives, and graduate program administration. The Associate Dean works collaboratively with the Dean, Graduate Program Directors, college leadership, faculty, students, and university stakeholders to advance the academic mission of the Graduate School and support excellence in graduate education. The Associate Dean supervises one full-time professional staff member and serves as a primary resource for graduate academic policy interpretation, implementation, and assessment across the university. Academic Policy Leadership Provide leadership for the development, implementation, interpretation, and periodic review of graduate academic policies, procedures, and standards. Direct and advise Dean on graduate student appeals and exceptions processes including, admissions appeals, enrolled student appeals, time extensions, and other exception requests. Recommend policy revisions to support student success, academic excellence, and regulatory compliance. Collaborate with university leadership, colleges, and departments to ensure consistent application of graduate policies. Monitor emerging issues, best practices, and national trends in graduate education and recommend appropriate responses. Graduate Academic Programs and Quality Assurance Provide oversight for graduate academic program review processes and continuous improvement efforts. Support academic units in the development of new graduate degrees, certificates, concentrations, and program modifications. Coordinate review of graduate curriculum proposals and academic program changes. Promote innovation and excellence in graduate education through evidence-based practices and strategic initiatives. Graduate Student Success and Academic Progress Lead policy initiatives that promote graduate student retention, progression, completion, and professional development. Guide university-wide policy approaches to graduate academic support and student success. Review complex academic issues involving graduate students and recommend resolutions consistent with university policy. Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and administrative units to ensure student success. Leadership and University Collaboration Serve as a member of the Graduate School senior leadership team. Represent the Graduate School on university committees, work groups, task forces, and external organizations. Foster productive relationships with Graduate Program Directors, department chairs, deans, faculty, and student groups. Provide and maintain Graduate Program Director resources, including GPD Orientation, the GPD Handbook and the Graduate Student Handbook. Collaborate with other Graduate School leaders on strategic planning, assessment, accreditation, and institutional initiatives. Supervision and Administrative Management Supervise, mentor, and evaluate one full-time professional staff member. Establish goals, priorities, and performance expectations for supervised personnel. Support the efficient administration of academic affairs functions within the Graduate School. Monitor workflows and implement process improvements. Other Duties as Assigned Undertake special projects and initiatives assigned by the Dean. Serve on university committees or represent the Graduate School at institutional and professional events. Perform other duties consistent with the responsibilities of an Associate Dean. Qualifications Academic master's degree or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate or terminal degree in an appropriate discipline from an accredited institution. Tenured faculty member at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Record of scholarly achievement and professional accomplishment sufficient to maintain graduate faculty status. Demonstrated experience in graduate education administration, academic leadership, program leadership, or related responsibilities. Knowledge of graduate academic policies, curriculum development, and academic program administration. Experience working collaboratively with faculty, academic administrators, and students. Demonstrated commitment to student success and academic excellence. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to supervise, mentor, and support professional staff. Ability to interpret and apply university policies, procedures, and regulations. Academic administrative experience as a department chair, associate chair, graduate program director, assistant/associate dean, or similar leadership role. Experience with graduate student success, admissions, retention, and completion strategies. Experience developing or revising academic policies and procedures. Experience working with faculty governance structures and university committees. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships across academic and administrative units. Record of leading major projects or managing complex organizational initiatives. Contact Info Brian Barton , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please submit a cover letter outlining your interest in the position, leadership experience, and qualifications relevant to the responsibilities of the Associate Dean role. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: After submitting your application, click the Careers link Click the My References link Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Appropriate rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. The distribution of effort between the administrative assignment within the Graduate School and teaching, research, service, and/or other faculty responsibilities in an academic department will be determined based on the selected candidate's qualifications and experience. Financial Disclosure may be required. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63647&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Associate - Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Program Associate - Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63647 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Coordinates and maintains student files and all related components for the Sport Psychology program (Master's and doctoral levels) from initial contact as applicants, through their graduation from the program, and beyond. Admission tasks, which occur on an annual cycle for Fall admission, include but are not limited to: preparing and regularly updating standard communication letters for applicants to be uploaded to Slate, communicating with applicants by e-mail and phone; calculating GPAs for faculty review; alerting faculty about strong completed applicant files for fellowship consideration; sending related admissions paperwork to OASIS for processing and serves as liaison with that office. Maintaining and evaluating admission statistics for the Sport Psychology program, including GRE score tracking, GPA tracking, and related information; reporting on admissions activities to the Sport Psychology faculty. Converts admissions files into permanent student files and maintains updated and accurate inventories of these files. Communicates graduation lists to Sport Psychology coordinators. Recommends policies and procedures related to admissions activities in Sport Psychology. Assists with academic advising activities of the Sport Psychology program. Processes travel for the Educational Psychology and Learning Systems department. Travel tasks include but are not limited to: entering T-auths and Expense reports for approval in Concur; collecting back-up receipts and other required documentation for travel processing; maintaining accurate records of all travel T-auths and Expense reports. Communicates with travelers regarding necessary documentation. Requires knowledge of various budgets related to travel (E&G, Auxiliary, C&G, Foundation), several of which are outside the department. Processes non-travel reimbursements in Concur as required. Creates and maintains the Course Schedule Master (CSM) each semester for entire EPLS department, working with faculty program coordinators and Associate Chair to gather accurate and complete data for CSM building. Processes Drop/Add slips, DIS, preliminary exams, dissertation hours, defenses, and similar coursework for all students in the Counselor Education and Combined PhD in Counseling and School Psychology programs. Advises students on policies and procedures related to coursework, Drop/Add, defenses, deadlines, timelines, signatures, programs of study, and all other registration and academically related matters. Processes departmental textbook orders each semester in conjunction with CSM building. Assists Senior Administrative Specialist with tuition waiver entry and tracking, FACET and AOR activities, Promotion and Tenure activities and serves as secondary attendance and leave representative. Serves as P-card proxy for the department, reconciles weekly charges against receipts and submits monthly reconciliation report with back-up to the Purchasing Department. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience providing administrative support in a higher education or academic environment. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to interpret academic program requirements and provide advice. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Experience processing travel, reimbursements, purchasing, or other financial transactions. Contact Info Bryan Richards , Search Committee Chair/Department Manager University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62604&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty - DNP Core Coordinator, 12 Month Salaried",
      "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - DNP Core Coordinator, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62604 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire a collaborative Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) Core Course Coordinator responsible for coordination of one or more courses within the DNP core curriculum, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide leadership and oversight for assigned DNP core course(s), including maintenance of the master syllabi and course structure. Ensure alignment of course objectives, assignments, and evaluations with DNP Program Outcomes and AACN Essentials (2021) competencies. Coordinate course implementation across multiple sections and faculty instructors, ensuring consistency in expectations and grading standards. Collaborate with program leadership to support sequencing and scaffolding of scholarly deliverables across the DNP curriculum. Support development of competencies related to evidence-based practice, systems leadership, quality improvement, and practice change initiatives. Provide guidance and support to faculty of record and adjunct instructors teaching the course. Monitor course outcomes, student performance trends, and evaluation data to support continuous curriculum improvement. Contribute to program evaluation, accreditation documentation, and curriculum planning activities as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. This role focuses on high-quality didactic instruction in the graduate nursing program and supports the college’s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship, and academic service in a collaborative, on-campus environment. For more information about our academic programs, please visit the following link: Academics | College of Nursing . Qualifications An academic doctorate (PhD, DNP) or highest-level terminal degree in nursing from an accredited institution is required, with eligibility for graduate faculty status. Non-nurse trained candidates will not be considered. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Three to five years of teaching experience in graduate nursing education. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of DNP education standards and AACN Essentials (2021) Experience with curriculum development, course coordination, or program evaluation Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. Other Information This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. Contact Info Inquiries about the positions may be directed to Dr. Susan A Baker , Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In your application, please include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Do not include reference letters in your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised as opened until filled. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62755&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty - FNP Coordinator, 12 Months Salaried - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty - FNP Coordinator, 12 Months Salaried - College of Nursing Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62755 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Nursing Join a nationally recognized leader in nursing education, known for research distinction and educational innovation. With simulation space in a brand new $126 million FSU Health building, $12 million to design a new building, and a transformative $10 million gift, the FSU College of Nursing is hiring additional faculty for strategic growth. Responsibilities The FSU College of Nursing is seeking to hire a collaborative educator to teach in our graduate program, based in Tallahassee, Florida (FL). Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Actively work with the Assistant Dean for Graduate Program to develop and revise Graduate Curriculum. Assume an active role in recruiting prospective graduate students to the FNP (Family Nurse Practitioner) major; Review potential plans of study with prospective students. Maintain pertinent professional organization membership and assume leadership roles in professional organizations that support FNP practice and education. Teach Core Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) or FNP courses as assigned; assume lead responsibility for practicum courses within program. Conduct DNP and certificate FNP Program orientation activities. Oversee Objective Structured Clinical Evaluation (OSCE) within track. Work with Clinical Coordinator to recruit high-quality clinical preceptors. Manage student clinical rotations in conjunction with assigned clinical faculty. Work with the Assistant Dean for Graduate Program to forecast student enrollments in track courses. Work with Clinical Coordinator to execute PEPs, or preceptor forms/letters as needed. Review and verify clinical logs of DNP and certificate FNP students, providing student and faculty feedback, as appropriate. Review and monitor clinical hours for graduate students. Track certification requirements and results for Graduate Program. Evaluate transfer credits for FNP students in conjunction with the Assistant Dean. Complete and conduct FNP student annual review (May - June) and guide students through admission, matriculation and completion of major related courses. Complete education verification forms for certification. Other duties as assigned in the coordination of track-related activities as the lead faculty program track faculty member, such as but not limited to: supporting new faculty teaching in both didactic and practicum courses (orient to course syllabus, set up Simple syllabus as needed, orient students and relevant faculty to the track, track courses, and track-related activities) This role focuses on high-quality instruction in the graduate nursing program and supports the college’s mission to prepare practice-ready, compassionate nurse leaders. Faculty are expected to be actively engaged in teaching, student mentorship and academic service in a collaborative environment. For more information about our academic programs, visit our Academics page . Qualifications An academic doctorate (PhD, DNP) or highest-level terminal degree in nursing from an accredited institution is required, with eligibility for graduate faculty status. Non-nurse trained candidates will not be considered. Active FL Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) license; or licensed in another state with eligibility to obtain FL licensure within 30 days of hire. Two to three years of teaching experience in graduate nursing education. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of DNP education standards and AACN Essentials (2021). Experience with curriculum development, course coordination, or program evaluation Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work well with students, faculty, and staff at all levels within a collaborative environment. Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook or equivalent software. Experience supervising and training employees. Experience meeting project deadlines. Other Information This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. Contact Info Inquiries about the positions may be directed to Dr. Susan A Baker , Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In your application, please include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) including a listing of courses developed and taught Teaching Philosophy, not to exceed two pages Please do not include reference letters in your application; they will be collected later in the recruiting process. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time, in-person position, and the level is commensurate with experience. Successful candidates must relocate to Tallahassee, Florida. Up to three official teaching evaluations from your most recent teaching experiences may be requested later in the recruiting process. This position is being readvertised as open until filled. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63642&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Meteorology)",
      "description": "Job Title Teaching Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried (Meteorology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63642 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science I College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean, and Atmospheric Sciences (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track, 12-month Teaching Faculty I position beginning Fall 2027 to teach undergraduate meteorology courses for majors and non-majors. We are particularly interested in candidates who can teach synoptic and broadcast meteorology. A full-time specialized faculty member in the Teaching Track (Teaching Faculty I, II, III) shall normally be assigned not less than 75% teaching responsibility and not more than 5% research responsibility, averaged over any academic year. This typically is represented as approximately eight 3-credit courses a year, with course reduction possible for substantial service roles such as academic advising or the TV Meteorology Program studio manager. Qualifications A Ph.D. or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in Meteorology or Atmospheric Science or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience is required, with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching. M.S. applicants with substantial teaching or broadcast meteorology experience post-degree are encouraged to apply. Other Information EOAS has 37 tenured/tenure-earning faculty, 3 teaching faculty, about 350 undergraduate students, about 100 graduate students, a student population, and grants undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. For additional information on EOAS research and FSU’s facilities and resources, please visit our website . The undergraduate meteorology degree program is large (typically 30 students each year) with a long and distinguished history dating back over 75 years. Contact Info Inquiries may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Prof. Robert Hart . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching interest/philosophy, and contact information for three references who can provide letters of recommendation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin immediately. The deadline for receipt of applications is November 13, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63653&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist - Office of the Senior VP for Finance & Administration",
      "description": "Job Title Administrative Specialist - Office of the Senior VP for Finance & Administration Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63653 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of the Senior Vice President for Finance & Administration Responsibilities This position will provide high level administrative support to the Office of the Senior Vice President for Finance & Administration, and includes the duties as listed below: Assist Sr. Administrative Specialist with financial and HR functions including employee onboarding, P-Card reconciliations, vendor and contract management, and other duties as assigned Assist Executive Assistant to Senior Vice President with clerical duties including answering phones, data entry, filing documents, scheduling appointments, sorting mail, and other duties as assigned Assist with travel bookings, expense reports, and reimbursements using Concur Assist with preparation and execution of departmental and divisional meetings and events. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Must have a valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Experience with FSU OMNI system and SAP Concur. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63476&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist - UBA/Herbert Wertheim College of Business",
      "description": "Job Title Administrative Specialist - UBA/Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63476 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators – Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities This position is responsible for managing administrative functions with a primary focus on faculty and a shared focus on USPS and A&P employees within the Herbert Wertheim College of Business (HWCOB), respective schools, departments, programs, and institutes. Faculty Personnel Administration Serves as the primary administrator for faculty personnel processes within the HWCOB, liaising between the college and its campus partners. Coordinates in consultation with the Assistant Director on faculty recruitment, RAMP screening, work authorization processes, appointments, reappointments, onboarding, assignments of responsibilities (AOR), FACET reporting, annual evaluations, promotion and tenure, post-tenure review, sabbaticals, leave requests, overloads, and other faculty employment actions. Interprets University policies and provides recommendations based on knowledge of the organization's business administrative objectives and activities. Ensures compliance with university regulations, collective bargaining agreements, policies, procedures, and deadlines. Maintains faculty personnel records and prepares required documentation and reports. Serves as a resource to college staff, faculty, and administrators regarding faculty personnel procedures. Staff Personnel Administration Provides shared transactional support for USPS and A&P personnel actions across the HWCOB. Collaborates with departmental team members to coordinate recruitment, hiring, onboarding, personnel transactions, evaluations, leave administration, funding changes, position updates, separation processes, and related duties. Provides guidance to supervisors, interpreting and applying university HR policies and procedures. Refers complex policy interpretation issues to the Assistant Director as appropriate. Ensures personnel documentation is processed accurately and timely. Provides backup support for faculty personnel administration functions. Records, Reporting, and Compliance Maintains departmental personnel records and tracking systems, monitors personnel deadlines, and prepares reports and documentation. Tracks departmental HR transactions throughout the workflow cycle, providing timely status updates and advising staff and supervisors on required actions, next steps, and appropriate procedures. Serves as a key resource and quality control checkpoint for departmental HR transactions initiated by supervisors, ensuring accuracy, policy alignment, and adherence to established standards. Utilizes myFSU Business Intelligence (BI) to generate cyclical HR Actives and cost center reports, reconciling appointments, compensation levels, and funding distributions to maintain data integrity. Prepares payroll certification documentation and HR Actives reports for leadership review, providing critical support in validating payroll accuracy and ensuring compliance with internal controls and audit requirements. Process Improvement and Administrative Support Identifies, recommends, and implements departmental HR process improvement initiatives. Contributes to special projects, communications, and operational support activities. Provides cross-training and backup support for other departmental HR functions as needed to ensure continuity of operations and customer service. Other duties as assigned for the HWCOB. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting human resources functions in a higher education environment Experience coordinating faculty personnel processes or academic employment actions Strong organizational, communication, and customer service skills University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63648&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Strategy, Assessment, and Innovation",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Director for Strategy, Assessment, and Innovation Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63648 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Center for Leadership and Service Responsibilities The Assistant Director for Strategy, Assessment & Innovation is responsible for developing and managing a wide range of grants and research that focuses on the development and incorporation of leadership and service as vital parts of a liberal arts education. This position is responsible for the grant portfolio of the Center for Leadership and Service, in addition to leading a team focused on the development and dissemination of research, data collection and analysis, assessment and innovation across the Center for Leadership and Service. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of and the ability to apply the principles and practices to strategically align tasks and people with organizational goals and objectives. Ability to demonstrate effective customer service skills. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to demonstrate critical thinking based upon in-depth data, substantiating information, considering and respecting others' input personal values, and ethics. Ability to prepare and monitor budget information. Ability to prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. Ability to provide leadership and direction in programmatic, budgetary, and operational functions. Ability to train and supervise employees. Ability to solicit donors. Knowledge of federal, state, and private sources for contract and grant funds. Knowledge of the principles and practices of project planning, development, and evaluation Skill in public speaking. Ability to perform assigned responsibilities with minimal to moderate supervision. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Mid $50,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63516&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Vocal Coaching, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Vocal Coaching, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63516 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music - Voice & Opera Area Responsibilities The qualified candidate will coach graduate voice majors in preparation for degree recitals and opera productions and will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to mentoring students. The candidate will also teach appropriate vocal-related courses in undergraduate and graduate sequences, including diction and song literature. Musical collaboration for faculty recitals will be expected. Additional responsibilities may include instructing graduate collaborative piano students; serving as Music Director of Opera Workshop; mentoring Opera Graduate Assistants; and contributing to other instructional and artistic activities appropriate to the candidate’s experience and expertise. Qualifications Candidate will have completed a doctoral degree in collaborative piano or a master's degree with equivalent professional experience with a record of achievement as an actively performing, collaborative artist. Knowledge of and experience in working as a vocal coach with professional proficiency in English, French, German and Italian lyric diction is required. Candidate must have experience coaching opera and vocal repertoire, across all major historical periods, at the post-secondary and/or professional level. The ideal candidate must be open to a range of musical styles and approaches to learning and teaching, recruitment, creative activity, and service. Preferred Qualifications Experience in Spanish, Russian and/or Czech is desired. The qualified candidate should demonstrate extensive experience performing and collaborating with vocal artists at the collegiate and/or professional levels. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and demonstrated ability/interest in working in a collegial and mutually supportive environment is expected. Other Information FSU Opera encompasses three fully staged opera productions each year with orchestra; up to two outreach opera productions; curricular Opera Workshop and Opera Literature courses; MM programs in opera coaching and opera stage direction; and fully staged opera scenes programs. The qualified candidate will be an experienced and proficient opera coach and rehearsal accompanist and will contribute as a member of the FSU Opera team. Additional opportunities and responsibilities may be available depending on the candidate’s experience and expertise. The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist Other inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair as follows: Dr. Marcía Porter , Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application Materials: Cover letter, one to two pages CV Names and contact information for five references Links to performances of operatic and art song repertoire in a variety of languages, 20 to 30 minutes Vocal coaching video of the candidate coaching singer(s) from the piano, 20 to 30 minutes All videos and recordings must be from the last five years Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 15, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63616&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Interior Design, 9 Month Salaried - School of Design",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Interior Design, 9 Month Salaried - School of Design Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63616 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Design Responsibilities Florida State University invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty position in Interior Design program at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. We seek a collaborative educator and scholar who will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education through innovative teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and student mentorship. The successful candidate will advance human-centered design, evidence-based inquiry, and creative and critical thinking while preparing students to address complex challenges in the built environment. Candidates should demonstrate expertise that complements and expands the program’s strengths and the ability to connect design inquiries with professional practice. We welcome contributions to interdisciplinary teaching and scholarship, graduate education, and the thoughtful integration of emerging technologies into design. Teach undergraduate and graduate studio, lecture, and/or seminar courses in interior design. Contribute expertise in Construction Documents, Construction Systems, Commercial Office and Hospitality Design, with flexibility to support other areas of the curriculum. Develop and sustain a program of research and/or creative scholarship, disseminate work through appropriate peer-reviewed or juried outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students; advise graduate research and creative work; and chair or serve on thesis committees. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation activities. Contribute to interdisciplinary collaboration and the integration of research, creative inquiry, and professional practice into teaching. Provide service to the academic unit, College, University, community, and profession, as appropriate to rank and assignment. Participate in relevant academic and/or professional organizations. Qualifications An earned master’s or doctoral degree in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field with substantial working experience Demonstrated teaching experience with Adobe Creative Cloud and Autodesk products, and familiarity with rendering & 3D visualization software (e.g., Enscape). Demonstrated ability to teach interior design studios and related courses effectively. Demonstrated ability to develop a sustained program of research and/or creative scholarship. Proficiency in design communication and the application of relevant design technologies in teaching, practice, and/or scholarship. Effective oral, written, and visual communication skills. Ability to collaborate with colleagues and support student learning and development. Candidates for appointment at the Assistant Professor rank should demonstrate promise in teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and service. Candidates for appointment at the Associate Professor rank should demonstrate a sustained record of teaching effectiveness, research and/or creative achievement, and service commensurate with appointment at that rank at Florida State University. Preferred Qualifications An MFA, M. Arch, PhD, or equivalent terminal degree in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field, completed by the appointment start date. Expertise in emerging design technologies (e.g., AI, VR, AR, etc.) and their thoughtful application to design education and inquiry (research/creative components). NCIDQ certification, architectural licensure or NCARB certification, and/or other relevant professional credentials. Teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Professional practice experience in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or related areas. Experience mentoring graduate students and supporting their thesis research or creative scholarship. Experience with interdisciplinary teaching, research, or collaborative design practice. Evidence of external funding activity or potential to develop externally supported projects. Familiarity with Council for Interior Design Accreditation standards and accreditation processes. Other Information The Interior Design Program in the School of Design at Florida State University emphasizes human-centered design, evidence-based design processes, and creative and critical thinking. The program prepares students to contribute to human health, safety, and well-being through the environments and experiences they design. Situated within the College of Fine Arts, the program offers opportunities to connect design education with broader artistic, scholarly, and interdisciplinary inquiry. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development of undergraduate and graduate education and help strengthen the program’s research and creative contributions. The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Search committee chair, Daejin Kim , Ph.D., Associate Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. A letter of interest addressing qualifications, teaching expertise, and anticipated contributions to the program. A curriculum vitae. A teaching statement of one to two pages. A research and/or creative scholarship statement of one to two pages. A PDF portfolio containing 10–20 examples of research, creative, professional, and/or teaching-related work. Identify the applicant’s role in collaborative projects and distinguish student work from the applicant’s own work. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to MiKayla Jackson, Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. mjj22e@fsu.edu Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Review of applications will begin on December 15 and continue until the position is filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63645&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Brand Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Job Title Brand Graphic Designer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63645 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Marketing Responsibilities The Brand Graphic Designer creates self-service toolkits, templates, and brand asset libraries that help colleges, departments, and sub-brands produce compliant communications while allowing the central creative team to focus on strategic and executive priorities. Design, launch, and manage a comprehensive library of self-service templates (via Canva for Enterprise, Adobe Express, or similar platforms) for use by campus communicators. Work with campus partners to identify areas of need and future template expansions. Develop standardized, plug-and-play toolkits for recurring campus needs, including event flyers, digital signage, social media avatars, and presentation decks. Provide brand consultations and training sessions for internal marketing and communications personnel across campus, teaching them how to effectively utilize the design systems. Gather feedback and improve training offerings. Assist in evaluating brand identity requests from various campus groups, ensuring clarity between academic, institutional, and marketplace sub-brands. Serves as representative to the director of branding when needed. Provide art direction and design support for major, university-wide strategic initiatives, internal marketing and communications conferences, and high-visibility institutional campaigns. Collaborate closely with fellow University Marketing graphic designers to ensure brand cohesion at all levels of university activity. Commit to continuous learning by staying abreast of industry trends and emerging marketing technologies. Foster a culture of continuous learning within the team. Mentor team members on branding principles, ensuring ongoing skill development through on-the-job training and staying updated with industry publications and training. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and three years of experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to seven years. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63658&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Business Manager",
      "description": "Job Title Business Manager Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63658 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Institute for Child Welfare Responsibilities Supports financial operations and implements efficient workflow processes. This includes budget management, procurement, expense and payroll corrections, reconciliations, financial analysis, and budget forecasting. Reviews transactions for accuracy and compliance. Must demonstrate clear knowledge of financial and accounting practices and university financial guidelines. Reviews and approves travel, purchasing transactions, and PCard transactions, ensures accurate chart field information, appropriate expenditures, and compliance with University requirements. Assists with post-award activities with the responsibility of maintaining the Contracts and Grants financial tracker, prepares financial and encumbrance reports, and supports year-end close-out, carryforward planning, and contract budget allocations. Drafts standard operating procedures, implements financial tools, completes institutional reporting requirements, and manages scholarship administration. Provides administrative and financial support to the Associate Director of Administration and completes assigned special projects. Works closely with executive leadership, program directors, staff, and students to meet financial and administrative needs while ensuring adherence to University guidelines. Participates in Institute initiatives, staff meetings, events, and professional development activities. Qualifications Bachelor's degree with two years of experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and relevant experience equal to six years) Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of financial accounting principles (GAAP), post-award experience, budget management and reconciliation, financial and data analysis, knowledge of procurement practices, advanced-level administrative support experience, excellent communication (verbal and written). Helpful The Florida Institute for Child Welfare is housed at the Florida State University College of Social Work. The purpose of the institute is to advance the well-being of children and families by improving the performance of child protection and child welfare services through research, policy analysis, evaluation, and leadership development. Suggested to visit Florida Institute for Child Welfare for more information. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary of $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63644&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Laboratory Assistant - Kopania (OPS)",
      "description": "Job Title Laboratory Assistant - Kopania (OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63644 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Dr. Emily Kopania's laboratory in the Department of Biological Scienc e at Florida State University (https://ekopania.github.io/ and https://www.bio.fsu.edu/). Our lab seeks to understand how selective pressures interact with developmental and functional constraints. We primarily do this by studying two different biological systems: (1) The evolution of vision in fish and (2) The evolution of reproduction in rodents. Our work integrates cutting-edge genomics and transcriptomics techniques with phylogenetic comparative approaches to understand molecular and trait evolution. Responsibilities The primary duties of this role include, but are not limited to, the following: Helping to set up a molecular genomics laboratory and fish husbandry facility. Performing molecular laboratory experiments. Examples include DNA and RNA extraction and library preparation, immunohistochemistry, and microscopy. General lab upkeep and organization, such as ordering supplies, scheduling, and maintaining supplies and equipment. Managing a fish (trout) facility through tasks such as regular feedings, health checks, and water quality monitoring. Mentoring and training others in laboratory techniques. Qualifications B.S. or B.A. degree (or higher) in the life sciences or related field. Exceptions may be made for students with laboratory research experience who are finishing their degrees this year. At least one year of experience in a biology laboratory. Proficiency with Microsoft Suite (Excel, Word, Teams) and Google Docs. A strong interest in evolutionary biology and genomics. Excellent time management, communication, and problem-solving skills. Strong ability to work with a team of students and researchers Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with molecular biology laboratory techniques. Previous experience working with animals in research settings, especially fish. Anticipated Salary Range Competitive salary commensurate with experience. Fringe benefits included. Ideal start date would be in October 2026 but is flexible based on candidate availability. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Please send your CV, a one-page statement describing your past research experience and interest in the position, and contact information for at least two references to Dr. Emily Kopania . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the position will remain open until filled. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . A full-time (40 hours/week), in-person research assistant position. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63460&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Medical Office Receptionist | FSU SeniorHealth",
      "description": "Job Title Medical Office Receptionist | FSU SeniorHealth Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63460 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine | Florida Medical Practice Plan (FMPP) FSU SeniorHealth™ 2390 Phillips Rd Tallahassee, FL 32308 Responsibilities You will act as the first point of contact to patients who walk in or call to schedule an appointment, and will promote an atmosphere of teamwork in accomplishing the mission and goals of FMPP. Schedule patient healthcare appointments for multiple clinics. Answer all calls according to FSU SeniorHealth policies and procedures in a timely and professional manner, screen incoming phone calls, answer routine questions and forward inquiries to appropriate departments. Verify patient insurance eligibility status, register patients, and provide information and support to patients regarding available healthcare services. Check patients in and out in a professional, timely, and hospitable manner. Collect required payments at the time of service and appropriately balance deposits. Maintain confidentiality follow applicable laws regarding personal health information. Attend departmental meetings and serve on committees as required. Exhibit a willingness to float to all areas of need for administrative support including check in, check out, referrals or other administrative area as necessary across FMPP clinics. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalency and two years of experience; or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to two years. Valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following is required: Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician, reporting negative results within the past six (6) months. Documentation of physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician within the past six (6) months. Within 30 days of hire, the candidate must provide: Documentation of Tetanus immunization within 10 years. Documentation of Hepatitis B vaccine or positive antibody titer. Preferred Qualifications Ability to take patient vital signs when a Certified Medical Assistant is unavailable. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will travel to Westminster Oaks, at 4449 Meandering Way, a couple days per week. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63643&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Professional Development Trainer/Bootcamp Instructor, ASCENT (Panama City Campus) (Multiple Vacancies) (Part-time, OPS)",
      "description": "Job Title Professional Development Trainer/Bootcamp Instructor, ASCENT (Panama City Campus) (Multiple Vacancies) (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63643 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department ASCENT - Office of Professional Engagement and Learning (OPEL) Florida State University is one of the nation’s top 25 public universities and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the sparkling waters of the Gulf. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ Responsibilities Providing classroom, online, or hybrid instruction in professional development and bootcamp formats. Fulfilling all contractual obligations during the term. Delivering training sessions aligned with pre-approved curricula and industry standards. Preparing thoroughly for each session and adhering to schedules. Leveraging modern teaching technologies, including learning management systems (LMS) and web-conferencing tools. Engaging learners actively, providing timely responses to questions and offering support or referrals when necessary. Collaborating with ASCENT staff to ensure seamless delivery and high-quality learner experiences. Assisting in the development and refinement of training content, as needed. Maintaining accurate records of attendance, grades, and evaluations, as applicable. Completing annual compliance training and adhering to university policies. Performing additional duties as assigned by the OPEL Program Manager. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Relevant industry certifications, coupled with two or more years of field experience. Preferred Qualifications Proven expertise in the subject areas being taught (e.g., technology, business, healthcare, etc.). Certifications in relevant tools or technologies (e.g., cybersecurity, IT, programming languages, project management, etc.). Post-secondary teaching or training experience preferred. Evidence of ongoing professional development through education, certifications, or other activities. Proficiency with teaching technologies, including LMS platforms, lecture-capture tools, and synchronous online engagement software. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with demonstrated ability to engage others. Contact Info Heidi Gentry University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The position is anticipated to begin in Fall 2026. This position requires a flexible schedule for trainings and occasional classes that start outside normal business hours. This position may be on location at any of the eight counties of the panhandle region. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63612&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse - FSUS",
      "description": "Job Title Registered Nurse - FSUS Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63612 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University School (FSUS) Responsibilities Develop and deliver engaging lessons aligned with State curriculum standards. Teach nursing assistant and allied health competencies through classroom, laboratory, and clinical instruction. Supervise students during clinical rotations and hands-on learning experiences. Evaluate student performance using assessments, skills checklists, projects, and industry standards. Prepare students for industry certifications such as CNA or related healthcare credentials. Maintain accurate attendance, grades, clinical records, and student competency documentation. Promote professionalism, communication, teamwork, and ethical behavior in the healthcare settings. Ensure compliance with OSHA, HIPAA, infection control, and school safety regulations. Coordinate with healthcare partners for clinical placements and career experiences. Participate in faculty meetings, professional development, advisory committees, and school activities. Maintain current nursing licensure as required. Qualifications Associates degree in nursing or related healthcare field and two years of clinical nursing experience. Current unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) or equivalent license. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with adolescents or teaching/training adults. Knowledge of healthcare industry standards and clinical procedures. Stong training, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to integrate technology into instruction. Experience with simulation labs and clinical instruction. Ability to build partnerships with healthcare facilities and community organizations. Commitment to student success, career readiniess, and workforce development. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63593&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant State Climatologist, 12 Month Salaried (Florida Climate Center)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant State Climatologist, 12 Month Salaried (Florida Climate Center) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63593 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Climate Center | Center for Ocean-Atmospheric Predication Studies (COAPS) | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The selected candidate will be involved in the day-to-day operations of the Florida Climate Center, especially as it pertains to outreach and communication. This position will serve as a key member of the Center for Ocean-Atmospheric Prediction Studies (COAPS) outreach team and help identify, plan, and participate in a variety of events and opportunities. Limited travel to outreach events and workshops may be required. Responsibilities include: Providing climate data and services to citizens, private businesses, and government agencies in the State of Florida. Duties involve responding to inquiries about climate and weather via phone and email. Independently utilizing all resources available to answer questions and formulate data, products, and reports to meet the needs of the customer. Developing and disseminating regular climate products and reports, and maintaining a suite of web-based climate data products in response to needs and gaps. Serving as a liaison between the Florida Climate Center and our partners in climate services at the National Centers for Environmental information, Southeast Regional Climate Center, other state climate offices, and the National Weather Service. Performing research-related tasks as opportunities arise or as driven by public demand and in support of other projects/grants in place at COAPS. This could include independent research projects assigned by the Director of the Florida Climate Center, as well as providing data and technical support for research projects from undergraduate students, graduate students, summer interns, and faculty. Leading outreach/educational presentations and experiments related to climate and weather information in classroom as well as informal settings. Creating, editing, and distributing routine climate reports and newsletters. Managing and providing content to social media accounts for the Florida Climate Center. Qualifications A master's degree from an accredited institution in the field of Meteorology or a related science is required. A bachelor’s degree in Meteorology or related field with a minimum of two years of experience in the field of Meteorology/Climatology/Climate Services or in Science Education/Outreach/Communication may also be considered. This position will be hired at the rank of Assistant in Research. The selected candidate must also possess: A friendly and helpful professional demeanor and be able to work well independently as well as with a variety of groups including other scientists, the general public, and stakeholder groups, such as educators, practitioners, school-aged children, etc. Ability to prepare publication-quality graphics and maps, have basic web and programming skills, strong organizational skills, good oral and written communication, and the ability to write on technical subjects and make them understandable for non-scientists. Experience with data analysis, including basic knowledge of and/or the ability to learn computer programming and statistical analysis software, such as Python, R, HTML, SASS, GIS, or Matlab, as well as some research experience, is preferred. Contact Info For more details, please contact Dr. Emily Powell . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a state funded part-time position (0.50 FTE, 20 hours per week). Subject to the availability of future grant funding, the position may increase up to full-time (1.0 FTE). Applications review will begin November 13, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63525&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Community Health Worker (OPS) Walton County, Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine",
      "description": "Job Title Community Health Worker (OPS) Walton County, Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63525 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University’s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Conduct health needs screenings and care navigation at every mobile unit stop. Will travel throughout Walton County attending mobile clinic events, visiting local clinics, interacting with community paramedicine providers, and ensuring patients are connected to the resources they require. Initiate and track referrals to Community Paramedicine, Remote Patient Telemonitoring, Retail Clinic Services and fixed-site primary care providers. Confirm appointment completion and document barriers to follow-through. Connect patients to local health and human services resources including WIC, transportation assistance, and social support programs. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalency and two years of experience. Valid FL or GA driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Community Health Worker Certification (CHWC) must be achieved within the first year of employment. Preferred Qualifications Ability to adhere to ethical business practices, promote ethical behavior, and represent the University in appointed area as required. Ability to demonstrate effective customer service skills and establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing and gather, interpret, report, and/or edit information. Ability to perform accurately in a detail-oriented environment and prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. Ability to maintain accurate records and retrieve files from active or archive sources. Basic filing practices to include numeric and alphabetic systems. Helpful This role will be the primary accountability bridge across five Rural Health Transformation Program initiatives that form a network to expand access to preventive and primary care services for rural populations. The initiatives are (1) mobile health, (2) on-site pharmacy/retail clinic services, (3) community paramedicine, (4) remote patient telemonitoring and (5) health information exchange. Contact Info Georgia Arnold University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is a full time OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be responsible for traveling throughout Walton County and will support Bundle 1 - Preventative Care & Care At Home Northwest region, which is defined as Bay, Calhoun, Escambia, Franklin, Gadsden, Gulf, Holmes, Jackson, Jefferson, Leon, Liberty, Okaloosa, Santa Rosa, Wakulla, Walton, Washington on the Rural Health Transformation Program Map . This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63641&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Job Title Director (Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63641 Location Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University’s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Provides strategic leadership, direction, and administrative oversight for the Rural Health Transformation (RHT) portfolio of six programs. For the overall RHT program at FSU, oversees the planning, development, implementation, review, and evaluation of program goals, objectives, policies, and procedures to support successful achievement of funding priorities, organizational objectives, and community health outcomes. Directs activities supporting the growth, sustainability, and long-term advancement of Rural Health Transformation initiatives. Identifies opportunities to expand programmatic impact through new partnerships, innovative initiatives, funding opportunities, and collaborative endeavors that support the University's rural health mission. Directs the establishment of operational frameworks, policies, procedures, and performance standards that promote alignment and consistency across Rural Health Transformation initiatives. Ensures program activities are conducted in accordance with University, state, federal, and funding agency requirements. Provides strategic leadership for relationships with key external partners including healthcare organizations, governmental agencies, academic institutions, community stakeholders, and other partners that support Rural Health Transformation objectives. Serves as a representative of the University in collaborative initiatives that advance rural health priorities throughout the state. Works with program evaluator, optimize program performance data impact through communication and dissemination activities publicly. Utilizes performance data and stakeholder input with Rural Health Transformation portfolio to measure program effectiveness, identify opportunities for improvement, and demonstrate organizational impact. Utilizes data and outcomes to guide decision-making, strategic planning, and future program development. Leads development of overall RHT program website, social media and other key dissemination and communication outlets. Serves as a resource to University leadership, program personnel, and stakeholders regarding Rural Health Transformation initiatives and priorities. Participates in and may lead committees, advisory groups, and collaborative efforts that advance program objectives and support the University's health and human services mission. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to administrative services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to ten years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Florida or Georgia Driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Contact Info Georgia Arnold University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires regular travel in support of program activities and responsibilities. Travel may occur within the employee’s assigned region and throughout the State of Florida, as needed. The frequency and location of travel may vary based on programmatic and operational needs. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62719&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Project Financial Assistant - NHMFL",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Project Financial Assistant - NHMFL Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62719 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory - MS&T Department Responsibilities Providing comprehensive financial support for the 40T project, including assisting with the preparation, review, and maintenance of the project cost book, compiling and validating required financial documentation, and supporting all phases of the proposal development process. This role works closely with project leadership and cross-functional teams to ensure cost estimates are accurate, well-documented, and compliant with University and sponsor guidelines. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Undergraduate or Graduate students interested in business analysis Proficiency in Microsoft Excel University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range $18 hourly How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The position requires an average commitment of approximately 10 hours each week. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63634&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Animal Care Assistant (Part-time, OPS)",
      "description": "Job Title Animal Care Assistant (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63634 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Laboratory Animal Resources (LAR ) is looking to fill the role of Animal Care Assistant (Part-time, OPS) Responsibilities This position performs routine duties associated with cage sanitation and preparation for reuse in a research setting, including cage maintenance, preventive maintenance of equipment, monitoring equipment for proper function, and maintaining sanitary conditions. Operates mechanical washers and ensures that cage washing and related equipment are in proper working order. Operates autoclaves to sterilize or decontaminate caging and equipment. Assists in receiving and storing materials, food, and supplies. Transports animals, caging, and supplies between animal rooms and facilities. Maintains the sanitary condition of cage wash facilities and other ancillary areas, including corridors and storage rooms. Takes necessary precautions to adhere to OSHA standards, other applicable federal and state regulations, and LAR standard operating procedures when working with hazardous agents, animals, and power equipment. They will provide diligent and responsible animal care. Feeds and waters animals. Changes and clean cages. Sanitizes equipment and facilities. Records and reports animal abnormalities, including altered eating, drinking, waste elimination, behavior, superficial lesions, and/or death. Assists with technical procedures, including record keeping, animal identification, breeding, sexing, specimen collection, preparing diets, and euthanasia. Records and reports any environmental abnormalities. Provides routine physical maintenance of assigned areas. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications High School diploma and one year of work experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. Ability to perform physical tasks, such as standing, gripping, reaching, bending, and the ability to regularly lift up to 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with animals or in research. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The desired schedule is 20 hours per week, Monday - Friday, between 07:30 am and 5:30 pm, as determined by the candidate and supervisor. Scheduled shifts would be a minimum of 4 hours. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63628&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Reading Education or Special Education",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Reading Education or Special Education Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63628 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and the Florida Center for Reading Research Responsibilities Candidates will be expected to maintain a rigorous grant writing and research program, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in their program, train doctoral students, and participate in university governance commensurate with rank. Qualifications Ph.D. in Reading Education, Special Education, or related field Demonstrated evidence of rigorous research productivity Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching and training Demonstrated commitment to continued grant-funded research and scholarly productivity Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to and evidence of developing doctoral students Demonstrated evidence of (or potential for) an externally funded, independent research program A quality program of research related to reading and/or writing development, assessment, instruction, intervention, or related topic areas (emerging at the assistant rank, established at the associate rank) Teaching experience in preschool through grade 12 settings Other Information The School of Teacher Education (STE) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences (Anne’s College) and the Florida Center for Reading Research (FCRR) at the Florida State University invite applications for a nine-month, tenured or tenure-earning assistant or associate professor of Reading Education or Special Education. The position will involve teaching, research, and service within STE, and will include a joint appointment with FCRR. The position carries a reduced teaching assignment with correspondingly high expectations for research productivity. The successful candidate will have a tenure home in one of two majors within STE: Reading Education or Special Education. These majors work closely together in STE and FCRR, so a collaborative orientation is desired. The candidate will be expected to maintain a rigorous grant writing and research program, including competitive externally funded research grants. The candidate will also teach undergraduate, masters, and/or doctoral level classes within their program, and train doctoral students through active participation in their research program. The candidate will also be expected to participate in university governance in the department, college, and FCRR, at a level that is commensurate with their rank. The candidate will join an interdisciplinary group of colleagues and students at STE, Anne’s College, and FCRR. Drawing from multiple disciplines, FCRR investigates all aspects of reading and reading-related skills across the lifespan. Through rigorous and robust research, innovation, and engagement, FCRR advances the science of reading to improve learning and achievement from birth through adulthood. Meanwhile, Anne’s College advances society and enriches our community through support and education, while enhancing the quality of life of all our students, faculty and staff. Through meaningful collaborations, commitment to public scholarship, and integration of research, practice and policy, Anne’s College addresses America’s urgent education challenges in the innovative manner characteristic of FSU. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Sonia Cabell , Ph.D., Sigmon Endowed Professor and Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a CV, a cover letter detailing how they meet the required and preferred qualifications, a sample publication, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin 10/26/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. The anticipated start date is August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63604&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director, FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business",
      "description": "Job Title Director, FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63604 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate and Legal Studies - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Advisory Board Management The Director leads the development and implementation of the objectives and strategic goals of the FSU Real Estate Center. Acts as the highly visible, senior external-facing leader and chief liaison to real estate industry personnel, employers, and alumni. Leverages an established industry network to expand opportunities for the Center. Manages the Center’s Executive Advisory Board, including directing Board communications and meetings, identifying and cultivating prominent industry leaders for new membership, assisting Board subcommittees, and reporting to the Board at its biannual meetings. Industry Engagement and Professional Events Provides the framework, strategic vision, and guidance for the Center’s professional events and activities, ensuring they serve as premier networking and talent pipeline opportunities. Oversees the annual TRENDS conference, the FSU-Kislak Market Strategy Forums, the Evan Jennings Speaker Series, the Real Deal & Entrepreneurs Series, and any future forums designed to advance the preeminence of the real estate program. Collaborates with faculty and external stakeholders to ensure programming reflects current industry trends, technologies, and market opportunities. Student Success and Career Pathways Responsible for connecting students in the real estate program with internships, mentorships, industry projects, and full-time career pathways through strategic employer partnerships. Coordinates the Center’s support of student activities, including the FSU Real Estate Society. Directs the Center’s program manager and other staff in the awarding of fellowships, travel grants, and administrative assistance for student participation in corporate tours, case competitions, networking opportunities, mentoring, and other experiential learning activities. Center Administration and Operation s Supervises Center staff and oversees the Center’s day-to-day administrative and financial operations. Coordinates Center communications with alumni, Executive Board members, sponsors, employers, students, and faculty. Ensures compliance with applicable University and State of Florida policies and requirements. Program Advocacy and Brand Management Serves as the primary external face of the Real Estate Center to industry leaders and professional organizations to articulate the successes and objectives of the Program, its faculty, and its students. Works with the College’s PR & marketing team to develop branding and messaging that elevates the Center’s national reputation. Assures that the FSUREC brand, mission, products, and services are consistently presented in a strong, positive image to relevant stakeholders. Donor Stewardship and Development Collaboration Acts as a subject-matter expert and strategic partner to the College’s development, engagement, business development, and career services teams to support fundraising, sponsorship, employer, executive education, and alumni/donor engagement efforts. Identifies and develops corporate sponsorship opportunities for Center programs and activities. Accompanies gift officers on strategic visits to provide programmatic vision, assisting in the cultivation and stewardship of employer and donor partners to enhance student, faculty, and Center resources. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to administrative services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and ten years of experience related to administrative services? (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated record of strategic leadership and partnership development, supported by a robust, existing network of commercial real estate professionals, employers, and industry leaders. Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder initiatives, professional events, and program budgets. An advanced degree in business, real estate, finance, planning, or a related field is highly desired. Six or more years of professional experience in commercial real estate development, commercial brokerage, investment, or related financial services. Experience working with students, faculty, and staff in a higher education setting. Professional credentials in real estate, planning, or finance are strongly advantageous. Contact Info J. Bradley Karl , PhD Chair, Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate and Legal Studies Dr. William T. Hold/The Alliance's Program in Risk Management and Insurance University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62364&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Law Enforcement Officer (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Job Title Law Enforcement Officer (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62364 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Panama City Campus Police & Public Safety Responsibilities The Law Enforcement Officer is responsible for the protection of life and property, prevention of crime, misconduct, traffic and crowd control, criminal and traffic law enforcement, criminal and traffic accident investigation, community service and providing information regarding laws, University policy, and distribution of information to the community. Patrols the FSU campus for the primary purposes of seeking out and apprehending violators of Florida statutes, identifying and reporting safety hazards and providing a visible presence throughout campus to deter crime. Responds to fire and burglar alarms, traffic accidents and other incidents that may be reported. Interacts with other law enforcement agencies to assist and cooperate in their efforts and to secure their assistance with preventing and responding to situations on campus. Protects the safety of drivers, bikers and pedestrians through traffic control and direction in the event of collisions, construction work or other mitigating circumstances. Provides non-emergency assistance to members of the University community, such as unlocking buildings and car doors as needed, helping with dormitory move-in and providing directions. Acts as a first responder when necessary, providing CPR and first aid. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Conducts Investigations in the resolution of open investigations by securing crime scenes, assisting with evidence collection, taking witness statements and conducting interviews with victims, witnesses and suspects. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Writes and submits reports with all pertinent details related to cases of lost, stolen or damaged property, incidents in which harm has been threatened or inflected on any person, and other miscellaneous incidents on campus with a bearing on safety and security. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Provides security services for scheduled events occurring both indoors and outdoors on campus, in partnership with other law enforcement agencies and security officers. Prevents crime and apprehends those in violation of the law through scheduled crime suppression details. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Supports Crime Prevention activities by participating in formal crime prevention programs, such as the RAD (Rape Aggression Defense) program, Click-It-Or-Ticket, and Bicycle Safety programs. Prevents crime through informal contact with students, faculty and staff to raise awareness of safety issues on campus and to encourage safe behavior and wise decision-making. These responsibilities apply to the campuses of Florida State University Panama City and the Gulf Coast State College. Other duties as assigned to support the mission of the Department and the University. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Must be at least 19 years of age. Must be a citizen of the United States. Must meet the requirements of Section 943.13, Florida Statutes, and the ability to pass the state certification exam for Law Enforcement Officers within six months of being hired. A valid State of Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Applicants may qualify for employment with the FSU Police Department through the Equivalency of Training (EOT) process if they meet one of the following: Out-of-State or Federal Officers: 1+ year full-time sworn experience Comparable training to Florida’s basic recruit academy No more than 8-year break in service Special Operations Forces Members: 5+ years of service No more than 4-year break in service Previously Certified Florida Officers: Fully certified in Florida 4–8-year break in service Contact Info Malia Brown - (850) 644-1239 - mbrown10@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . All applicants must successfully complete a Physical Standards Test (PST) as part of the selection process. Successful completion of the assessment is mandatory for employment consideration. Law enforcement officers assigned to the Patrol Division will work 12-hour shifts (6:30pm - 6:30am or 6:30am - 6:30pm), 80 hours bi-weekly. Additionally, the position may be required to assist during home football games, holidays, and during state, national or University emergencies. Special assignments as directed by law enforcement chain of command. This position requires completion of a supplemental employment questionnaire and a post-offer employment physical exam, drug screening, psychological evaluation, police background check, and Federal Bureau of Investigations (FBI)/Florida Department of Law Enforcement (FDLE) fingerprinting. This position qualifies for special risk benefits and classification under applicable retirement or insurance programs. Final approval for special risk benefits is subject to Florida Retirement System review and approval. This position is located in Panama City, FL. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63635&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Senior Grants Specialist",
      "description": "Job Title Senior Grants Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63635 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department ICON-Health within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Senior Grants Specialist position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for the comprehensive pre- and post-award administration of sponsored projects, ensuring absolute accuracy and compliance with university (FSU), division, center, and agency policies and regulations. This includes developing, reviewing, and analyzing sponsored project documents for accuracy and compliance. Assist Principal Investigators (PIs) with long-term planning, budget development, analysis, forecasting, amendments, and grant closeout. Serve as the local subject matter expert on federal, institutional, and funding agency policies; interpret guidelines for grantees and advise faculty on allowable expenditures (materials, supplies, services). Prepare, review, and audit budget reports and amendments in a timely manner, monitoring all project activities to ensure fiscal compliance. Act as the primary liaison between faculty, Sponsored Research Administration (SRA), University central offices, the Office of Research, and the College of Medicine throughout the grant lifecycle from submission to closeout. This position reviews and analyzes fiscal transactions and reconciliation reports on a monthly basis, provides monthly budget summary to PIs. Makes corrections as needed. Audits and ensures completion of all post award transactional grant activities including appointments, purchases, travel corrections such as DOLs, eRDFs, etc. Advises PIs on fund utilization in order to maximize budget allocations. This position approves travel and procurement actions to ensure alignment with PIs request, overall fund management strategy, and compliance with Federal, State, University and Agency regulations, laws, policies and guidelines. Trains new staff and recommends policies, procedures, and guidelines related to grants activities. This position organizes and communicates personnel appointments and verifies effort certification is accurately reflected for PIs and personnel employed on assigned projects. Coordinates mass appointment data each semester for sponsored project funded graduate students and faculty. Approves personnel appointments to ensure alignment with fund management. Identifies funding opportunities, conducts research, and interprets advanced technical information for grantees. Additional duties as assigned as it relates to the grant management, business operations and overall success of ICON-Health. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to seven years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification series within the first six months from start date. Preferred Qualifications Experience in pre – and post-award Research Administration Contact Info Averi Allbritton at adeering@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
