    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63502&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Jazz Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Jazz Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63502 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate-level jazz trumpet students, and supervise graduate teaching assistants. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio Serve on doctoral and master’s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include teaching courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Qualifications A doctoral degree in a related field or a master’s degree with equivalent professional experience is required at the time of appointment. The successful candidate will: Hold a record of successful university-level teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Other Information The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist For questions regarding the position, please contact Rodney Jordan , Professor of Jazz Bass and Coordinator of Jazz and Music Industry University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Application Materials: Cover Letter, CV, List of Links, etc. Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 1st, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63500&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music Therapy, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Music Therapy, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63500 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teaches undergraduate and graduate-level courses in Music Therapy or related areas. Courses will be selected from current area offerings and/or implemented in the candidate's area of expertise. Supervises clinical music therapy experiences. Directs doctoral and master's-level committees. Conducts research and scholarly activities related to their interests and areas of expertise. Engage in recruitment of outstanding students. Develop and maintain community partnerships. Participates in university and professional service activities appropriate to rank. Qualifications Academic doctorate or highest-level terminal degree from an accredited institution in Music Therapy or related area. Credentialing through the Certification Board for Music Therapists (MT-BC) is required. Minimum of five years of full time (or equivalent) clinical experience as an MT-BC is also required. A record of successful university-level teaching experience. Demonstrated excellence in clinical musicianship as a practicing professional. Experience as a clinical supervisor. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with substantial clinical and supervision experience, and who hold the NICU-MT and/or other specializations. A record of ongoing research/scholarly activity is also preferred. Other Information The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist Other inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair as follows: Dr. Lori Gooding , Associate Professor of Music Therapy and Co-Coordinator of Music Education & Music Therapy University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Each item below should be uploaded as a PDF to the Additional Documents section of the online application: One to two-page cover letter Curriculum vitae A copy of scholarly writing that clearly reflects your research focus and direction such as a refereed published article, an in-press article, or a doctoral-level scholarly paper Link to a 20-minute video of the applicant teaching Confidential letters of recommendation from at least three references will also need to be submitted on your behalf. Letters may be solicited through our system or directed to CM-HiringDocs@fsu.edu Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link 2) Click the My References link 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by October 20th, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63625&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Senior Academic Program Specialist (School of Information)",
      "description": "Job Title Senior Academic Program Specialist (School of Information) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63625 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The School of Information College of Communication & Information Responsibilities The individual in this position has lead responsibility for coordinating admissions, advising, outreach, recruitment, retention, and graduation for students in the Master of Science in Information Technology (MSIT) program and certificates within the School of Information. The position supports academic program operations, student success initiatives, enrollment management, and program growth while serving as a representative and ambassador for the School. Academic Program Leadership and Student Success Serves as primary Student Services Advisor for students in the MSIT program and certificates from initial point of inquiry to graduation and fosters a welcoming and supportive environment. Monitors student success, retention, registration, and graduation clearances and ensures compliance with University systems. Collaborates with academic leadership to support student success initiatives, academic interventions, and scholarship administration. Provides cross-functional support during peak operational periods and performs other duties as assigned. Strategic Recruitment, Outreach, and Program Promotion Coordinates communications and marketing initiatives that support recruitment, retention, and student engagement goals. Develops and maintains partnerships with university departments, alumni, employers, professional organizations, and community stakeholders to support program growth and student opportunities. Oversees relevant websites, publications, social media, and recruitment materials to ensure accuracy and alignment with School of Information objectives. Coordination and Operational Oversight Provides coordination and oversight for academic program activities and student service operations. Assists with training, process documentation, workflow improvements, and implementation of best practices to ensure effective delivery of services and achievement of departmental goals. Provides guidance and coordination of activities within the Student Services team and recommends enhancements to operational processes and procedures. Program Planning, Assessment, and Reporting Conducts research and analyzes admissions, enrollment, retention, graduation, and employment outcome data to evaluate program effectiveness and identify opportunities for improvement. Compiles and interprets statistical reports and provides recommendations to leadership regarding enrollment management, student success, and improvements to MSIT program and certificate performance. Supports strategic planning and continuous improvement initiatives. Policy Interpretation and Departmental Resource Interprets and applies University, Graduate School, and departmental policies and procedures related to admissions, enrollment, advising, academic progression, graduation requirements, and student records. Ensures compliance with institutional requirements and recommends improvements to policies, procedures, and operational processes that enhance efficiency and service delivery. Serves as a resource to faculty, staff, administrators, and students on academic policies, procedures, and program requirements. Service and Leadership Contributions Represents the School of Information on departmental, college, university, and professional committees, workgroups, and special projects. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience in academic advising, student services, admissions, enrollment management, higher education administration, or a related field; or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to six years. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Information Technology, Computer Science, Instructional Design, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience in academic advising, student services, graduate program administration, or a related higher education setting. Experience with graduate admissions, recruitment, enrollment management, and student retention initiatives. Knowledge of university policies, procedures, student information systems, and related administrative processes. Experience collecting, analyzing, interpreting, and reporting student or program data. Experience developing communications, outreach materials, recruitment materials, or other student-facing content. Knowledge of information technology, computing, or related academic disciplines. Demonstrated experience leading projects, coordinating initiatives, and implementing process improvements. Experience providing customer service, advising, program coordination, or student support. Ability to interpret, apply, and communicate policies, procedures, and guidelines. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work effectively in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with computer applications, student information systems, databases, and data management tools. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and diverse populations. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63084&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Admissions Operations (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Director, Admissions Operations (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63084 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Admissions About Us | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Oversees the implementation of strategies to support campus enrollment goals, admissions priorities, and strategic marketing initiatives. Collaborates with staff to ensure consistent, timely, and relevant communications with prospective students, applicants, and admitted students through outreach campaigns, engagement initiatives, and Slate-based communication strategies. Serves as a point of contact for applicants, parents, university officials, and community stakeholders. Develops expertise in residency and judicial processes related to admissions and promotes an environment of exceptional customer service throughout the admissions experience. Works closely with FSU Panama City staff and Tallahassee admissions partners to ensure compliance with university admissions procedures, branding standards, enrollment objectives, and strategic admissions goals. Assists campus leadership in the management of daily operational functions within the Admissions Office. Develops and implements processes that improve operational efficiency, enhance prospective student experiences, and support departmental objectives. Oversees appropriate Slate system access and collaborates with Tallahassee partners to maintain effective admissions operations. Supports policy development, workflow improvements, and strategic initiatives that advance enrollment goals. Assists with the administration of admissions systems, communication strategies, and office operations while maintaining productive relationships with university partners and stakeholders. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years’ experience related to academic and/or student services or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to eight years in the same. Preferred Qualifications Master’s Degree. Prior experience working in higher education admissions, enrollment management, student services, or related areas. Expertise in Slate or other admissions CRM platforms. Experience supervising professional staff and managing operational workflows. Knowledge of residency determination, admissions policies, and higher education regulations. Experience developing strategic communication or recruitment campaigns. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Experience developing and implementing policies, procedures, and operational processes. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, families, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and multitasking skills. Proficiency with computer applications and student information systems. Proficiency in Microsoft 365 Applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams, etc.). Contact Info Inquiries should be directed to Dr. Tyler Towne for more information regarding this position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $51,500, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position will begin in Fall 2026. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
