      "title": "Export Control Officer",
      "description": "Job Title Export Control Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63587 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Research, Integrity, Security & Ethics within the Division of Research seeks to fill the role of Export Control Officer. Responsibilities This role will develop, implement, and maintain the university's export control compliance program. Interpret and apply federal regulations including ITAR, EAR, OFAC, and related research security requirements. Develop policies, procedures, guidance documents, and internal controls to ensure institutional compliance and minimize regulatory risk. Monitor regulatory and agency changes and recommend program modifications as necessary. Review research proposals, contracts, grants, agreements, disclosures, international collaborations, shipments, and activities for export control implications. Evaluate foreign national participation, controlled technologies, technical data, and restricted research requirements. Provide recommendations and compliance determinations to faculty, staff, and leadership. Will develop, implement, and monitor Technology Control Plans (TCPs) and related security measures for export-controlled research and controlled unclassified information. Conduct risk assessments, compliance reviews, and monitoring activities to ensure adherence to institutional and regulatory requirements. Oversee restricted party screening and international compliance review processes. Evaluate international visitors, collaborators, vendors, sponsors, and research partners for sanctions or export control concerns. Document determinations and maintain required records. Develop and deliver training, educational programs, and compliance resources related to export controls, research security, international collaborations, foreign influence, and related regulatory requirements. Promote awareness and compliance across the research community. Prepare license applications and regulatory submissions when required. Serve as the university liaison with federal regulatory agencies. Investigate potential compliance concerns, recommend corrective actions, maintain required records, and prepare reports for institutional leadership. Qualifications Bachelor's degree with six years of professional experience. Four years of experience will need to be in research compliance, export controls, regulatory compliance, research administration, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Our Ideal candidate would have experience within a higher education setting, developing and implementing compliance programs and plans, and hold current certifications of ITAR, EAR, and OFAC. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62416&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Ascension Bay Internal Medicine) College of Medicine",
      "description": "Job Title Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Ascension Bay Internal Medicine) College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62416 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, COM Residency Program Administration Responsibilities The Program Director oversees the Internal Medicine Residency Program (“IM Program” or “Program”) under the guidance of the Designated Institutional Official (DIO). The Program Director handles the general management, curriculum development, hiring, and teaching and mentoring of the Program. The Program Director sets the strategic vision of the Program and ensures its standards, quality, and reputation. The Program Director is expected to support the collaboration of the IM Program with physician practices and hospital clinical services in a way that improves value and quality, and that fosters a positive environment for professional practice and medical education. The Program Director will also work in collaboration with the program leadership to ensure outstanding educational offerings within Ascension Sacred Heart Bay Hospital. Clinical Teaching and Supervision of Residents Core Program Clinical Teaching Clinical Practice in Internal Medicine or applicable Subspecialty General Administration Graduate Medical Education (GME) Committees/Meetings GME Lecturing/Teaching Conferences GME Recruiting/Interviewing GME Research/Scholarly Activity Resident Evaluation/Monitoring Program Evaluation Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Valid FL medical license, or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL licensure. Must be board certified in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM). Must have a minimum of three years of faculty and administrative experience in an ACGME accredited internal medicine residency program. Preferred Qualifications Effective professional management skills, including the ability to plan, organize and schedule work in an efficient and productive manner, focusing on key priorities and meeting deadlines. Outstanding interpersonal, leadership, mentoring and teaching skills. A strong work ethic and desire to participate in a team-oriented, performance-driven health system. Ability to communicate with others in a clear, understandable, and professional manner in person, on the phone, electronically, and in writing. Ability to build and lead high-performing teams; must be able to provide clear and accurate direction and guidance. Strong administrative and team building skills. Other Information Ascension Sacred Heart Bay – Panama City, FL As part of Ascension, the largest non-profit health system in the U.S. and the world’s largest Catholic health system: Sacred Heart was founded by the Daughters of Charity in 1915. While our technology has improved dramatically, and the buildings have grown and expanded, our commitment to the mission remains steadfast: to provide excellent health care to all people, with special attention to the poor and vulnerable. Sacred Heart Health System includes hospital campuses in Pensacola, Miramar Beach, Panama City, and Port St. Joe, Florida, as well as The Studer Family Children’s Hospital at Sacred Heart, Northwest Florida’s only children’s hospital and Sacred Heart Medical Group, the largest network of primary care and specialty physicians in Northwest Florida. The 47-million-dollar renovation of Bay Medical after Hurricane Michael is in process and aims to create a facility with 200 private rooms. The improvements include major upgrades to information technology and creation of new space for physician offices and other services, including the laboratory, imaging and pharmacy. Bay offers an accredited Stroke Center, a Level II Trauma Center, which provides 24-hour emergency care for life-threatening injuries and illnesses, and emergency services located at the main hospital as well as a freestanding emergency center on Panama City Beach. Helpful The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape the program in their vision and recruit core faculty. Candidates with recent scholarly activity such as peer reviewed funding, publication of original research or review articles in peer-reviewed journals, chapters in textbooks, publication or presentation of case reports or clinical series at scientific society meetings, or participation in national committees or educational organizations are highly encouraged to apply. Contact Info Jessee Graham: jjgraham@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Faculty Information This faculty position is jointly affiliated with Florida State University (FSU) and Ascension Sacred Heart. Appointment is contingent upon the successful completion of all onboarding and employment requirements of both institutions. These requirements include, but are not limited to: a comprehensive credentialing process through Ascension Sacred Heart Medical Staff Office, background screening, professional reference checks, drug screening, and submission of a self-query report from the National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB). Please note that Ascension Sacred Heart credentialing process may take up to 90 days from the date the offer is accepted. Final appointment and the ability to initiate clinical responsibilities are contingent upon the approval of medical staff membership and clinical privileges by Ascension Sacred Heart. Further details regarding onboarding and credentialing processes will be provided during the interview and offer stages. Additional list of Ascension Sacred Heart Program Director Requirements . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a clinical/non-tenure earning role, and rank is commensurate with experience. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63602&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Job Title Admissions Counselor Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63602 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Admissions Responsibilities The Office of Admissions is a unit within the Division of Enrollment Management, which is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions , Office of the University Registrar , Office of Financial Aid , and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management’s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the student's development and progression in their academic experience – from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families and to campus partners across the University. Responsible for the evaluation of first-year application types and the implementation of University policies and procedures as they relate to first-year Admissions. Assists in the planning and coordinating of recruitment activities and represents Florida State University to prospective students, parents, and counselors. Assists in the coordination and management of the application review process for first-year students to the University. Responsible for the implementation of University policies and procedures as they relate to first-year Admissions. Shares in the management of the acknowledgment of incomplete first-year applications. Represents the University for first-year admissions. Frequent contact with prospective students, applicants and their parents, the general public, officials and personnel associated with colleges/community colleges/universities, and high school counselors. Provides interpretation of policies and procedures to aforementioned entities. Some contact with principals and teachers. Participates in special events hosted by the Office of Admissions. Extensive travel throughout Florida and out of state. Due to travel needs, position requires operation of a motor vehicle. Counsels prospective students and represents the University at sponsored events pertaining to Admissions and provides information about the University and its programs. Assists in the review and evaluation of policies and procedures, making suggestions and recommendations to senior leadership. Counsels current and prospective students regarding admission scholarship opportunities, eligibility and renewals requirements. Refers specialized scholarship questions to Program Manager and/or senior leadership. Assists other sections during peak times in support of the goals of the Division of Enrollment Management. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and one year of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and five years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to five years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications A Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of complimentary experience preferred. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are detail-oriented, and who work well independently as well as in a team. Experience working with populations, reviewing transcripts, and interpreting and applying admissions tests is preferred. Candidates should have the ability to review, analyze, formulate, and organize data and information and follow through on assignments. Experience should be relevant and related to the responsibilities of the job. Qualified candidates will possess the ability to prioritize and organize multiple work assignments simultaneously. Experience counseling and/or providing expertise and advice is required. Qualified candidates will have experience using Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook or comparable software. Applicants should be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships and be able to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ideal candidates will have a strong sense of initiative, the demonstrated ability to manage multiple responsibilities concurrently, and the ability to make sound judgments while working in a deadline-driven environment. Candidates must attach a resume to be considered for the position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $44,056.80, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires extensive travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63607&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Chemical Oceanography/Aquatic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Chemical Oceanography/Aquatic Chemistry) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63607 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science l College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Chemical Oceanography / Aquatic Chemistry. We seek candidates whose research centers on aquatic chemical processes and biogeochemical cycling. Research areas of interest include, but are not limited to, the inorganic carbon system, ocean gas exchange, isotope geochemistry, nutrient cycling, chemical tracers of ocean circulation, aquatic / marine pollution, and modeling of chemical and biogeochemical processes in aquatic / marine systems. The appointee is expected to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in Oceanography and Environmental Science, as well as to supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in research and creative activities. The faculty member would support core instruction in chemical oceanography while developing advanced courses in specialized areas such as biogeochemical cycles, aquatic geochemistry, isotope geochemistry, and aquatic / marine pollution. The successful candidate would develop a vigorous externally funded research program focused on aquatic / marine chemical processes and biogeochemical cycling. Qualifications Candidates must hold a Doctoral degree or the highest degree appropriate in Oceanography / Environmental Science or a related discipline. Other Information EOAS is housed in a recent building (2020) with state-of-the-art facilities and laboratories, has approximately 35 tenure-track faculty and 100 graduate students, and offers undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. In addition to collaborations with other faculty within EOAS, the appointee can expect collaborations with colleagues at the Center for Ocean-Atmosphere Prediction Studies and the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. For additional information on EOAS and FSU’s resources, please check our website . Contact Info For any inquiries, please, reach out to search committee chair Dr. Robert Spencer . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Required application materials include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statements on research and teaching interests Contact information for three references to provide letters of recommendation Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63619&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker, Evening - FSUS",
      "description": "Job Title Custodial Worker, Evening - FSUS Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63619 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools (FSUS) Responsibilities Performs custodial duties ensuring assigned areas meet cleanliness standards. Clean assigned classrooms/offices to include vacuuming, mopping, wiping down furniture/desks, cleaning windows, doors, door jams, and door handles. Empties wastebaskets, removing garbage, bags, and contaminated waste and materials. Make simple repairs and report major repair problems. Lock and secure assigned area when finished. Sweeps doorways, clean mats, enterances and inner hallways. Cleans exterior corridors and removes any garbage or discarded items to the proper receptacles. Cleans elevators, wiping down walls and sweeping and mopping floor. Cleans and sanitizes bathrooms. Replaces and restocks bathroom supplies. Executes set-up and cleaning needs for all campus events including extra-curricular activities. Cleans carpets and rugs using appropriate cleaning equipment. Strips, waxes, and buffs non-carpeted floors using appropriate equipment. Supports special custodial projects as assigned, including seasonal exterior needs. Supports quality control protocols for cleaning standards. Assists Custodial Supervisor and Asst. Director for Facilities as necessary with team and individual training or mentoring as appropriate. Assists all FSUS personnel with moving furniture and supplies throughout campus. Delivers goods to campus personnel as needed. Supports safety and security protocols of K-12 campus environment. Qualifications Completion of the 9th grade. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-clas university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63326&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Monographic Cataloging Librarian, 12 Months Salaried",
      "description": "Job Title Monographic Cataloging Librarian, 12 Months Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63326 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Libraries Responsibilities Leads monographic cataloging operations, including the creation, editing, analysis, and quality control of metadata for monographic and foreign language resources. Develops, implements, and improves cataloging and metadata workflows and coordinates the identification and remediation of metadata quality issues. Applies established cataloging and authority control standards and works with local and statewide colleagues on cataloging practices and system-wide changes. Supervises two full-time cataloging staff and provides training, guidance, and documentation related to monographic and foreign language cataloging. Contributes to the work of FSU Libraries and the profession through collaborative projects, committees, research, professional organizations, conferences, and continuing education. Qualifications MLS/MLIS degree from a program accredited by the American Library Association (or international equivalent), or a master's degree in a specialized area directly relevant to the position. At least one year of cataloging experience using MARC 21 and experience applying established cataloging standards and guidelines such as RDA, NACO, LCC, and PCC. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to take initiative, learn new technologies and technical skills quickly, and adapt to changing priorities. Ability to plan and coordinate projects and workflows, provide clear guidance and documentation, and work both independently and collaboratively. Strong communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with colleagues in a collaborative environment. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are welcomed but are not required. Candidates are encouraged to apply even if they do not have experience in every area listed below. Experience with or interest in cataloging resources in non-Roman alphabets, particularly Chinese, Japanese, and/or Korean, or a background in linguistics or language studies. Familiarity with library systems and tools used for cataloging and authority control, such as Ex Libris Alma, OCLC Connexion, NACO, ORCID, or ISNI. Experience in supervision, project management, and/or providing instruction and training in an academic or research library environment. Helpful FSU Libraries seeks an innovative and resourceful librarian to lead and help shape its monographic cataloging program. This is an exciting opportunity for an early- to mid-career librarian who is eager to build their expertise while solving complex problems, improving workflows, and exploring how emerging technologies can support the future of resource description and discovery. This position will lead cataloging operations for monographic resources in all languages, including materials in non-Roman scripts, and will work with colleagues to re-envision monographic and foreign language cataloging procedures at FSU. A particularly exciting area of exploration will be the use of AI-assisted approaches to support the translation and transliteration of materials in non-Roman alphabets, particularly Chinese, Japanese, and Korean, while maintaining the accuracy and quality essential to library metadata. This faculty librarian will supervise two full-time catalogers and will combine hands-on cataloging expertise with workflow development, staff training, quality control, and collaborative problem solving. The position offers opportunities to build specialized expertise, contribute to professional service and research, and grow as part of a team of enthusiastic learners. Contact Info Alex Chisum , Head of Cataloging and Metadata University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $60,000 - $75,00, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63605&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs – Associate/Full Professor or Teaching Faculty II/III Rank - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Associate Dean for Academic Affairs – Associate/Full Professor or Teaching Faculty II/III Rank - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63605 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs serves in a leadership position, overseeing the operations of the Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) in the College. Leadership & Oversight Supervising, assigning areas of responsibility, and evaluating all faculty and staff within the Academic Affairs unit (approximately 17 faculty and staff). Overseeing the unit’s financial planning and budgeting activities. Student Affairs Serving as the Academic Dean for all student-related processes, which includes, but is not limited to: Advising students, faculty, and chairs regarding Grade Appeals and General Grievance processes. Advising the College Student Leadership Committee (SLC). Academic Affairs Serving as the Academic Dean and the College liaison for University-level entities, including the Office of Accreditation and Quality Assurance, the Office of Institutional Performance and Assessment, the Office of Faculty Development and Advancement, Undergraduate Studies and the Graduate School. Serving on multiple committees as the College representative for academic affairs. Maintaining the College Degree Program Inventory (DPI) and Certificate Program Inventory (CPI) with FSU IR. Assisting academic programs with new degree, major, and certificate proposals. Working closely with chairs, faculty, academic staff, and students regarding the College and FSU graduate and undergraduate policies and procedures. Overseeing the College curriculum committee and associated curriculum proposal process. Approving all Graduate Faculty Status, Graduate Teaching Status, and Co-Directive applications. Recruitment, Admissions, & Enrollment Management Data Overseeing all College academic affairs data processes, including analysis and reporting. Coordinating annual student Program Satisfaction Surveys. Assisting with design and maintenance of the College Data SharePoint site. Accreditation & State Program Approval (Office of Quality Assurance) Serving as FSU’s Florida Department of Education Liaison for all educator preparation programs (Anne’s College, Panama City, Fine Arts, and Music). Maintaining curriculum, policies, and procedures for all FLDOE approved educator preparation programs. Working with nationally accredited programs through assisting in the design and full implementation of student learning outcome assessment systems. Working Environment Promoting methods for communicating policies and procedures to faculty and academic staff; Supports department academic staff in all areas of academic affairs. Maintaining a congenial and collaborative relationship with all departments and academic support units within the College. Teaching Department responsibilities are limited to teaching and advising doctoral students. Teaching responsibilities equivalent to one course per academic year in the fall or spring semester for tenure-track candidates or two courses per academic year for specialized faculty candidates. Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in a discipline related to one of the academic units in the College. Demonstrated success in research and/or teaching, depending on the type of faculty line (tenured/tenure-earning or specialized teaching) sought. Prior experience in academic leadership at the program, center, institute, department, or college level. Ability to analyze data and make data-informed decisions. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with state-approved and/or nationally accredited academic programs. Prior experience developing new academic degree programs. Other Information The Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for an Associate Dean for Academic Affairs position to start in July or August of 2027. For external candidates, the faculty rank (tenure-track associate/full professor or specialized teaching faculty II/III) associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. The Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) is the representative office for the academic dean of the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. OASIS strives to provide students, staff, and faculty, with the tools and support needed for student success. OASIS serves as the central repository for all student records, monitors required academic milestones, provides academic advising and support for undergraduate students, collaborates with academic departments to provide academic support for graduate students, and serves as the primary liaison between current students and the Office of the Registrar, the Division of Undergraduate Studies, and The Graduate School. OASIS directly manages the undergraduate admission process and provides support to academic departments in the admission of graduate students. Additionally, OASIS works with educator preparation programs throughout the university to coordinate internship placements and field-based experiences with PK-12 schools and students. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Toby Park-Gaghan , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of academic affairs leadership philosophy. Transcripts, work samples (such as journal articles or teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. A 9-month versus 12-month appointment will be dependent on the selected candidate's rank and program. Review of candidates will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63592&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried - School of Dance Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63592 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Dance Responsibilities The Florida State University School of Dance invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Open Rank Faculty in Dance with expertise in Dance Science, Dancer Health and Wellness, and evidence-informed approaches to dancer training. We seek a collaborative scholar, educator, and mentor whose work bridges scientific inquiry, embodied practice, and creative exploration in ways that advance the preparation and well-being of dancers. Situated within our nationally recognized Dancer Training Program, this position offers a distinctive opportunity for an individual whose expertise may span areas such as applied science, performance research, pedagogy, somatic practices, rehabilitation, conditioning, creative scholarship, or interdisciplinary inquiry, while maintaining a clear commitment to optimizing dancer development through research-informed practice. The successful candidate will join a dynamic community of faculty, staff, and students dedicated to innovation, excellence, and the evolving future of dancer training. Teaching The successful candidate will contribute to the School's nationally recognized Dancer Training Program through teaching that reflects expertise in dance science, dancer health and wellness, and evidence-informed approaches to training. Teaching courses such as Dance Conditioning, Dance Kinesiology, Science of Dance Training, Dance Coaching, Research in the Dance Sciences, and related topics. Contributing specialized instruction in areas aligned with the candidate's expertise, such as Pilates, Gyrotonic, Yoga, Strength and Conditioning, Somatic Practices, Motor Learning, Injury Risk Management, Rehabilitation-Informed Training, Dance Technique, and other movement-based practices. Developing innovative courses and learning experiences that integrate scientific inquiry, embodied practice, creative exploration, and emerging approaches to dancer development. Research and Creative Scholarship The successful candidate will maintain an active research and/or creative scholarship agenda that advances the preparation, performance, health, and well-being of dancers. Conducting research related to dancer health, wellness, performance optimization, conditioning, pedagogy, injury risk management, motor learning, and related areas in the dance sciences. Disseminating scholarship through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other professional activities and venues with national and international reach. Engaging in applied, practice-based, and creative forms of inquiry that connect research with studio, classroom, laboratory, rehearsal, or performance settings. Contributing to the continued evolution of the dance sciences through interdisciplinary, collaborative, and innovative approaches to research and artistic practice. Service The successful candidate will contribute to the shared governance and mission of the School of Dance through service to the program, university, and profession. Serving on the Dance Conditioning and Wellness Committee and supporting initiatives within the School's Movement Training Laboratory. Contributing expertise to programs and initiatives that promote dancer health, wellness, and performance excellence. Participating in School, College, and University governance through committee work and other service assignments determined through faculty governance processes and in consultation with the Chair. Engaging in professional service activities that support the broader fields of dance science, dancer training, and higher education. Mentoring and Student Development The successful candidate will mentor undergraduate and graduate students as artists, scholars, researchers, and movement practitioners. Advising students pursuing interests in the dance sciences, dancer health and wellness, movement training, performance coaching, or related fields. Mentoring student research, creative scholarship, and practice-based inquiry. Guiding students in the application of evidence-informed approaches to performance preparation, training, recovery, and injury-risk reduction. Supporting students' professional development and preparation for careers in academic, artistic, clinical, research, or interdisciplinary settings. Contributing to an environment of student success through mentoring that extends across teaching, scholarship, service, and community engagement. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization from an accredited institution in one of the dance sciences or a related field with an emphasis on working with dancers. Evidence of scholarly, creative, or applied research activity related to dancer development, health and wellness, performance optimization, pedagogy, movement training, or closely related areas. Demonstrated ability to contribute to a collaborative academic environment and to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students in advancing initiatives related to dancer training, health, and wellness. Demonstrated commitment to evidence-informed practice and the integration of research, embodied knowledge, and teaching. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching courses related to the dance sciences, dancer health and wellness, movement training, conditioning, kinesiology, performance preparation, pedagogy, coaching, or related fields. Experience teaching, coaching, training, or facilitating movement-based practices such as Pilates, Gyrotonic, Yoga, Strength and Conditioning, Somatics, Motor Learning, Injury Risk Management, Rehabilitation-Informed Training, Dance Technique, or other approaches that support dancer development and well-being. Active research, creative scholarship, or applied professional practice that advances understanding of healthy and effective dancer training. Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students in research, creative inquiry, professional practice, or career pathways related to dance science, dancer health and wellness, and movement training. Demonstrated ability to bridge scientific inquiry, embodied practice, and artistic exploration in teaching, scholarship, or professional work. Familiarity with quantitative, qualitative, mixed-methods, and/or practice-based research approaches relevant to dancer training and performance, including experience with small-N and within-subject research designs. Other Information The College of Fine Arts at Florida State University is dedicated to fostering artistic excellence, creative exploration, and scholarly inquiry across a variety of disciplines. Our renowned faculty and staff educate and empower students to become visionary performers, artists, educators, art historians, designers, curators, art therapists, researchers, and arts administrators who shape the future of the visual arts, healing arts, performing arts, and design. Through passionate teaching, community engagement, innovative research, and artistic practice we enrich lives, elevate artistic expression, and inspire positive change and well-being in society. Montgomery Hall is one of the best developed dancer training facilities in the nation. The Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC) is an internationally recognized dance choreographic research center and part of the School of Dance. This unique and visionary institute brings a steady stream of prominent and emerging dance artists to campus to create and develop the work that the rest of the world will experience in years to come. Add to this mix an esteemed faculty and talented, highly motivated students, and it is easy to see why we are excited for what is to come. Contact Info Search Committee Chair: Professor Gwen Welliver University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants are required to submit: Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three references. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applicants will begin on December 1, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63081&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Ultrafast XUV Spectroscopy in High Magnetic Fields (OPS)",
      "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate in Ultrafast XUV Spectroscopy in High Magnetic Fields (OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63081 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory , headquartered at Florida State University, a top-tier research-intensive university, seeks highly qualified applicants to join our program in optical spectroscopy of condensed matter, with an emphasis on ultrafast optical techniques. The NHMFL is the world’s largest and highest-powered magnet laboratory. It is home to several world-record-breaking magnets, including the 45 T Hybrid and the 25 T Split-Florida Helix. Research spans physics, chemistry, materials science, biochemistry, instrumentation, and related fields. The NHMFL hosts one of the world's largest communities of scientists working in high magnetic fields and provides a highly collaborative environment with extensive technical and scientific support. The post-doctoral associate being sought will work with a team to develop and use instrumentation to produce, deliver, and measure extreme ultraviolet (XUV) light to samples placed in the 25 T Split-Florida Helix magnet. Responsibilities The successful candidate will contribute to the development of a novel experimental platform combining ultrafast extreme ultraviolet spectroscopy with high magnetic fields to investigate emergent phenomena in quantum materials and other condensed matter systems. The candidate will work closely with DC Magnetic Field staff, external project co-PIs, MagLab users, graduate students, and postdoctoral fellows; contribute to collaborative and independent research projects; publish manuscripts; and participate in the development of external grant proposals. Postdoctoral applicants must have completed a Ph.D. in a STEM field and demonstrate strong scholarly potential in the ultrafast spectroscopy of condensed matter, chemistry, biochemistry, or related subject matter. Qualifications PhD in Physics, Chemistry, or a related area Applicants should have demonstrated expertise in ultrafast optical spectroscopy including (but not limited to) sample preparation, data acquisition, experiment design and construction. Experience with high-harmonic generation, XUV spectroscopy, or related ultrafast nonlinear optical techniques is highly desirable. Familiarity with cryogenic and vacuum technologies for low-temperature measurements. The ability to bring innovative methods, technology development, or collaborative opportunities will be considered a significant strength. Other Information Please include: Curriculum vitae Cover letter describing research experience and future interests Contact information for at least three references (letters submitted through the application system) Contact Info For inquiries about this position, please contact Dr. Stephen McGill . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check. The position is full-time and includes health benefits. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63596&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Professor & Director, 9 Month Salaried - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Professor & Director, 9 Month Salaried - School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63596 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Provide leadership and strategic direction for all academic programs in the School Lead and enhance the School’s strategic efforts for research productivity and excellence Lead the effort for identifying the major priorities of the School, including the combined BS/MS pathways in teacher education, and other graduate programs (e.g., PhD and master’s) Align the School’s strategic planning goals with the strategic plans of the University and the College Manage budgetary, personnel, and other departmental resources Foster and maintain a supportive environment for all faculty, staff, and students in the School Provide leadership and direction for creating an environment of transparency and open communication within the School Enhance the rigor and quality of research in the School, as well as the opportunities for PhD students Collaborate with the Director of the Florida Center for Reading Research and the Learning Systems Institute to continue developing productive research partnerships that promote the work of faculty in the department Lead efforts to build relationships within and outside the University that lead to the betterment of the College, and the well-being of the community and the region Qualifications Earned doctorate from one of the educational disciplines found within the School, or a closely-related field. A record of scholarly accomplishments consistent with the rank of full professor with tenure; exceptionally qualified candidates may also be considered for the Mack and Effie Campbell Distinguished Professorship. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in academic leadership, including budgetary oversight and management Broad research knowledge and experience at Research 1 universities—to understand, guide, and communicate with faculty working in different fields within various paradigms and methodologies Experience as a leader for faculty members’ professional development and growth. Experience with building and maintaining relationships with K-12 and community agency field partners and field-placement management Demonstrated commitment to faculty development and advancement Other Information The Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a Professor and Director of the School of Teacher Education. The College encourages applications from visionary leaders committed to education and its role in maximizing human potential. Reporting to the Dean of the College, the Director is responsible for the overall success of the School, its students, and its faculty and staff. The School of Teacher Education is committed to high quality personnel preparation programs; service to the state of Florida; and high-quality scholarly research in elementary education, early childhood education, reading/language arts, second language education, special education, blindness and low vision, science education, math education, social science education, English education, and related areas. The School strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with world-class training in teaching, research, and professional development. Through the guidance and mentorship of faculty, students graduate to serve as educational leaders who will contribute to the betterment of a pluralistic, global society in the context of the state of Florida's needs for an educated, global-minded citizenry. In addition to mentoring and preparing the next generation of educators, faculty engage in a wide range of research activities. Faculty work routinely appears in prestigious publications and is cited by peers. Furthermore, faculty receive support from a robust Office of Research to pursue research opportunities, professional awards, and more. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. Alysia Roehrig , Search Committee Chair Questions regarding the application submission system and process should be directed to the application coordinator: Jania Kadar , Sr. Administrative Specialist University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted prior to notifying applicants), and a cover letter of no more than four pages that articulates the candidate’s experience and vision for the School as related to: (1) leadership, innovation, and strategic partnerships; (2) research; and (3) teaching. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of candidates will begin October 31, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position has a proposed start date of July 1, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62745&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, Level II-IV (Magnet Science & Technology - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)",
      "description": "Job Title Research Engineer, Level II-IV (Magnet Science & Technology - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62745 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Responsible for mechanical design applying standard engineering practices, procedures, and criteria in designing complex high field magnet assemblies at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory. Engineering Design & Analysis Responsible for selecting standard engineering techniques, procedures, and criteria in designing complex magnets. Evaluate requirements and constraints of magnets, designed to meet scientific or research needs, and create mechanical designs to accommodate them according to their applied loads. Perform structural analyses to designed hardware and fasteners. Read and understand technical drawings including geometric dimensioning and tolerancing. System Design & Development Directs conceptual design, detailed system design, and preparation of engineering drawings/documents of magnet systems using 3D CAD and may also include software such as Autodesk Inventor, Solid Works, Pro-Engineer, etc. Design from engineering prototype to final system using technology development, fabrication process development, preparation of engineering documentation, and supply chain management. Testing, Fabrication & Quality Develop tooling and assist in building mechanical assemblies while applying quality controls and adhering to safe practices. Responsible for preparing, testing, and evaluating plans and specifications of magnets designed to meet scientific or research needs. Ensures the product quality meets the researchers needs. Develops unique methods and processes for technical tasks such as system assembly, performance testing and analysis of results. Project Coordination & Collaboration Interacts and coordinates with external users, researchers, and scientists in the development and implementation of projects. Assists group leaders in directing individual project/programs. In absence of group leaders may need to provide leadership decision making concerning acquisitions, staff and technical project details. Attend team meetings to discuss project testing needs and report test results. Conduct background research to help develop and define engineering requirements. Interact with other professional staff for test method development, and the design and construction of magnet systems. Laboratory Operations Perform general laboratory duties such as creating purchase requests, maintaining tools and equipment, and organizing and maintaining inventory. Research, Publications & Outreach Publish and/or present the results designs, testing, or other works in journals or conferences when appropriate. Participate in outreach activities and interact with numerous technical visitors from domestic and international laboratories and industries. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma and seven years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Additional experience qualifies candidates for higher-level consideration (III–VI). Each level requires three additional years of experience. Helpful What you Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info Please contact Kayla West if you have questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Level II – Mid $60,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level III – Mid $70,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level IV – Mid $80,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63538&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Research, 9 Month Salaried - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Associate Dean for Research, 9 Month Salaried - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63538 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The Associate Dean for Research serves in a leadership position, overseeing the operations of the Office of Research in the College. Operations Supervising, assigning areas of responsibility, and evaluating faculty, clinical and administrative staff within the Office of Research unit (approximately 15 faculty and staff), as appropriate Overseeing the Office of Research (OoR) operations, including but not limited to: Identifying and implementing effective grant development activities and proposal tracking systems for efficient operation within the OoR Supervising the administration of all grants related activities effectively and with a commitment to the highest quality of customer service for faculty and staff Creating and implementing innovative programs expanding research activities Tracking and supporting grant activity, using a variety of analytical tools (e.g., Academic Analytics) to analyze proposal submissions, grant awards, journal article publications, journal article citations, and honorific awards Maintaining fiscal responsibility for the OoR budget, external fund sources affiliated with the OoR, and OoR SRAD funds Collaborating with, PIs, OoR senior editor(s), and methodologist in the conceptualization and design phases of grant proposals and other research projects Managing administrative facility requests, including, but not limited to Office of Research space allocation requests/usage and activities associated with research amplification Supporting Faculty Meeting with prospective faculty members to communicate college expectations related to all aspects of Anne’s College research enterprise, including expectations for faculty grant submission, programs aligned to successful proposal development and awards, and direct Office of Research (OoR) support in grant development, including faculty research agenda development, administration, and amplification Assisting faculty in applying for and obtaining external funding including, but not limited to, differentiating various support mechanisms managed by the OoR Evaluating faculty candidate readiness to engage in grant activities and high-impact research (e.g., proposal preparation skills, likelihood of obtaining funding to support research interests, working on grant projects, publishing in high-impact journals) Communicating with College leadership faculty candidate readiness to undertake a robust and impactful research agenda Collaborating with new faculty, in conjunction with appropriate OoR personnel, to discern research interest, develop research agenda, identify funding opportunities, and develop supportive plans to apply and obtain funding across various institution specific opportunities (e.g., FYAP program) Developing and implementing all programs and activities related to internal research catalyst funding Liaising with the Office of Research Development and Sponsored Research Administration to elevate and expand Anne’s College research footprint in campus-wide interdisciplinary research programs, including facilitating the management of internal grant applications, mock review panels, and faculty research profiles intra-institutionally Coordinating all research amplification activities, including targeted social media posts, facilitating the College’s Open Access Publishing program, and enhancing programs related to indexed journal article publishing Leadership Serving as a visible member of the Dean’s Cabinet Ensuring alignment of OoR activities with College strategic plans and policies Providing the Dean and the College leadership team with data analysis to support and inform research-related strategic planning and resource allocation decisions Chairing Strategic Planning Committee’s Academic Quality Subcommittee Administering the annual Dean’s Circle Catalyst Grant Program Leading the Academy of Scholars program and helping to coordinate all related activities throughout the year Ensuring the successful planning and implementation of College research events Coordinating all research partnerships with the Florida Department of Education Advising the College’s department chairs on the potential impact grant activities might have on faculty workload and SRAD distribution Working with the OoR Program Director and at the discretion of the Dean to provide administrative support and oversight to Florida State University Schools, FSU Pembroke Pines, and the Collegiate School at Panama City External Relations Attending, and serving as spokesperson at, College grant-related research meetings Establishing strategic professional relationships with key individuals within various funding agencies (e.g., IES, NSF, NIH, Spencer Foundation, W.T. Grant Foundation) Developing and maintaining effective collaborative relationships with all relevant individuals and groups (e.g., FSU VP for Research, other Associate Deans for Research, Director of the Office of Research Development, FSU Office of Research, LSI, FCRR) Serving as a member of the Council of Associate Deans for Research (CADR) Serving as the College’s representative member of the LEARN Coalition Representing the Dean or College/University interests at regional, national, or international conferences, convenings, or events at the discretion of the Dean Teaching Department responsibilities are limited to teaching and advising doctoral students Teaching responsibilities equivalent to one course per academic year in the fall or spring semester. Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in a discipline related to one of the academic units in the College. Demonstrated success in research that would warrant tenure in a discipline within the College Prior experience in academic leadership at the program, center, institute, department, or college level. Ability to analyze data and make data-informed decisions. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in navigating and establishing strategic professional relationships with key individuals within an institutional structure as well as governmental or private extramural funding agencies. Prior experience in developing and maintaining effective and collaborative college and campus relationships with individuals and groups relevant to the portfolio of responsibilities for the position. Prior experience developing programs to support faculty research and elevate institutional profile. Prior experience in supervision of organizational structures comparable to the Anne’s College Office of Research. Other Information The Office of the Dean in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for an Associate Dean for Research position to start in July or August of 2027. For external candidates, the faculty rank associated with the tenure-track appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. The mission of the Office of Research (OoR) is to provide excellent service to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences faculty in the development, administration, and amplification of research efforts. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Bob Eklund , Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research leadership philosophy. Transcripts, work samples (such as journal articles or teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. This is a 9-month faculty position with a guaranteed summer appointment for the administrative role. Review of candidates will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62366&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Talent Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Job Title Talent Engagement Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62366 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Human Resources - Talent Acquisition Responsibilities About This Role Florida State University - recognized as a Forbes Best-In-State Employer - is a place where meaningful work and organizational impact intersect every day. The Talent Engagement Specialist strengthens FSU’s ability to compete for top talent by enhancing outreach, guiding hiring leaders with consultative support, and improving how candidates experience FSU at every stage of the recruitment journey. This role meets immediate workforce needs while steadily building the pipelines that keep the university positioned for long-term success. This position is dedicated to advancing strategic recruitment partnerships and initiatives across the university, with a specialized focus on our Facilities teams. Through talent intelligence, sourcing expertise, and relationship-driven outreach, the Talent Engagement Specialist helps ensure FSU is positioned to meet highly technical, operational, and mission-critical staffing needs across a large and evolving campus environment. Why This Role Matters Talent Acquisition at FSU supports an evolving proactive, insight-driven model that aligns recruitment with the university’s long-range strategic priorities. This role is central to that progression, strengthening our ability to anticipate workforce needs, activate talent pipelines early, and support hiring leaders with guided strategies that keep FSU competitive in a dynamic talent landscape. In this role, you’ll help FSU attract and engage talent for critical operational, technical, and leadership positions, with a primary focus on Facilities. Your work will directly support the teams who maintain and enhance the physical environments where students learn, researchers innovate, and campus life thrives. What You’ll Do Strategic Sourcing & Talent Research Develop targeted sourcing strategies to identify passive talent for specialized, technical, and leadership roles, with a primary focus on Facilities staffing needs. Conduct talent mapping, market research, and advanced searches to build high-quality candidate pools. Leverage digital platforms, AI-enabled tools, and sourcing technology to expand reach and accelerate candidate engagement. Candidate Engagement & Pipeline Development Build and maintain talent pipelines for key workforce areas, including operations, skilled trades, technical specialists, and Facilities leadership. Create targeted outreach campaigns and refine messaging based on candidate engagement and response data. Represent FSU’s employment brand through professional, responsive, and engaging candidate interactions. Recruitment Partnership & Strategy Partner with Facilities leadership, HR Representatives, and hiring managers to understand current and future workforce needs. Provide market insights, talent availability data, and sourcing recommendations to support recruitment decisions. Align sourcing efforts with FSU’s Talent Acquisition strategy and broader university priorities. Technology, Analytics & Continuous Improvement Use CRM, ATS, LinkedIn, Indeed, and other digital recruitment platforms to execute and manage sourcing campaigns. Organize and segment prospective candidates for current and future opportunities. Track outreach, engagement, and conversion metrics and provide regular updates to Talent Acquisition leadership and Facilities partners. Continuously improve sourcing strategies based on recruitment data, workforce trends, and stakeholder feedback. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Communications, Marketing, or a related field and two years of experience in strategic sourcing, senior level recruiting, or talent acquisition; or a high school diploma or equivalent and the same experience equal to six years. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to source, engage, and cultivate relationships with passive candidates across niche, technical, and leadership talent markets. Familiarity with ATS and CRM platforms. Proficiency with CRM platforms such as Avature, Beamery, or Yello. Certifications such as AIRS, LinkedIn Certified Recruiter, or SHRM-CP. Advanced sourcing methodologies Talent mapping and market research CRM/ATS proficiency Helpful Working at Florida State University At FSU, you’ll be part of a vibrant academic and professional community where ideas matter, collaboration fuels progress, and meaningful work shapes the future. The Talent Acquisition team plays a critical role in supporting the people who make FSU exceptional — ensuring the university can attract and retain the talent needed to advance our mission. Love What YOU DO at FSU! Your future begins here. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $50,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63573&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "UGS Academic Advisor Pool - Fall 2026 (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Job Title UGS Academic Advisor Pool - Fall 2026 (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63573 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Advising First – Division of Undergraduate Studies Responsibilities Responsible for advising undergraduate students in the development of academic schedules appropriate for stated education goals. Takes a proactive approach to academic advising, seeking out contact with students and staff, and providing advising services on request. Works with academic departments and other units within Undergraduate Studies to develop advising programs. Engages, helps plan, and participates in special projects for Advising First/UGST. Recommends changes and additions in existing policies and procedures that positively implement a successful advising program. Performs special projects as assigned by Undergraduate Studies. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of University rules and regulations. Prior customer service experience and /or experience working with students in an educational setting. Ability to extract complex academic information from various sources and maintain confidentiality. Experience and/or working knowledge of student advising, counseling, or working one-on-one with people in a professional or academic setting. Creative problem-solving skills. Master’s degree is preferred. Computer skills to include experience with Microsoft Office and web-based applications. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously with minimal to moderate supervision. Ability to deal with people in a calm, confident manner and with complete objectivity. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $44,184, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
