    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63492&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Musicology, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Musicology, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63492 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Maintain an active program of research and creative/scholarly activity leading toward tenure; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Early Music, Musicology, and additional areas of expertise; mentor graduate students in the Musicology Area; contribute to the intellectual and artistic life of the College of Music; and participate in appropriate service. The successful candidate will also contribute to FSU's Early Music Program through historically informed performance, which may include coaching, directing, performing with, or otherwise supporting Early Music ensembles and related activities. Qualifications Completed doctorate or highest degree appropriate in Musicology, Historical Musicology, Ethnomusicology, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Evidence of a developing record of excellence in research and teaching appropriate to a tenure-earning appointment. Scholarly expertise in Early Music (broadly defined) and demonstrated knowledge of historically informed performance practice. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates whose scholarship and teaching engage substantially with performance and performance practice and who can contribute actively to FSU's Early Music Program. Demonstrated experience performing, coaching, directing, or otherwise working with historically informed vocal and/or instrumental performance is especially desirable. Additional areas of scholarly expertise are open. Other Information The Musicology Area seeks a scholar specializing in Early Music whose work integrates historical research with historically informed performance. The successful candidate will contribute to FSU's longstanding strengths in Early Music and its integration of musicological study, performance practice, and ensemble participation. The College of Music at Florida State University: is the largest such college in the Southeast and the third largest university-based music program in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info Eden Wahlquist , Sr. Administrative Specialist (for technical assistance applying to this position) Dr. Frank Gunderson , Professor of Musicology (for inquiries for the search committee chair) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Supplemental Application Materials: Please submit as individual PDFs a current CV and a cover letter. Three confidential letters of recommendation are required prior to the time of hire. Please be prepared to facilitate this process upon request. Additionally, we may request a writing sample and recording samples at a later date. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by October 15th, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 9th, 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63501&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Trumpet, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63501 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate- and graduate-level trumpet, coordinate with large ensemble conductors and other cohorts, and supervise graduate teaching assistants. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio. Serve on doctoral and master’s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include teaching courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Qualifications The successful candidate will: Have completed a doctoral degree at the time of appointment or demonstrate a record of equivalent performance and teaching experience. Hold a record of successful university-level teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer of solo, chamber music, and orchestral music. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Demonstrate a proven commitment to creating an environment which contributes to the vibrancy, and economy of the university community and engages students and citizens from different backgrounds and walks of life. Other Information Seeking new knowledge and deeper understanding of music in interdisciplinary contexts through innovative research, music performance, and creative activity, The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and one of the largest university-based music programs in the nation. With over 90 faculty and 40 support staff, the College offers a range of degrees in music, baccalaureate through the doctorate. We are home to approximately 700 undergraduate and 400 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 20 foreign countries. Contact Info For inquiries related to specifications of this position, please contact Professor Jeff Keesecker , Search Committee Chair For technical assistance applying to this position, please contact Eden Wahlquist , Sr. Administrative Specialist For all other inquiries, please contact Erica Francis , Dean’s Executive Assistant University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. It is necessary to fully complete the online application for consideration. Please also upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, links to representative recordings of solo playing (live recordings preferred), links to video recordings of teaching, and three letters of reference. PDF format is preferred. If the representative recordings PDFs include YouTube links, please ensure that privacy settings are set to “public” or “unlisted,” but not “private.” Video recordings of teaching must be no more than 20 minutes in length total and should include one undergraduate applied student and one graduate applied student. Playing recordings should be no more than 30 minutes in length total, and live recordings are preferred. Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled; however, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by November 1st, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Appointment will begin August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63555&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Sport Management - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant/Associate Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried - Department of Sport Management - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63555 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Sport Management - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The individual hired will be required to maintain an active research agenda, possess strong knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methods for the effective mentoring of master’s and doctoral student research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses (including teaching online courses), seek external funding, aid in developing external partnerships, and contribute to department and university growth through appropriate service activities. Qualifications Minimum qualifications for the position include earned doctorate degree in Sport Management or related field; college/university teaching experience; mentoring experience; evidence of scholarly productivity; experience procuring external funding, or evidence of ability to procure external funding. An individual’s program of research should align with one of the department’s core content areas. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to individuals with a research interest aligned with business-related content (e.g., marketing, finance, economics, management). Preference will also be given to individuals with a record of procuring external funding. Other Information Candidates are being sought for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor position in the Department Sport Management in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. The department has thematic pillar areas which provide the broad context from which our research and course offerings are derived: Legal and Policy Issues in Sport, Management of Sport, Sport Economics/Finance, Sport Marketing, and Sport Media and Culture Studies. Contact Info Dr. Timothy Kellison , Search Committee Chair Katherine Maddox , Sr. Administrative Specialist (for questions regarding the application submission system and process) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include: Current curriculum vitae Letter of interest highlighting their qualifications for the position Names and contact information of three references Statement of research Statement of teaching philosophy. Transcripts and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. This position will begin Fall 2027. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
