    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63562&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Education and Social Sciences Librarian,12 Months Salaried",
      "description": "Job Title Education and Social Sciences Librarian,12 Months Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63562 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Libraries Responsibilities Serve as a library liaison to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and assigned social science departments, building relationships with faculty, students, and staff. Design and deliver engaging library instruction, workshops, research guides, and other learning opportunities in both online and in-person environments. Help students and faculty navigate the research process through consultations and referrals to relevant library resources, services, and expertise. Support the development and assessment of library collections and resources for assigned subject areas. Collaborate with colleagues across FSU Libraries and engage with emerging approaches and technologies, including AI, that support teaching, learning, and research. Qualifications Master’s degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program (or international equivalent) or expected completion of the degree prior to beginning employment. Teaching or instructional experience and an interest in supporting student learning. Strong communication and interpersonal skills and an interest in building collaborative relationships with students, faculty, and colleagues. Interest in education, health, human or social sciences and enthusiasm for developing subject expertise in these areas. Demonstrated interest in emerging technologies, including AI, and their applications to teaching, learning, research, or libraries. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with education, health and human sciences, and/or social science research resources, including databases and systematic or evidence synthesis review methods. Exposure to or interest in collection development in an academic or research library setting. Familiarity with instructional technologies and tools used to support teaching and learning in online and in-person environments. Helpful FSU Libraries is seeking an early-career librarian who is excited to grow as an educator, research partner, and member of a collaborative academic library. As the library liaison to the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences and other social science departments, you will work directly with students and faculty to support teaching, learning, and research. You will provide library instruction, help students develop research and information literacy skills, connect faculty and students with resources and services, and help build collections that support their academic and research needs. You will also have opportunities to explore how emerging technologies, including AI, are changing teaching, research, and librarianship. We are looking for someone who is curious about these developments and excited to learn, experiment, and contribute as FSU Libraries continues to expand its work in this area. This position is designed to provide opportunities to learn and grow. You do not need to arrive knowing every aspect of academic librarianship. We are looking for someone with a strong foundation, an eagerness and ability to learn, an interest in teaching and research support, and enthusiasm for developing their skills alongside experienced colleagues. Contact Info Kelly Grove , STEM Program Director | GIS and Earth Sciences Librarian University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary is $60,000. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63554&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Parent and Family Philanthropy & Engagement",
      "description": "Job Title Director of Parent and Family Philanthropy & Engagement Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63554 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Director of Parent & Family Philanthropy & Engagement is a strategic advancement leader responsible for designing and executing a comprehensive parent and family giving program. This role integrates annual giving, leadership annual giving, and major gift development to build a sustainable donor pipeline. The Director demonstrates expertise across philanthropy, alumni and constituent engagement, leadership, and data-informed decision-making. The Director oversees all parent and family giving efforts while managing a portfolio of prospects and donors, and supervises one staff member. Philanthropy Develop, execute and analyze a comprehensive parent and family philanthropy and engagement strategy. Manage a portfolio of 25–50 parent and family prospects; qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward donors; collaborate with major gift colleagues on strategies that align with their unit priorities. Create compelling, donor-centered solicitations aligned with institutional priorities. Oversee an omni-channel solicitation calendar that is produced in collaboration with other internal stakeholders to ensure messaging is donor-centric, impact-driven, and aligned with institutional brand and priorities. Constituent Engagement & Donor Relations Oversee stewardship and engagement strategies that deepen parent and family connection and philanthropic participation. Build a multi-year donor pipeline that transitions parents from first-time donors to leadership and major gift levels. Oversee volunteer structures and events (e.g., Parent & Family Advancement Council and philanthropic/engagement events). Partner with campus stakeholders to integrate philanthropy into the full parent lifecycle. Partner with volunteer engagement and alumni engagement teams to maximize regional outreach. Travel frequently and work outside of normal business hours for donor engagement. Leadership & Talent Management Supervise and mentor one staff member, setting clear performance goals and supporting professional growth. Foster a collaborative and high-performing team aligned with advancement best practices. Provide strategic leadership for parent philanthropy initiatives across the division; foster collaborative relations across campus to amplify the role of family philanthropy in advancing the university’s academic mission. Data, Research & Analytics Cultivate relationships with campus partners, including the Division of Student Affairs, Office of Graduation, Admissions, Colleges/Schools/Unit, and others. Leverage CRM systems and analytics to manage donor pipelines, track engagement, and measure fundraising performance. Analyze participation, retention, and giving trends to inform strategy and optimize results. Utilize data to segment audiences and tailor solicitation strategies. Ethics, Policy & Professional Practice (5%) Adhere to ethical standards and best practices as outlined by CASE and advancement industry guidelines. Maintain confidentiality and ensure responsible use of donor data. Promote an environment of integrity, accountability, and transparency in all fundraising activities. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and six years of experience related to the job duties or in an advancement field; or a high school diploma/equivalent and ten years of experience related to the job duties or in an advancement field. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain upon hire date University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
