    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63519&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Grants Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Title Grants Coordinator Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63519 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University. Responsibilities This role coordinates institutional grants for The Ringling, including overseeing end-to-end grant processing, grant data preparation, Research Administration Management Portal (RAMP) routing, proposal submissions, fiscal coordination with Accounting, reporting, solicitation tracking, and communications to support for grant-funded projects. Manages a portfolio of local, state and national grant opportunities; researches and tracks solicitations and deadlines; maintains the annual grants calendar. Prepares and submits letters of inquiry and intent, grant applications, sponsorship proposals, and acknowledgment letters. Maintains all grant reporting files, including government and foundation grants. Oversees end-to-end grant processing, including gathering required institutional and project data, coordinating approvals, and routing submissions through the Research Administration Management Portal (RAMP) or other required systems. Ensures timely proposal submissions, approval process, and reporting. Works closely with Ringling Accounting, FSU Sponsored Research Administration, and other appropriate offices to monitor back-end/fiscal grant responsibilities. Collects data and metrics for reporting and analysis per grant application and reporting requirements; assists with monitoring expenditures and activities. Completes grant reporting and closeout activities. Meets with representatives from foundations and corporations to cultivate interest in supporting museum initiatives through grant funding and establishes ongoing relationships with constituents that provide grant support to the museum. Coordinates with Marketing and Communications to support features, acknowledgments, and public-facing content related to grant-funded projects; may provide copy editing for grant-related communications and other marketing communications as needed. Collaborates with the Development Team to coordinate corporate and foundation grant applications, reduce request redundancy, and ensure relevant records are in the FSU Foundation CRM donor database. Performs other duties, as assigned, that support departmental and organizational projects and goals. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and one year of experience or a combination of post-high-school education and experience equal to five years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including professional business writing Robust interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate with internal and external partners Demonstrated problem-solving skills and ability to work independently with minimal supervision Certified Grant Writer (CGW) or Grant Professional Certification (GPC) Advanced: Project management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines Attention to detail and accuracy in documentation and data management Skill in Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel, Word, and Outlook Experience with: Coordinating grant applications, awards, and reporting requirements Preparing, reviewing, or monitoring budgets and financial reports Grant management software, databases, or CRM systems Experience coordinating meetings, maintaining records, and tracking deliverables Previous experience in grant administration, sponsored research, development, fundraising, or nonprofit operations Knowledge of: Grant compliance, regulations, and funding agency guidelines Nonprofit, higher education, government, or museum funding environments Ability to: Research and identify funding opportunities Analyze data and prepare reports for stakeholders and funding agencies Maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2773. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Commensurate with the education, skills, and experience of the selected applicant. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Your application is not considered complete without attaching the following items: Cover Letter Resume Contact information (phone/email) for three or more references Considerations This is an A&P position. This role: Is based in Sarasota, FL. Is required to adhere to the business dress standards. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check. Working Hours Monday – Friday from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM with a one-hour meal period. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63017&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Media & Communications (Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment, Anne's College)",
      "description": "Job Title Program Manager, Media & Communications (Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment, Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63017 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Lead the development and execution of the college's communications and marketing strategy across print, digital, web, social media, photography, video, and other multimedia platforms. Oversee the creation and distribution of marketing, recruitment, and communications materials, including news stories, newsletters, promotional content, and digital media. Manage and enhance the college website by ensuring timely, engaging, and accurate content while monitoring website performance and search engine optimization (SEO). Develop and implement communications strategies to support college events, student recruitment initiatives, and strategic priorities in collaboration with internal stakeholders. Manage communications and recruitment projects by coordinating timelines, facilitating stakeholder collaboration, and ensuring successful project completion. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with university partners to promote college programs, events, and initiatives. Supervise communications staff, interns, and student employees while fostering a collaborative and creative work environment. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience related to media, communications, and/or marketing services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and eight years of related experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Preferred Qualifications Strong writing, editing, and verbal communication skills. Experience in communication, recruitment, and event management. Strong working knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign) and photo/video editing tools. Experience supervising staff and/or student employees. Experience managing social media accounts for an organization. Experience with web content management systems and SEO best practices. Contact Info Melissa Powell Director, Office of Strategic Outreach & Recruitment University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary for this position is in the $50,000s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
