      "title": "Service Desk Fall Pool",
      "description": "Job Title Service Desk Fall Pool Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63557 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Information Technology Services (ITS) The ITS Service Desk is the first point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and constituents of the University when associated with requesting and receiving support for technologies provided by ITS. Responsibilities This position helps ensure that ITS support and service requests are properly managed by ITS service providers and their staff. Answer inbound calls, resolve basic IT issues using Case Management Guidelines. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications Customer Service experience and Time Management Skills. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? Self-starter, ability to follow instructions; ability to work in a structured work environment. Exceptional customer service and time management skills. What is a typical day in this position? Answer inbound calls via a call center environment, manage Cases to resolution and be a team player. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63545&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Cognitive Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Cognitive Neuroscience) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63545 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities Responsibilities include teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, conducting and publishing research in cognitive neuroscience, and providing service to the department through work on committees. Qualifications PhD in Psychology, Neuroscience, Cognitive Science or related disciplines. Candidates must have a strong research program with a high likelihood of obtaining extramural funding and the potential for excellent teaching and mentorship. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in network-based functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI). Examination of the brain and cognition across the lifespan. Other Information The Psychology Department faculty is very active in research, with Ph.D. programs in cognition and cognitive neuroscience, neuroscience, social, clinical, and developmental psychology. FSU has a state-of-the-art research-dedicated MRI center featuring a 3T Siemens Prisma scanner, an MR-compatible high-density EEG system, MR- compatible TMS and tES systems, and peripheral equipment. Florida State ranks in the top 25 of National Public Universities (U. S. News & World Report). Contact Info Inquiries about the position may be directed to Derek Nee , search chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on September 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63544&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Clinical Psychology)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Clinical Psychology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63544 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Psychology at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology with a start date in August 2027. Area of specialization and research is open. Responsibilities will include conducting and publishing research in Clinical Psychology, teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and providing service to the department through work on committees. Qualifications A doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology or closely related field is required. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong research program, high likelihood of obtaining extramural funding, potential for excellence in teaching undergraduate and graduate students, and the ability to train graduate students in our APA-accredited Clinical Psychology program. Candidates with lines of research in any area of Clinical Psychology are encouraged to apply. Other Information FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1 (Very High Research Activity) institution and ranks in the top 25 of National Public Universities (U.S. News & World Report). The Department of Psychology faculty pursue active programs of research, producing high-impact findings and mentoring students in Ph.D. programs in clinical, social, and developmental psychology, as well as cognition/cognitive neuroscience and neuroscience. The department has an outstanding research infrastructure, with each faculty member having a dedicated laboratory suite, and a fully-staffed electronics and machine shop. FSU has a state-of-the-art research-dedicated MRI center featuring a 3T Siemens Prisma scanner, an MR-compatible high-density EEG system, MR-compatible TMS and tES systems, as well as peripheral equipment. Faculty have access to core equipment and resources (e.g., a confocal microscope and common-use histology/molecular laboratory in the building and numerous other shared resources across the department and campus). The department has a highly favorable teaching load and a collegial atmosphere. FSU is located in beautiful Tallahassee, the capital of Florida where it offers an exceptional quality of life with the amenities of a vibrant college town and the friendliness and accessibility of a close-knit community. The city combines affordable housing and highly regarded schools with short commute times and minimal traffic. Tallahassee also has a vibrant scene, with live music throughout the city and nationally recognized performers and productions brought to the community through Florida State University’s Opening Nights and the Adderley Amphitheater at Cascades Park. Residents also have access to an abundance of regional springs, lakes, and rivers, an extensive trail system, and pristine beaches in the Gulf. Contact Info Inquiries about this position may be directed to Rick Macatee , Search Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please submit the following: (1) cover letter (2-page maximum), (2) curriculum vitae, (3) research statement (3-page maximum), (4) teaching statement (3-page maximum), (5) up to four peer-reviewed papers, and (6) names and contact information for 3 letters of recommendation. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63540&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Neuroscience) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63540 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Psychology | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Psychology at Florida State University seeks to hire a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Behavioral/Systems/Computational Neuroscience, with a start date in August 2027. Responsibilities will include conducting and publishing research in Neuroscience, teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and providing service to the department through work on committees. Qualifications Ph.D. or the highest degree appropriate from an accredited institution in Neuroscience or a related field. In addition, candidates must have a strong research program with a high likelihood of obtaining extramural funding and the potential for excellent teaching and mentoring. Candidates with lines of laboratory research in any area of Neuroscience are encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to applicants whose research programs synergize with existing departmental strengths in chemosensation, learning and memory, social behavior, neuroendocrinology, and the neurobiology of motivated behavior. Helpful For more information about our department visit the Psychology website, and for the Neuroscience program visit the Neuroscience website. Contact Info Inquiries about the position may be directed to Adam Dewan , Search Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. The following are required with the application: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement (maximum 2 pages) Teaching statement (maximum 1 page) List (with online access links) highlighting up to four peer-reviewed papers Names and contact information for three references who can provide letters of recommendation Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63484&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Statistics)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Statistics) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63484 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Statistics | College of Arts and Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Statistics at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting in August 2027. The position provides an opportunity for engagement with our large undergraduate program and vibrant M.S. and Ph.D. programs in Biostatistics, Data Science, and Statistics. The successful candidate will join a faculty with research expertise including machine learning, high dimensional data, network analysis, survival and longitudinal analysis, Bayesian analysis, shape/object data analysis, causality and data privacy, to name a few ( our website ), in a collaborative environment at a comprehensive, Carnegie R1 University. Responsibilities include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, conducting research, and student mentoring. Qualifications A Doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Biostatistics, Data Science, Statistics, or a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching and academic research is required. Candidates with research areas in Biostatistics, Data Science, Statistics or related fields are encouraged to apply. Contact Info For questions about our hiring process, please contact Pamela McGhee . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. This position requires that you submit statements on research and on teaching and have at least three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The deadline for applications is November 13, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=60308&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Laboratory Assistant (Medicine Biomedical Sciences) Medicine",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Laboratory Assistant (Medicine Biomedical Sciences) Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 60308 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Medicine Biomedical Sciences Responsibilities Responsible for performing scientific experiments under the direction of the principal investigator related to immunology, infectious diseases, biochemistry, and structural biology. Instructs lab members in procedures and operation of laboratory equipment and lab safety. Responsible for performing independent laboratory research, to include designing and performing biochemical and immunological assays at the bench, taking detailed notes of experimental procedures, analyzing experimental data, writing research reports and manuscripts, and helping the PI prepare research proposals for grant applications. Analyzes existing methodologies, formulates hypotheses and develops new protocols. Responsible for maintaining accurate and complete laboratory notebooks and research reports, managing the PI’s grant accounts, ordering supplies and reagents, generating monthly expense reports on personnel and lab purchases, and assisting in the general management of the lab including routine cleaning and maintenance of all lab equipment, training new personnel, and supervising lab members assigned by the PI. Manages the day to day lab environment, including individual lab member duties. Qualifications A bachelor’s degree or higher (Ph.D., M.D., ScD., D.V.M., etc.) in an appropriate field is required. Preferred Qualifications Excellent scientific writing ability and strong oral communication skills. The ability to work effectively and collegially with colleagues. Two years of experience working in a laboratory environment. Prior experience working with rodent animal models. Contact Info Dr. Jarrod Mousa University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time role, listed as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62817&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Testing Center Support, Office of Accessibility Services - Fall 2026",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Testing Center Support, Office of Accessibility Services - Fall 2026 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62817 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Accessibility Services | Department of Student Support & Transitions Responsibilities The responsibilities include directing visitors, answering and managing incoming calls, handling inquiries, and providing administrative support to various departments. The position will be primarily testing and transportation support. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent. Preferred Qualifications This role requires a professional and courteous demeanor, excellent communications skills, and the ability to manage multiple tasks efficiently. Preference for graduate students. Contact Info Amber Wagner Director of the Office of Accessibility Services / Assistant Dean of Students 850-644-9566 DOS_OAS_Admin@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position's schedule is M-F, 8 AM - 5 PM. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62316&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, Level II-VI - (Machine Shop - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)",
      "description": "Job Title Research Engineer, Level II-VI - (Machine Shop - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62316 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities This position supervises the daily operations of the MagLab’s prototype machine shop that works in close collaboration with designers, engineers, and technical staff to develop advanced, one of a kind mechanical components and assemblies. The role leads the integration of machining, prototyping, and design iteration to enable innovative research tools and push the boundaries of what is possible in support of laboratory scientists and users. Machining & Prototype Fabrication Leadership Lead machining and prototype fabrication activities to ensure quality, precision, and safety. Manage fabrication requests and ensure compliance with engineering and documentation standards. Support CNC programming, troubleshooting, testing, and custom prototype development. Collaborate with researchers and stakeholders to deliver fabrication solutions. Operations, Equipment & Resource Management Oversee shop operations, scheduling, resource allocation, and long-term planning. Manage equipment, tooling, inventory, maintenance, and procurement activities. Maintain budgets, job priorities, and operational records. Ensure fabrication technologies and practices align with industry standards. Team Leadership & Workforce Development Supervise, coach, and evaluate machinists to promote safety and performance. Manage work assignments, productivity, quality, and compliance. Provide technical guidance for complex projects and initiatives. Foster collaboration and support organizational values. Engineering Collaboration & Project Coordination Serve as the liaison between machinists, engineers, researchers, and project teams. Coordinate project schedules, communication, and execution. Review designs for machinability, safety, quality, and compliance. Strengthen integration between design, engineering, and fabrication functions. Training, Safety & Continuous Improvement Lead training programs on machining, equipment operation, and safe work practices. Develop and maintain technical and safety training for laboratory personnel. Support and advance laboratory safety initiatives and programs. Promote continuous learning, innovation, and process improvement. Research Support & External Engagement Support scientific research through advanced fabrication and engineering solutions. Collaborate with external users, visiting scientists, and research partners. Contribute to outreach efforts that advance the laboratory's mission and impact. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Additional experience qualifies candidates for higher-level consideration (III–VI). Each level requires three additional years of experience. Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Level II – Mid $60,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level III – Mid $70,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level IV – Mid $80,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level V – High $90,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. Level VI – Low $110,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63535&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Paleobiology/Geobiology)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Paleobiology/Geobiology) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63535 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean & Atmospheric Science l College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Earth, Ocean & Atmospheric Science (EOAS) at Florida State University (FSU) seeks a full-time tenure-track faculty member in the field of Paleobiology/Geobiology at the Assistant Professor level. Successful candidates will investigate the coevolution of life and environment with implications for planetary habitability of Earth and exoplanets, biosignatures for life (radiations and extinctions), and modern implications. Some of the research areas of interest include but are not limited to: paleobiology, geobiology, extinction dynamics, paleoecology, paleontology, biotic responses to global change, and biogeochemistry. The appointee is expected to develop and maintain a vigorous externally funded research program and contribute to the undergraduate and graduate programs by teaching Earth History and Paleontology and providing experiential learning experiences. Qualifications Candidates must hold a Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in Earth Science or a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Other Information EOAS is housed in a recent building (2020) with state-of-the-art facilities and laboratories, has approximately 35 faculty members and 110 graduate students, and offers undergraduate and/or graduate degrees in Geology, Meteorology, Oceanography, and Environmental Sciences. Please visit the EOAS website for additional information. Contact Info Inquiries may be addressed to the Search Committee or the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Seth Young . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching interests, and contact information for at least three references. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63474&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering Florida A&M University–Florida State University College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering Florida A&M University–Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63474 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Chemical & Biomedical Engineering (CBE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)–Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for a tenure track faculty position in biomedical engineering, in the city of Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities Successful candidates are expected to develop research programs that are internationally recognized with significant and sustained funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus, and demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in education. Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses and supervising undergraduate, graduate, and post-doctoral researchers are expected. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in biomedical engineering, chemical engineering, or a related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research. Although all applications will be reviewed, priority will be given to candidates that complement and build upon our research in polymeric biomaterials, regenerative medicine, and 3D bioprinting with a goal of aligning with the new FSU Health Initiative. Areas of particular interest include stem cell engineering, nanoparticle engineering, gene editing, immunomodulation, biomaterials, and biomedical imaging. Helpful The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the college of engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R1 public research university. The College fosters interdisciplinary research and collaboration across engineering, science, medicine, and other fields, while providing faculty, researchers, and students access to the complementary expertise and resources of both universities. All seven of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Tristan Driscoll, Search Committee Chair, at tdriscoll2@eng.famu.fsu.edu. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the Department and universities. A one-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information CBE has a dynamic group of faculty members actively involved in research encompassing various areas of chemical engineering, materials science and engineering, and biomedical engineering. The department has seen major expansion in the graduate and undergraduate biomedical and chemical engineering education and research activities since the establishment of an undergraduate BME degree in 2019 through the hiring of 15 new faculty members and approximately doubling of the graduate and undergraduate enrollment. The expanding college of engineering has increased research expenditures by 195% over the last 5 years ($87.6M in FY2025) and is continuing to grow its faculty and campus. A new research facility (the Interdisciplinary Research and Commercialization Building) was completed in Spring of 2025, and an additional engineering building was recently funded by the state legislature. Our nationally recognized and award-winning faculty members have access to state-of-the-art laboratories for research in biomedical and chemical engineering and the two programs are closely integrated in research and education. In addition to present faculty at the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering and its associated research centers, successful candidates will have many opportunities to interact and collaborate at both universities (including the FSU College of Medicine, the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, and the FAMU College of Pharmacy). Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on November 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63542&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Faculty - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) - Bioinformatics and Proteomics Software Development (NHMFL)",
      "description": "Job Title Research Faculty - 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) - Bioinformatics and Proteomics Software Development (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63542 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Ion Cyclotron Resonance (ICR) Program, National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL). The NHMFL is operated for the National Science Foundation by a collaboration of institutions comprising Florida State University, the University of Florida, and Los Alamos National Laboratory and houses the world’s premier ICR laboratory, with state-of-the-art FT-ICR mass spectrometers that operate at 21 T, 14.5 T, 9.4 T, and 9.4 T, for research in chemistry, materials science, engineering, geochemistry, biochemistry, and biology. Current areas include natural organic matter, emerging environmental contaminants, biofuels, top-down proteomics, lipidomics, metabolomics, and mass spectrometry imaging. Responsibilities The ICR Program seeks a research faculty member with expertise in bioinformatics, computational mass spectrometry, and scientific software development. The successful candidate will collaborate with researchers in the ICR Program to develop, implement, and validate novel algorithms for the analysis of high-resolution mass spectrometry data, with particular emphasis on top-down proteomics, de novo sequencing, proteoform characterization, and related applications in metabolomics and lipidomics. The candidate will contribute to the design of software tools and computational workflows for processing data generated by state-of-the-art FT-ICR and Orbitrap mass spectrometers. The candidate is expected to collaborate with NHMFL staff, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and external users; publish manuscripts; present at scientific conferences; and contribute to applications for external research funding. Additional responsibilities include maintaining software resources, supporting users with computational aspects of their projects, and helping to establish robust and reproducible data analysis pipelines for the ICR user community. Qualifications Candidates are expected to have a Ph.D. in Bioinformatics, Computer Science, Computational Biology, Analytical Chemistry, Data Science, or a closely related STEM field, along with experience conducting interdisciplinary research in a collaborative environment. For the Research Faculty I level, 2-5 years of additional experience in these areas is required. For the rank of Research Faculty II or III, 6-9 or 10+ years, respectively, of additional experience is required. The successful candidate must have demonstrated expertise in software development and scientific programming in Python, including the ability to independently design, implement, test, and maintain research software, scientific algorithms, and computational workflows. Candidates should have a record of scholarly achievement through peer-reviewed publications, software development, or other research accomplishments and experience analyzing large, complex biological datasets. Applicants must demonstrate experience developing computational tools through peer-reviewed software publications, publicly available software packages, GitHub repositories, or equivalent evidence of software development. Preferred Qualifications Desired qualifications include experience with mass spectrometry-based proteomics, metabolomics, lipidomics, or related omics disciplines; development of algorithms and software for scientific data analysis; database searching and identification workflows for proteins, peptides, metabolites, or other biomolecules; and quantitative analysis of biological datasets. Experience applying artificial intelligence, machine learning, graph-based methods, pattern recognition, or statistical modeling to biological data is highly desirable. Additional experience with de novo sequencing, computational mass spectrometry, high-performance computing, and open-source software development is preferred. Familiarity with mass spectrometry data formats, computational workflows for high-resolution mass spectrometry, and the development of reproducible and well-documented software tools is desirable. Contact Info Kristina Hakansson , ICR Director, khakansson@magnet.fsu.edu Kayla West , NHMFL HR Director University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62407&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Chair, Professor 9 Month, Salaried (Materials Science and Engineering Department-FAMU-FSU College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Chair, Professor 9 Month, Salaried (Materials Science and Engineering Department-FAMU-FSU College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62407 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The newly established Department of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) seeks applications from highly qualified individuals for the position of Chair and Professor. Responsibilities The inaugural Chair of the Department of Materials Science and Engineering at the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering will provide visionary, strategic, and collaborative leadership to build and grow a department. Reporting to the Dean of the joint College, the Chair will play a pivotal role in shaping the department’s identity and trajectory. The Chair will lead the rapid establishment and growth of the department. The Chair will play a leading role in developing curricula, faculty recruitment and onboarding, faculty development, increasing research expenditures, and growing graduate production in a department that currently enrolls 18 Ph.D. students and benefits from over 20 affiliated faculty. Key priorities for the Chair include: Building and expanding the department through strategic hiring, mentorship, and program development. Developing and executing a strategic plan for the department aligned with the College’s Engineering Our Future (2024–2029) plan and using data-driven approaches to guide growth, assess impact, and ensure continuous improvement. Recruiting high-caliber faculty and quality graduate students. Setting the academic and research direction of the department, including establishing research priorities and funding strategies, as well as critical and shared research infrastructure development. Overseeing graduate curriculum development, with opportunities to expand existing MSE-related offerings across the College. Fostering multidisciplinary collaboration across departments and with external partners, including industry. Strengthening relationships with national laboratories, including leveraging proximity to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory and FSU’s membership in the Oak Ridge Associated Universities. Advocating for students, ensuring robust mentorship, support structures, and career development. Maximizing the use of new facilities, including the IRCB, which houses MSE offices and laboratories, and the forthcoming Engineering Building C, designed to expand instructional and research space. Engaging in fundraising and external relations, including establishing advisory councils and collaborating with College level advancement staff. The Chair will serve as a key advocate for the department within the College and across both universities, ensuring alignment with institutional goals and the College’s strategic priorities. Qualifications Candidate must possess an earned Ph.D. in materials science, or a closely related discipline. The successful candidate will be a visionary and strategic leader with a clear ability to build and grow academic and research programs. They will possess a strong record of scholarly achievement and be research-active, with credentials appropriate for appointment as a full professor. Exceptional candidates with equivalent qualifications may also be considered. Ideal candidates will demonstrate: A proven record of leadership through developing a high-impact, well-funded Ph.D.-level research program within their own area of research. Demonstrated success in leading major department or college-level initiatives and task forces and/or large research centers or programs in the related engineering fields. A long-term vision for the future of materials science and engineering, including curriculum development, research impact, and student success. Relevant experience in academic administration, strategic planning, and organizational development. The ability to drive rapid growth, creativity, and ambition to shape a new department. Strong management and people skills, with the ability to support and guide faculty, staff, and students. A collaborative spirit, with evidence of interdisciplinary research and programmatic partnerships. A commitment to mentorship, particularly of graduate students and early-career faculty. Diplomacy, emotional intelligence, and empathy, with the ability to navigate complex institutional structures and foster a collegial and departmental environment. Resilience and adaptability, with the capacity to lead through change and uncertainty. Listening and communication skills, with a transparent and leadership style. A track record of recruiting and retaining talent, and the ability to develop strategies that attract various faculty and students. The Chair must be comfortable operating within a unique joint college structure, where faculty hold tenure at either FAMU or FSU and maintain joint appointments. The Chair will create synergies and operationalize opportunities for collaboration and customized initiatives and programs. The role requires navigating two institutions and partnering across administrative boundaries. Other Information The newly established Department of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) represents a transformative opportunity to build on the foundations of an established interdisciplinary Ph.D. program. This includes defining MSE’s vision, recruiting faculty, developing academic programs, and training the next generation of materials scientists and engineers. The department currently offers graduate programs but is well-positioned for future expansion, potentially including undergraduate offerings as strategic priorities evolve. The MSE Department is centered in the brand-new Interdisciplinary Research and Commercialization Building (IRCB)— a state-of-the-art, 116,000-square-foot facility designed to accelerate interdisciplinary discovery and commercialization, which just opened in March 2025. Located in Innovation Park, the IRCB offers flexible open laboratories, core instrumentation, and collaborative spaces, placing the department at the center of a vibrant research ecosystem. This ecosystem includes: National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) High-Performance Materials Institute (HPMI) Applied Superconductivity Center (ASC) Florida Center for Advanced Aero-Propulsion (FCAAP) Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) Center for Resilient Infrastructure and Disaster Response (RIDER) Aero-Propulsion, Mechatronics, and Energy Center (AME) Together, these leading research centers and national labs create one of the most concentrated engineering research environments in the country, enabling collaboration across advanced materials, energy, aerospace, and national defense. Further enhancing the department’s capabilities will be the construction of Building C, a new 164,000-square-foot engineering facility that will expand research and instructional space. Designed for flexibility and growth, Building C will support cutting-edge laboratory development and will be tailored to the needs of new faculty and interdisciplinary research teams. MSE is also strategically aligned with initiatives in Quantum Science and Engineering and the Quantum Engineering Center, which includes new faculty hires and research in quantum materials, advanced manufacturing, and superconductivity. The MSE Department will benefit from the new Institute for Strategic Partnerships, Innovation, Research, and Education (InSPIRE) in Panama City. Supported by a $98.4 million grant from Triumph Gulf Coast, InSPIRE connects materials research with regional economic development, workforce training, and national security applications—particularly in aerospace-related materials and manufacturing. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include curriculum vitae and letter of interest. Faculty Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is a unique institution, established by the Florida Legislature in 1982, serving as the joint college of engineering for both Florida A&M University and Florida State University. Located in Innovation Park in Tallahassee, Florida, adjacent to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory home to the world’s most powerful magnets. The college is a hub for cutting-edge research and global collaboration. The FAMU-FSU joint college model is the only one of its kind in the United States, combining the strengths of two major public universities: FSU, a top-tier R1 research institution, and FAMU, a leading HBCU and land-grant university. This partnership fosters a dynamic and unique academic environment that merges the rigor of high-impact research with the mission-driven focus of historically Black colleges and universities. It results in one of the most pluralistic educational environments for engineering in the nation, giving students the opportunity to operate in teams that are closer to the real world than any other engineering school. The College of Engineering boasts over 3,200 enrolled students, including 2,727 undergraduates and 564 graduate students. Over the past five years, enrollment has surged across all levels: +22% in undergraduate, +44% in graduate, +74% in master’s, and +25% in doctoral programs. The College of Engineering is home to 13 degree areas, 8 Ph.D. programs, 6 academic departments, and 4 certificate programs. The research enterprise is growing at an extraordinary pace, reaching $83.8 million in annual research expenditures, representing a 234% increase since 2020. Research productivity per faculty has grown by 168%, now averaging $586,000 per faculty member, a powerful reflection of the College’s remarkable energy, drive, and upward trajectory. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This posting is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63506&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Head Coach - Middle School Girls Basketball (Part-time, OPS)",
      "description": "Job Title Head Coach - Middle School Girls Basketball (Part-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63506 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities Florida State University Schools (Florida High) is seeking a dedicated and student-centered Middle School Girls Basketball Head Coach to lead and grow our middle school Girls Basketball program. The MS Girls Basketball Head Coach will be responsible for fostering a positive, competitive, and developmentally appropriate environment that emphasizes sportsmanship, academic accountability, and athletic excellence. This position reports directly to the Athletic Director and is expected to uphold all FSUS, FHSAA, and FSU policies and procedures while supporting the mission and values of Florida High Athletics. Lead and supervise all aspects of the MS Girls Basketball program Plan and conduct practices, conditioning sessions, and skill development activities Develop training plans that promote athlete safety, technical development, and competitive growth Schedule contests in accordance with guidelines and school policies Monitor and support student-athlete academic progress and eligibility Establish effective communication with student-athletes, parents, administration, and staff Coordinate game logistics, transportation, and supervision in alignment with FSUS policies Promote the program through school communication, social media, and community engagement Organize team events, awards, and end-of-season recognition Manage equipment, uniforms, filed needs, and program inventory Ensure compliance with rules, district regulations, and FSUS clearance procedures Assist with off-season development, camps, clinics, and program growth initiatives Collaborate with youth and feeder programs to strengthen the long-term success of the MS Girls Basketball program Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent Valid State of Florida Coaching Certificate (or ability to obtain) Current certifications in CPR, First Aid, Concussion in Sports, and Sudden Cardiac Arrest (required prior to season) Experience working with children and young adults in an educational or athletic setting Strong organizational, leadership, and communication skills Preferred Qualifications Previous basketball coaching experience at the middle school, high school, club, or collegiate level Knowledge of rules and interscholastic athletics Playing experience at the high school, collegiate, or professional level College coursework or degree in Education, Kinesiology, Sports Management, or a related field Experience with player development, team management, and program building Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment were curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/Temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63503&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Director of Development for the John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art",
      "description": "Job Title Senior Associate Director of Development for the John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63503 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Senior Associate Director of Development for the John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art (The Ringling). will design and execute a personal solicitation program resulting in philanthropic support by maximizing the identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of prospects for gifts at the $100,000 and up level. This individual will secure, on an annual basis, private support at the major gift range and will also be responsible for identification of potential major gift prospects. This individual will be expected to uphold and exemplify the operating practices and mission of the Foundation. Strategic Fundraising Development Works with the Executive Director, Senior Director for Development, and other members of The Ringling’s development, communication and alumni team to develop and execute strategic fundraising initiatives on behalf of The Ringling, the University and the Foundation. Develops, coordinates and executes an annual major gift plan of The Ringling, implementing fund-raising activities designed to meet an established monetary goal. Establishes new relationships resulting in philanthropic revenue, maintains existing relationships which may generate new philanthropic revenue, and provides prospect/donor-related assessments of the performance of The Ringling. Identifies, qualifies and sustains a donor prospect portfolio with individuals who have a giving capacity of $100,000 or more. Secures gifts and pledges from alumni, parents, faculty, staff and friends of FSU. Administrative/Events Prepares proposals and gift agreements as required for proper gift documentation. Prepares correspondence with prospects and documents communications, solicitation activity and gift information in compliance with Foundation reporting guidelines. Creates, inspires and maintains donor loyalty, interest and enthusiasm through stewardship communication and activities designed to express recognition, appreciation and the impact of their gift(s). Implementation of such a stewardship plan may include but should not be limited to letters, communication of unit or university initiatives, invitations to appropriate activities, meetings, events, student engagement or the facilitation of campus visits. Central Development Collaboration Coordinates with FSU Foundation colleagues to identify prospects for planned giving, corporate and foundation giving, and major giving. Exhibits and promotes a comprehensive understanding of the philanthropic priorities of the unit, effectively matching the specific interests of prospects to those specific needs. Assists in the facilitation of meetings, communications, informational exchanges and project/philanthropic coordination with curators and department chairs. Plans for and initiates direct activities with prospects that are designed to enhance the affiliation between the prospect and the University. Travels frequently to meet with alumni, parents, faculty, staff and friends of FSU. Protects confidential information. Perform other related duties as required and assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and five years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and nine years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) A valid Florida Driver's License or the ability to obtain. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63490&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63490 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Computer Science | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Computer Science at the Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to begin in August 2027. This position is 9-month, full-time, and benefits eligible. We seek strong candidates in the theory, applications, or systems of AI and Data Science. We will also consider outstanding candidates in related areas. Outstanding applicants in other areas will also be considered. Responsibilities will include teaching, research, and service activities. Qualifications Applicants should hold a Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of Computer Science or closely related field and have a demonstrated record of scholarly accomplishments. Other Information The department currently has 31 tenure-track and 7 specialized faculty members and offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees, including an AI Concentration, a new MS in CyberAI, and a new BS in AI. The department is an NSA/DHS Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education (CAE/CDE) and Research (CAE-R). FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1: Doctoral Universities – Very High Research Activity and is ranked No. 17 among public universities in TIME’S America’s Best Colleges list. Its primary role is to serve as a center for advanced graduate and professional studies, with an emphasis on research and excellence in undergraduate education. Contact Info Questions can be emailed to Prof. Xiuwen Liu , Faculty Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include a curriculum vitae and statements of teaching and research philosophy with the online application. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Application review will begin on December 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63482&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Development, College of Medicine",
      "description": "Job Title Director of Development, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63482 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional development officers’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Director of Development will strategically execute a personal solicitation program resulting in philanthropic support by maximizing the identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of prospects for gifts at the $100,000 and up level for College of Medicine. This individual will secure, on an annual basis, private support at the major and principal gift level and will be responsible for identification of potential major and principal gift prospects. The Director of Development will be expected to uphold and exemplify the operating practices of the Division of University Advancement while raising philanthropic dollars in support of the mission of Florida State University. Works with the Dean, and the other members of the College of Medicine development, communication and alumni team to develop and execute strategic fundraising initiatives on behalf of the College and the university. Develops, coordinates, and executes an annual major gift plan, implementing fund-raising activities designed to meet an established monetary goal while also hitting a set suite of metrics. Establishes new relationships resulting in philanthropic investment, maintains existing relationships, which may generate new philanthropic investments, and provides prospect/donor-related assessments and feedback for the College and the Division of University Advancement. Identifies, qualifies and sustains a donor prospect portfolio with individuals who have a giving capacity of $500,000 or more. Travels frequently, and secures gifts and pledges from alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of FSU. Exhibits and promotes a comprehensive understanding of the philanthropic priorities of the College, effectively matching the specific interests of prospects to those needs. Plans for and initiates direct activities with prospects that are designed to enhance the affiliation between the prospect and FSU. Effectively communicates FSU’s mission and represents FSU’s culture to external stakeholders. Central Development Collaboration Coordinates with the Division of University Advancement colleagues to identify prospects for planned giving, corporate and foundation giving in partnership with the Office of University Research, and principal giving in partnership with the Principal Gifts Team. Protects confidential information. Perform other related duties as required and assigned. Administrative/Events Assists in the facilitation of meetings, communications, informational exchanges and project / philanthropic coordination with the faculty and faculty chairs. Prepares proposals and gift agreements as required for proper gift documentation. Prepares correspondence with prospects and documents communications, solicitation activity and gift information in compliance with the FSU Foundation’s reporting guidelines. Creates, inspires, and maintains donor loyalty, interest and enthusiasm through stewardship communication and activities designed to express recognition, appreciation and the impact of their gift(s). Implementation of such a stewardship plan may include but should not be limited to letters, communication of unit or university initiatives, invitations to appropriate activities, meetings, events, student engagement or the facilitation of campus visits. Board/Volunteer Management Assists in the management of all volunteer boards associated with the College of Medicine. Qualifications Master's degree and four years of experience in a related advancement field or a Bachelor's degree and six years of related experience. Higher education can substitute for experience at a comparable rate. A valid Florida Driver's License or the ability to obtain upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This role requires driving and travel. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63491&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Data Science & AI) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63491 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Computer Science | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Computer Science at Florida State University invites applications for a tenure-track open rank Professor position to begin in August 2027. The position is 9-month, full-time, and eligible for benefits. Focus areas include Machine Learning Systems, Foundation Models, and Multi-Agent Systems, as well as supporting domains for AI, such as Big Data Engineering, Edge Computing and Sensor Networks, High-Performance Computing, and Human-Computer Interaction. We will also consider outstanding candidates in related areas. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in Computer Science or closely related field with demonstrated record of achievement in teaching and academic research is required. Candidates with outstanding academic credentials commensurate with tenured Associate or Full Professors are encouraged. Candidates at this level will be expected to have the experience and expertise to lead a cutting-edge research group. Other Information The department currently has 31 tenure-track and 7 specialized faculty members and offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees, including an AI Concentration, a new MS in CyberAI, and a new BS in AI. The department is an NSA/DHS Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education (CAE/CDE) and Research (CAE-R). FSU is classified as a Carnegie R1: Doctoral Universities – Very High Research Activity and is ranked No. 17 among public universities in TIME’S America’s Best Colleges list. Its primary role is to serve as a center for advanced graduate and professional studies, with an emphasis on research and excellence in undergraduate education. Contact Info Questions can be emailed to Prof. Xiuwen Liu , Faculty Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include a curriculum vitae and statements of teaching and research philosophy with the online application. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Application review will begin on December 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63499&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried, Center for Advanced Power Systems",
      "description": "Job Title Research Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried, Center for Advanced Power Systems Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63499 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) Responsibilities Responsibilities include, but are not limited to the following: Research and development of MV power converter for transportation and grid applications. Develop novel designs of gate drivers for WBG modules. Conduct collaborative research with CAPS Faculty and other researchers at FSU and other universities. Develop an independent research program engaging post-doctoral researchers and graduate students in the power electronics area. Develop compelling proposals for competitive external grants and contracts from federal agencies and industry sponsors. Publish research results in reputed journals and internal conferences. Qualifications An academic doctorate or the highest-level degree in electrical engineering with a specialization in power electronics, or a related field from an accredited institution with a demonstrated record of achievement in research. Preferred Qualifications At least one year of experience in power electronics or a related field. Strong publication record in power electronics or related fields. Rich experience with high voltage and high power hardware development. Demonstrated record of collaboration, publications, and conference presentations. Contact Info Rachel Brouwer , 850-645-2157 FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
