    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63437&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Human Development and Family Science - Department of Human Development and Family Science - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Human Development and Family Science - Department of Human Development and Family Science - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63437 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Human Development and Family Science - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Conduct quality research in the broad domain of human development and family science. Provide guidance, leadership, and mentorship to graduate students. Provide quality teaching to undergraduate and graduate students. Support the service needs of the Department, College, and University. Collaborate with and support Departmental Centers and Institutes, such as the Family Institute and the Center for Couples and Family Therapy. Qualifications Earned doctorate in a relevant area of study (e.g., family studies/science, human development, or psychology). A record of research accomplishments with the potential for extramural funding. Evidence of college-level teaching excellence. Preferred Qualifications Experience with or secured extramural funding. Experience at Research 1 universities. Ability to teach online, hybrid, and traditional modes. Demonstrated success working with all student populations. Other Information The Department of Human Development and Family Science (HDFS) in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor position. We seek a colleague committed to research, mentorship, teaching, and advising. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in ongoing research in a well-defined scholarship area within the broad domain of human development and family science, with clear connections to human development (child, adolescent, adult or old age), family processes, family policy/programs, and/or relationship interventions. They will advise and mentor graduate students in the MS and Ph.D. programs, chair doctoral dissertation committees, contribute to academic service for the Department, College, and University, and apply for external funding to support and advance their research projects. The Department of Human Development and Family Science is committed to making a difference in the lives of people. Our programs focus on human development, family processes, and empirically supported relationship interventions. Specifically, our research, teaching, and service activities reflect our three program foci: Relational development and enhancement of children adolescents, young adults, couples, older adults, and families; distressed families and relational interventions; and the link between parenting and peer processes and relational and mental health outcomes. The Department also has a focus on health and well-being across the lifespan. The Department strives to provide undergraduate and graduate students with outstanding academic experiences in teaching, research, and professional development. For more information about the Department of Human Development and Family Science, visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/hdfs . The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Search Committee Co-Chairs: Francis Fincham and Tom Ledermann University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of research. Transcripts, work samples (such as published manuscripts and teaching artifacts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 11/30/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63390&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Institutional Review Board Administrator (Remote eligible), Office of Human Subjects Protection",
      "description": "Job Title Institutional Review Board Administrator (Remote eligible), Office of Human Subjects Protection Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63390 Location Remote Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Human Subjects Protection within the Division of Research seeks to fill the IRB Administrator position. Responsibilities This position provides human research subject matter information to Institutional Review Board (IRB) members, researchers and study staff and FSU employees by interpreting and communicating current regulatory requirements; assisting with completion of human research submission materials and use of the electronic protocol management system (RAMP IRB); and referral to related guidance, templates, information and other resources. Is responsible for conducting pre- and post-review of assigned human research and related submissions by applying applicable laws, policies and procedures; documenting all required and other findings; and communicating outcomes or need for clarification from researchers and study staff. Performs post-approval compliance monitoring (PACM) audits for select IRB approved and exempt studies; selected studies and audits will be prioritized based on the Risk Assessment Worksheet score. Focused and directed audits are triggered by PACM requests from reviewing IRB's, study sponsors, external funding and regulatory agencies, human research subjects' complaints, study team members, the OHSP Director, or other FSU leadership. Coordinates with supervisors and other staff in PACM audits to document trends and patterns about whether research is being conducted as approved by the IRB and in compliance with all applicable laws and policies pertaining to human subjects protections. Activities include preparing and disseminating reports of findings, and training researchers as may be necessary. Contributes to the development and implementation or delivery of human research guidance materials, templates and human research training and educational content for use by other staff, IRB members, researchers and study staff and FSU employees. Other duties as assigned as it relates to human subjects research compliance at FSU. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in related field with two years of human subjects protection experience. Degree may be substituted by a high school diploma/equivalent, an additional three years of related human subjects protection experience with documentation of increasingly advanced human subjects protection responsibilities, and certifications of completion of business courses. Certified IRB Professional (CIP), or eligibility for CIP within three years of hire. Preferred Qualifications Certified IRB Professional or research-related certification, such as CCRP or CHRC. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position has been designated as eligible for remote work based on the current position/job functions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63406&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Cooks/Hospitality Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Cooks/Hospitality Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63406 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Childcare & Early Learning Program Responsibilities Assist in meal preparation (per USDA standards), meal delivery, loading and unloading dishwasher, stocking food, and paper goods and general kitchen duties as it relates to the childcare facility. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent. Ability to follow verbal and written instructions. Ability to communicate verbally and in writing. Ability to lift/move up to 25 lbs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15 per hour How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Hours are flexible and depend on the Center's needs; typically 10 - 20 hours per week. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63405&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Teaching Classroom Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Teaching Classroom Assistants - FSU Childcare (Multiple Positions) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63405 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Childcare & Early Learning Program Responsibilities Assist faculty in the supervision of young children, six weeks to five years of age, in daily activities. Assist with housekeeping tasks, such as wiping down tables, cleaning the floors, etc. Assist with other needs of FSU Childcare as needed. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and some experience working with children. Preferred Qualifications Associate's degree or a degree in Early Childhood Education, Early Childhood Special Education, Child Development, or Family and Child Science. Other Information Applicable DCF-mandated post-hire training will be required. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15 per hour. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Hours are flexible and depend on the Center's needs; typically 10 - 20 hours per week. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63425&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Multiple Positions in Computer Engineering -Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering FAMU-FSU College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Multiple Positions in Computer Engineering -Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering FAMU-FSU College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63425 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities Candidates are expected to develop research programs that are internationally recognized with significant and sustained funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, supervise undergraduate, graduate and post-doctoral researchers, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in computer engineering, computer science, electrical engineering, or a closely related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research. Helpful The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint university is the college of engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven (7) of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Rodney Roberts, Search Committee Chair, at rroberts@eng.famu.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement including research interests and plans and how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page statement on teaching and philosophy No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. We are seeking faculty members with expertise in Computer Networks Security, Data Science, AI, Computer Vision, Robotics & Autonomy, Embedded Computing, and Cyber-physical Systems Security. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. The ECE Department currently has 37 faculty, 100+ graduate students, 450+ undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $20M. The two universities and outstanding research facilities in the affiliated research buildings/centers provide opportunities for collaboration with faculty in Computer Science and Scientific Computing, the Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) FAMU Center for Cyber Security, National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL), Center for Intelligent Systems, Control and Robotics (CISCOR), FSU Institute of Molecular Biophysics , FSU Jim Moran College of Entrepreneurship , and FSU College of Medicine. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Applications will be reviewed beginning on December 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63367&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Affiliation Agreements, 12 Month Salaried (0.5 FTE) (Office of Academic Services & Intern Support - Anne's College)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Director of Affiliation Agreements, 12 Month Salaried (0.5 FTE) (Office of Academic Services & Intern Support - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63367 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Academic Services and Intern Support (OASIS) | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Coordinate the full lifecycle of affiliation agreements and Memorandum of Understanding (MOUs), including drafting, routing, review, execution, and renewal. Serve as the primary point of contact for academic departments, university administrative offices, legal counsel, and external partner organizations regarding affiliation agreements. Maintain a centralized database of active agreements and supporting documentation. Monitor agreement expiration and renewal timelines to prevent disruptions to clinical, internship, practicum, and other experiential learning placements. Ensure agreements comply with university policies, accreditation standards, and applicable legal requirements. Track agreement status and provide updates to faculty, administrators, and external partners. Develop and maintain efficient workflows and documentation processes that improve operational effectiveness. Assist academic programs in establishing new partnerships by facilitating timely execution of required agreements. Qualifications Academic master’s degree from an accredited institution in education or a closely related field. Experience in administrative coordination, contract administration, project coordination, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Excellent organizational and project management skills with exceptional attention to detail. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with document management systems and Microsoft Office applications. Experience working with contracts, affiliation agreements, or Memorandums of Understanding. Knowledge of accreditation requirements related to clinical, practicum, internship, or experiential learning programs. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Experience maintaining confidential records and databases. Ability to collaborate effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Other Information The Office of Academic and Intern Support (OASIS) in Annes College is seeking a highly organized and collaborative professional to serve as the Assistant Director of Affiliation Agreements & Partnerships. This position plays a vital role in supporting the College's expanding network of clinical, internship, practicum, and experiential learning partnerships by managing affiliation agreements and Memorandums of Understanding (MOUs) with school districts, clinical sites, hospitals, healthcare systems, community organizations, agencies, and other external partners. This position will provide centralized oversight of affiliation agreements, ensuring timely execution, regulatory compliance, accurate recordkeeping, and effective collaboration with university offices and external partners. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Jessica Tucker University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities – from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application and names of three references with contact information. Review of candidates will begin 09/08/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a part-time, 20 hours per week (0.5 FTE) faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63407&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Month Salaried (School of Information)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor 9 Month Salaried (School of Information) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63407 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Communication & Information School of Information Responsibilities We are seeking a faculty colleague whose research and teaching will be in the broad domain of cybersecurity and who will employ a behavioral, sociotechnical, and/or technical perspective. Specific areas of research interest may include, but are not limited to, how cybersecurity interacts with areas such as artificial intelligence (AI), human-computer interaction (HCI), data science, information policy, information ethics, and computer networking. Successful candidates will have strong technical and/or analytical skills and be able to articulate a research agenda that aligns with the broader research interests of the iSchool. They must also clearly demonstrate the ability to work effectively within a highly interdisciplinary environment. Candidates should also indicate a clear plan for actively seeking external funding. In addition to strong research, the iSchool values highly effective and innovative teaching. Successful applicants must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching in cybersecurity-related areas. The successful candidate will be expected to teach at all levels, including courses in the iSchool’s bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. Experience teaching online, as well as face-to-face, is preferred. Faculty typically teach two courses per semester each academic year. All faculty members are expected to advise students, serve on iSchool, College, and University committees, and be active in professional and academic organizations. Qualifications Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Qualified applicants will have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in information science, information systems, information technology, or a cognate field. Other Information The School of Information is one of three academic units within the College of Communication and Information at Florida State University. The FSU iSchool offers a Bachelor’s degree program with majors in Information Technology (IT) and Information, Communication, and Technology (ICT); Master’s degree programs in Information Technology and Information; and a Ph.D. program in Information. The iSchool faculty also operates the eHealth Lab and iSensor Lab, and is a founding partner in FSU’s Innovation Hub, an innovation center and fab lab/makerspace for teaching and research that utilizes technologies including virtual/augmented reality, 3D printing, and 3D visualization. The School of Information, which launched in 1926, was formally founded in 1947 and is nationally ranked among the top information science graduate schools in the country. The iSchool's Master’s in Information Technology program is nationally ranked at #8 among online IT programs, #5 among IT programs for veterans, and the ALA-accredited Master's in Information is ranked among U.S. News & World Report's “Best Graduate Programs in Library and Information Science” as 12th overall. School of Information faculty have been awarded over $50 million in federal, state, local, and foundation research grants, and maintain strong connections to the community through various information, literacy, and service initiatives. Funding has been received from NIH, IMLS, NSF, and the DOD as well as The Robert Wood Johnson Foundation, The McKnight Foundation, and others. iSchool faculty have strong collaborations with researchers in the College of Medicine, College of Social Work, College of Nursing, College of Education, Health and Human Sciences, and College of Arts and Sciences. More information about the School of Information is available online at: http://ischool.cci.fsu.edu/ The iSchool is a member of the College of Communication and Information and has a student population of approximately 390 undergraduates and 566 graduate students. The iSchool boasts 18 tenured/tenure-track and 10 full-time non-tenure-track faculty members. The College is a leader on campus and is nationally recognized for its distance and online education programs. For more information about the college, see https://cci.fsu.edu/. Contact Info Inquiries should be directed to: George Moore 850-644-5775 gmm26c@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. All applications must include a cover letter, CV, research statement, and teaching statement. The School of Information (iSchool) at Florida State University seeks to fill one (1) nine-month tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. Review of applications will begin on September 30, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63363&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Counseling Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Counseling Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63363 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities This position will involve the following: research/scholarship in any substantive area related to counseling psychology. graduate teaching (e.g., assessment courses, clinical courses). supervision of doctoral students in clinical practicum settings. chairing and serving on graduate student supervisory committees. mentoring/supervising doctoral student research. serving on program, departmental, and college committees. program/curriculum development and evaluation of the APA-accredited doctoral program. Qualifications Ph.D. or terminal degree from an accredited institution in Counseling Psychology, or a closely related field is required. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to research and scholarship, teaching, supervision, program development, and the integration of science and practice, while serving as a professional role model. Preferred Qualifications We encourage applicants with expertise in Counseling Psychology, knowledge of APA-accreditation procedures, and familiarity with national training issues in professional psychology. Additionally, candidates with experience conducting and publishing research in areas relevant to counseling psychology are strongly encouraged to apply. We seek candidates with counseling or supervision experience, prior teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level, and a developing or well-established independent research program. A record of success, or strong potential for success, in teaching, research, and service is highly valued. Preference will be given to candidates who hold a Ph.D. in Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited program and who demonstrate a commitment to the professional identity of a health service psychologist. Current licensure, or eligibility for licensure within the first year of employment, as a psychologist in Florida is strongly preferred. Additionally, prior tenure-track experience and demonstrated potential or proven success in securing external research funding are highly desirable. Other Information The Department of Educational Psychology and Learning Systems (EPLS) invites applications for a tenure-earning Assistant Professor position within the Psychological and Counseling Services (PCS) program, specifically for the Combined Counseling Psychology & School Psychology doctoral program. Our faculty brings a broad range of experiences and research interests, and we are eager to welcome a new team member who will enhance our department. We seek an exceptional candidate with strong training and professional identity in the field of Counseling Psychology. The EPLS department is home to the Assessment, Learning Evaluation, & Counseling (ALEC) Center , which serves as a hub for training doctoral students and conducting research. The department also has a NASP-accredited School Psychology program and CACREP-approved programs in Mental Health Counseling, School Counseling, and Career Counseling. Our faculty brings a broad range of experiences and research interests, and we are eager to welcome a new team member who will enhance our department, academic programs, and ALEC. The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. Debra Osborn Search Committee Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities – from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, a statement of teaching interests, and a research statement. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/02/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63368&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Sport Management - Anne's College)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Sport Management, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Sport Management - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63368 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Sport Management | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The individual hired will be required to maintain an active research agenda, possess strong knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methods for the effective mentoring of master’s and doctoral student research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses (including teaching online courses), seek external funding, aid in developing external partnerships, and contribute to department and university growth through appropriate service activities. Qualifications Earned doctorate degree in Sport Management or related field; college/university teaching experience; mentoring experience; evidence of scholarly productivity; experience procuring external funding, or evidence of ability to procure external funding. An individual’s program of research should align with one of the department’s core content areas. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to individuals with a research interest aligned with business-related content (e.g., marketing, finance, economics, management). Preference will also be given to individuals with a record of procuring external funding. Other Information Candidates are being sought for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department Sport Management in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences. The department has four core areas: Legal and Policy Studies, Management, Marketing, and Media and Cultural Studies. This is a nine-month position, with possible summer employment. Candidates should be available to start in the Fall 2027 semester (approximately August 9, 2027). The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Dr. James Du Search Committee Chair Questions regarding the application submission system and process should be directed to the application coordinator: Katherine Maddox Sr. Administrative Specialist University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities – from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include (1) a current curriculum vitae, (2) a letter of interest highlighting their qualifications for the position, (3) the names and contact information of three references, (4) a statement of research, and 5) a statement of teaching philosophy. Transcripts and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of applications will begin October 19, 2026. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63365&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Sport Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor in Sport Psychology, 9 Month Salaried (Educational Psychology & Learning Systems - Anne's College) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63365 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems | Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to serve on doctoral committees and supervise student research, in addition to teaching and providing service to the program, department, college, and university. Candidates are also responsible for developing a program of research and scholarly activity in the realm of sport psychology. Qualifications Candidates for this position should have an earned doctorate from a recognized doctoral program in Sport Psychology or a closely related field (e.g., Kinesiology, Exercise Science). Preferred Qualifications Prior tenure-track experience and demonstrated potential or proven success in securing external research funding are highly desirable. Prior experience mentoring doctoral students is also preferred. Other Information The program is seeking a candidate with clearly expressed interest in sport psychology research and professional issues. The successful candidate will demonstrate an aptitude for conducting research, teaching, and mentoring graduate students, as well as a commitment to both the Sport Psychology MS and PhD programs. We are seeking a candidate who will contribute to strengthening program quality and student recruitment. The successful candidate will also demonstrate skills related to the quality teaching of sport psychology courses. This top-ranked program has a vibrant Sport Psychology Lab and connections to the Institute of Sport Science and Medicine (ISSM) . The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. Contact Info Search Committee Co-Chairs: Brady DeCouto David Eccles University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Tallahassee as a community is a vibrant mid-size city with abundant opportunities – from government internships and legislative initiatives to special events, shopping, dining, and outdoor activities. Tallahassee is located near the Gulf Beaches of Florida and enjoys abundant sunshine and four seasons with a mild winter climate. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, a statement of teaching interests, and a research statement. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin 10/02/2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63386&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Violin, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor of Violin, 9 Month Salaried - College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63386 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Music Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate-level violin students. Recruit and maintain a successful teaching studio. Serve on doctoral and master’s committees and juries. Maintain a professional career as a performing artist. Participate in university and professional service activities nationally and internationally as appropriate. Additional responsibilities may include coaching chamber music and teaching courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Qualifications Hold a doctoral degree or demonstrate a record of equivalent performance and teaching experience. Hold a record of successful university-level studio teaching experience and proven artistry as a professional performer. Demonstrate strong commitment to the recruitment of outstanding students. Demonstrate a proven commitment to creating an environment which contributes to the vibrancy and economy of the university community and engages students. Other Information Seeking new knowledge and deeper understanding of music in interdisciplinary contexts through innovative research, music performance, and creative activity, The College of Music at Florida State University is the largest such college in the Southeast and one of the largest university-based music programs in the nation. We are home to over 600 undergraduate and over 300 graduate students, who represent nearly every state in the nation and 26 foreign countries. Contact Info Alexander Jimenez , Professor of Conducting and Director of Orchestral Activities University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In addition to the online application, please attach a single document that includes: Cover Letter (1-2 pages) Curriculum Vitae Contact information for four professional references (mailing address, phone, email). Links to video recordings made within the past five years that include: A 20-minute teaching video. A performance video (s) demonstrating a variety of styles. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin August 2027. However, for priority consideration, please complete all application materials by September 28, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain ongoing until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63374&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Elementary Mathematics Education School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Elementary Mathematics Education School of Teacher Education - Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63374 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences Responsibilities Applicants will be expected to engage in research and seek external funding related to Mathematics Education for Elementary Students, teach undergraduate courses (specifically elementary mathematics methods courses) and graduate courses, collaborate with Elementary Education faculty, advise and mentor Master’s and Doctoral students, conduct research that informs the field, collaborate with STEM faculty, and provide service to the university, local community partners, and the profession. Qualifications Earned doctorate in Elementary Education, Mathematics Education (or a related field such as Curriculum & Instruction with a focus on STEM education) by August 2027. A strong record of scholarship commensurate with position, as indicated by peer-reviewed journal publications, conference presentations, and collaborative projects. A productive and innovative research agenda that operates within a strong theoretical and empirical approach to understanding some facet of Elementary Mathematics Teaching or Learning Experience teaching at elementary and post-secondary levels. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience securing and/or working on externally funded research projects. Experience collaborating with STEM faculty and/or elementary schools. A research focus on learning technologies, AI, and/or data science in the context of mathematics and statistics teaching and learning. Other Information The School of Teacher Education in the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences at Florida State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning assistant professor of Elementary Mathematics Education position to start in August of 2027. Faculty in the Mathematics Education Program in the School of Teacher Education strive to develop a deep understanding of, and respect for, our teaching candidates and colleagues. The fac ulty have a long history of internationally recognized scholarship and a track-record of award-winning scholarship and consistent external funding. Our goal is to inform the field’s understanding of mathematics teaching and learning through research and policy development aimed at transforming lives and striving towards collective wellness and more sustainable ways of being . For information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences, visit https://annescollege.fsu.edu . For more information about the program, visit https://annescollege.fsu.edu/mathematics-education The roots of FSU’s Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences date back to the university’s establishment, and it is the oldest college of its kind in Florida. The College is home to six academic departments united through a common goal to maximize human potential. In total, the College includes the Department of Educational Leadership & Policy Studies, Department of Educational Psychology & Learning Systems, Department of Human Development & Family Sciences, Department of Health, Nutrition & Food Sciences, Department of Sport Management, School of Teacher Education, numerous research centers, and three laboratory schools (Florida State University School, FSU Pembroke Pines Charter School, and The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City). Anne’s College serves over 4,000 students via approximately 200 full-time faculty and nearly 80 full-time staff. For more information about the Anne Spencer Daves College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences visit: https://annescollege.fsu.edu/ . Contact Info Christine Andrews-Larson University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should also include a letter of application, names of three references with contact information, and a statement of teaching interests. Transcripts, work samples (such as teaching artifacts or manuscripts), and three letters of recommendation will be required of candidates selected for an interview. Review of candidates will begin Oct 2, 2026 and will continue until filled. We urge interested candidates to submit materials as soon as possible. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
