    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63327&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63327 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College Of Criminology and Criminal Justice The College of Criminology and Criminal Justice at Florida State University is a vibrant academic community which fosters an environment of collaborative research and intellectual stimulation among its faculty and students. The College invites applications for assistant professor positions to begin Fall 2027. The areas of specialization are open. Responsibilities • Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a state university • Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities • Responsible for academic advising and related activities • May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees Qualifications Applicants must have demonstrated effectiveness in research and teaching. Candidates should have a Ph.D. in Criminology and Criminal Justice or a related field (such as sociology, psychology, or public policy). ABD candidates who anticipate degree completion no later than August 2027 will also be considered. A Juris Doctorate alone is not sufficient for consideration. Contact Info Any questions regarding the position may be directed to search committee chair Sonja Siennick at ssiennick@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Interested persons should complete an application and submit a cover letter, statements on research and teaching, and a curriculum vitae. In addition, they should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent to CCCJ-SearchCommittee@fsu.edu with the subject line “Letter of Recommendation for [applicant].” Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63329&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice)",
      "description": "Job Title Associate Professor, 9 Month Salaried (College of Criminology and Criminal Justice) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63329 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Criminology and Criminal Justice The College of Criminology and Criminal Justice at Florida State University is a vibrant academic community which fosters an environment of collaborative research and intellectual stimulation among its faculty and students. The College invites applications for a tenure-track associate or full professor position to begin Fall 2027. The areas of specialization are open. Responsibilities • Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a state university • Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities • Responsible for academic advising and related activities • May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees Qualifications Applicants must have demonstrated excellence in research and teaching. Candidates should have a Ph.D. in Criminology and Criminal Justice or a related field (such as sociology, psychology, or public policy). A Juris Doctorate alone is not sufficient for consideration. Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026. Contact Info Any questions regarding the position may be directed to search committee chair Sonja Siennick at ssiennick@fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. In addition, you should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent to CCCJ-SearchCommittee@fsu.edu with the subject line “Letter of Recommendation for [applicant].” Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on September 28, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63299&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Molecular Biodesign)",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Molecular Biodesign) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63299 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry seeks to fill a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor at the intersection of chemistry, biology, and medicine. Leveraging the resources of the Institute of Molecular Biophysics (IMB), this search is open to all areas of the chemical sciences with a focus on molecular biodesign, including biochemistry, organic chemistry, medicinal chemistry, bioanalytical chemistry, chemical biology, bioinorganic chemistry, and biophysical chemistry. Outstanding candidates are sought to pursue innovative experimental research that advances the molecular understanding of biological systems and enables the discovery and development of new therapeutics. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a nationally and internationally recognized and externally funded research program in addition to teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service is required. Candidates whose research incorporates artificial intelligence and machine learning are encouraged to apply. Contact Info Questions may be directed to the Faculty Search Team . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications must include the following: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Prospectus Teaching Statement Applicants should also arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent via email to The Faculty Search Team . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on October 19, 2026. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63298&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Theoretical/Computational Chemistry & Biochemistry) - Multiple Positions",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Theoretical/Computational Chemistry & Biochemistry) - Multiple Positions Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63298 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry at Florida State University seeks candidates for two tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor in theoretical/computational chemistry and biochemistry. One position is open to all areas of theory and computation relevant to the chemical and biochemical sciences. The second position will focus on leveraging advances in artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) for chemistry and biochemistry, broadly defined. Applications where AI/ML work is complemented by experimental validation are also encouraged. The successful candidates will be expected to develop nationally and internationally recognized and externally funded research programs in addition to teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in a related field with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service is required. Contact Info Questions may be directed to the Faculty Search Team . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications must include the following: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Prospectus Teaching Statement Applicants should also arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent via email to The Faculty Search Team . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Review of applications will begin on October 16, 2026. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63287&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Accounting Department - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) - Fall 2027",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Accounting Department - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) - Fall 2027 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63287 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Accounting | Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Florida State University, Department of Accounting, invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 2027. This position will be required to publish in leading scholarly journals, along with teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. You will also continue research efforts and progress towards promotion and tenure. Qualifications All candidates should have a Ph.D. in Accounting. Preferred Qualifications Candidates must demonstrate an ability to publish in leading scholarly journals and a commitment to excellence in teaching. All areas of research and teaching expertise will be considered. Applicants with a professional background in financial planning may have an opportunity to teach a specialized wealth management course and should note this in their applications. Contact Info Allen Blay Department Chair University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit their curriculum vitae, at least one working paper, and three reference letters by email to acctg-recruiting1@business.fsu.edu . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63263&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "FSUS Paraprofessional, 6 -12 (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Job Title FSUS Paraprofessional, 6 -12 (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63263 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities The paraprofessional will work under the direction and supervision of certified staff to support academic and behavioral needs of students in the classroom and other school settings. This role involves assisting with instructional activities, supervising students, and providing one-on-one or small group support to help students achieve academic success and positive social outcomes. Assist the classroom teacher in implementing lesson plans and instructional activities. Work with individual students or small groups to reinforce learning concepts introduced by the teacher. Support students with special needs by implementing IEP accommodations and modifications as directed. Assist with classroom management by monitoring student behavior and promoting a safe and respectful environment. Help with the preparation of instructional materials and classroom organization. Supervise students in various settings, including classrooms, hallways, cafeterias, playgrounds, and school events. Provide clerical support such as photocopying, filing, and data entry as needed. Maintain confidentiality and demonstrate professionalism at all times. Participate in training and professional development activities as required. Qualifications High school diploma. Experience working with childeren or in an educational settng. Strong communication, collaboration, and orgainzational skills. Ability to follow directions, take initiative, and respond flexibly to changing needs. Patience, Compassion, and a commitment to supporting student learning and well-being. Preferred Qualifications Associate or bachelor's degree, two years of college (60 credit hours), or successful completion of a state4-approved paraprofessional assessment. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. Contact Info Jaye Corbett University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/Temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62884&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Grants Officer Open Level (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Job Title Grants Officer Open Level (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62884 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Sponsored Research Administration | Pre-Award Responsibilities Grants Officer I This entry-level position will advise and assist faculty and staff in pre-award and post-award non-financial sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities, including proposal preparation, review, submission, and tracking of sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities from public sources. Negotiate basic agreements by serving as the primary liaison with funding/sponsoring agencies. Review sub-recipient documents and determine contract/vendor relationships. Accept awards and coordinate post-award non-financial activities. Maintain regular contact with principal investigators, deans, chairs, departmental administrators, and funding agency officials regarding interpretation and application, and procedures. Grants Officer II This intermediate-level position will advise and assist faculty and staff in pre-award and post-award nonfinancial sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities, including, but not limited to, proposal preparation, review, submission, and tracking of sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities from public sources. Negotiate basic and complex agreements by serving as the primary liaison with funding/sponsoring agencies. Review sub-recipient documents. Accept awards and coordinate post-award non-financial activities. Maintain regular contact with principal investigators, deans, chairs, departmental administrators, and funding agency officials regarding interpretation, application, and procedures. Grants Officer III This advanced-level position will advise and assist faculty and staff in pre-award and post-award non-financial sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities, including, but not limited to, proposal preparation, review, submission, and tracking of sponsored research, instruction, and public service activities from public sources. Negotiate basic and complex agreements by serving as the primary liaison with funding/sponsoring agencies. Review sub-recipient documents. Accept awards and coordinate post award non-financial activities. Maintain regular contact with principal investigators, deans, chairs, departmental administrators, and funding agency officials regarding interpretation, application, and procedures. Mentor staff. Have a limited delegation of signature authority for the Vice President for Research. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of relevant experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Level I - Bachelor’s degree and 2 years’ experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 6 years. Level II - Bachelor’s degree and 3 years’ experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 7 years. Level III - Bachelor’s degree and 4 years’ experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to 8 years plus CRA certification. These positions require successful completion of the eSPEAR certification series within the first six months from the start date. Preferred Qualifications Experience and the ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to comprehend and interpret state, federal, and sponsoring agencies' rules, regulations, policies, and laws regarding sponsored research. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, changing environment and to interact with people at all levels diplomatically, tactfully, and professionally. Preferred experience with contract review and negotiations (e.g., FAR clauses, federal contracting, SBIRs, and STTRs). Helpful Who is the ideal candidate for this position? You will be known as the go-to person for a specific department range within SRA. You have a good rapport with others and can work closely with department representatives, faculty members, and colleagues in SRA via telephone, Zoom/Teams, and e-mail. You will also work directly with grants/contracts/administrative officers at a sponsor (e.g., FL Department of Health, National Science Foundation), which likewise requires diplomacy, tact, and good communication skills for resolving issues and negotiating. You are detail-oriented and analytical, as well as a good multitasker and problem solver. You enjoy learning something new every day. You are both a team player and an independent worker. What is a typical day in this position? Every day can be different. One day, you may be submitting several proposals and setting up award time extensions while, the next day, you could be reviewing and negotiating contracts, reviewing a budget and budget justification for an upcoming proposal, and reaching out to a faculty member about their upcoming amendment for time and money. You will attend team meetings regularly and a full staff meeting monthly. If you enjoy working in a medium-sized department, which is a collegial professional and has you learning something new all of the time, you'll be happy in SRA. There are many training opportunities that can be attended virtually and in person. What can I expect in the first 60 – 90 days? In the first few weeks, you will meet your team and the entire SRA staff. Our IT team will make sure you are up and running usually by the end of your first day. Then, you will be able to get acquainted with our website and our policies and procedures. You will be shadowing and working closely with team members, completing the eSPEAR Certificate Series online training, and starting to work on certain tasks independently. At the 6-month mark, you will notice that you've learned much and are comfortable in your position. Our staff is always available to answer any questions you may have while learning your new position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. A cover letter must be provided to be considered for this position. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is based in Tallahassee and is eligible for a hybrid work schedule. The schedule is Monday-Friday 8:00 AM-5:00 PM. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as received. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63257&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "FSUS Paraprofessional, K-5 (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Job Title FSUS Paraprofessional, K-5 (Full-time, OPS) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63257 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities The paraprofessional will work under the direction and supervision of certified staff to support the academic and behavioral needs of students in the classroom and other school settings. This role involves assisting with instructional activities, supervising students, and providing one-on-one or small group support to help students achieve academic success and positive social outcomes. Assist the classroom teacher in implementing lesson plans and instructional activities. Work with individual students or small groups to reinforce learning concepts introduced by the teacher. Support students with special needs by implementing IEP accommodations and modifications as directed. Assist with classroom management by monitoring student behavior and promoting a safe and respectful environment. Help with the preparation of instructional materials and classroom organization. Supervise students in various settings, including classrooms, hallways, cafeterias, playgrounds, and school events. Provide clerical support such as photocopying, filing, and data entry as needed. Maintain confidentiality and demonstrate professionalism at all times. Participate in training and professional development activities as required. Qualifications High school diploma Experience working with children or in an educational setting Strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills Ability to follow directions, take initiative, and respond flexibly to changing needs Patience, compassion, and a commitment to supporting student learning and well-being Preferred Qualifications Associate or bachelor's degree, two years of college (60 credit hours), or successful completion of a state-approved paraprofessional assessment. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors or academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights, directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. Contact Info Jaye Corbett University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via ACHA's Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the ACHA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61131&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Psychologist (Two Positions) – Clinical Assistant Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Student Affairs/Admissions - Medicine)",
      "description": "Job Title Faculty Psychologist (Two Positions) – Clinical Assistant Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Student Affairs/Admissions - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61131 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Student Affairs/Admissions Responsibilities The FSU College of Medicine (COM) Office of Student Counseling Services provides psychological and educational support services to graduate students in the Medicine, Physician Assistant, Bridge to Medicine, and Biomedical Sciences programs. The faculty psychologist will be responsible for providing individual therapy and personal counseling to matriculated students for general mental health concerns, adjustment disorders, personal stressors, and the promotion of well-being; for advising students and developing strategies to address academic deficiencies and to facilitate academic success; for the initial evaluation, screening, and referral as appropriate of matriculated students for psychiatric care; and for developing and managing a network of referral relationships with qualified practitioners who can provide additional services for students if required. All services are provided on-site in the FSU COM via in-person or telehealth scheduled appointments. As faculty, the incumbent will be expected to be active in teaching, clinical service, and research consistent with the College of Medicine's mission. Qualifications Applicants must hold a doctoral degree from an American Psychological Association (APA)-approved counseling or clinical psychology program to include an APA-approved pre-doctoral internship and Florida licensure as a psychologist, or eligibility to obtain within 90 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications At least two years of experience in counseling or clinical psychology, with a minimum of one year of post-doctoral clinical experience in individual and group counseling, to include psychological assessments, and/or consultations. Strong oral and written communication skills. Preference given to candidates with postdoctoral work experience with college students or with young adults in a health science setting and/or experience providing academic support services. Doctorate level training in the science of learning, including educational psychology or school psychology. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for the role? This role is ideal for a team-oriented candidate looking for an opportunity to work in a small office with three psychologists and one administrative support employee in a collaborative environment. The candidate must enjoy and be passionate about providing clinical services to the graduate student population, which includes not only therapy services but also academic support services. What is a typical day? A typical day primarily involves provision of direct service (academic and/or mental health support) to College of Medicine graduate students in individual appointments. Some group services may be provided in either an academic or therapy context. This faculty position also includes a small percentage of scholarly and teaching responsibilities. Contact Info Taylor Thompson, Ph.D. 850/644-0492 tlthompson@admin.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position is expected to offer a salary in the range of $95,000 – $105,000; however, final compensation will be determined based on experience and qualifications. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The job opening serves to recruit for two non-tenure earning positions. There is no remote work option for these positions. This job opening is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=59627&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Family Physician/Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried – Multiple Positions (Family Medicine & Rural Health - Medicine - Tallahassee, FL)",
      "description": "Job Title Family Physician/Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried – Multiple Positions (Family Medicine & Rural Health - Medicine - Tallahassee, FL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 59627 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Family Medicine & Rural Health Responsibilities The Department of Family Medicine and Rural Health is seeking academic family medicine physicians to fill full-time 12-month open rank faculty positions at a minimum rank of either Assistant or Associate Professor, dependent upon qualifications and experience. This is a clinical position and is not tenure-earning eligible. The positions will involve substantial teaching and supervision of health professional students as well as assisting in the delivery of an innovative, integrated curriculum and practice in a clinical facility. The positions will include around 40% direct patient care at an affiliated primary care practice (credentialing required). The Department has research interests in the areas of health equity, community health, rural health, and innovative health care. Qualifications Applicants must have a doctoral degree (MD or DO) in an appropriate field from an accredited institution and personal and professional goals which are consistent with the mission of the FSU College of Medicine. Applicants must have completed an approved U.S. Residency Program. Applicants must have Board Certification in Family Medicine or other acceptable discipline and participate in maintenance of certification. Applicants should have relevant academic, clinical, and professional experience, excellent skills in communication and collaboration, and be passionate about the field of family medicine and rural health. Additional specific requirements and qualifications include: Must possess, or obtain within 90 days of hire, a valid Florida license to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification by a certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to foster an educational environment conducive to patient-centered medical student and physician assistant education. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following will be required: Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician reporting negative results within the past six months. Documentation of physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician within the past six months. Within 30 days of hire, must provide: Documentation of vaccination for Tetanus within the last 10 years. Proof of immunization OR positive titers for Hepatitis B. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching medical students and primary care research is highly desired. Clinical experience post-residency/fellowship is desired. Scholarly interest, knowledge and experience with health equity or community-based health outcomes or clinical research is desired. Knowledge and experience with medical informatics is desired. Other Information The Florida State University College of Medicine (FSU COM) has a focused mission of training patient-centered physicians devoted to the needs of rural, underserved, minority, and elderly populations. FSU COM is very “Family Medicine friendly” with family physicians holding several key administrative positions including Dean of the College. As a community-based medical school, FSU COM is particularly well-suited for conducting research in primary care and community settings. Contact Info Ms. Ute Sartin, Assistant Director, Email: ute.sartin@med.fsu.edu Ms. Danyel White, Sr. Administrative Specialist, Email: danyel.white@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include the following: Cover letter of interest Curriculum vitae Letters of Reference (refer to steps below) 2 - 3 page teaching, mentoring, and service statement that describes prior experiences and future plans 2 - 3 page research statement that briefly summarizes your significant research accomplishments and describes your future research plans Request Letters of Reference This position requires that you have 3 - 4 confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as received. This job opening serves to recruit for two positions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61261&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Geriatrics - Medicine)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 12 Months Salaried (Geriatrics - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61261 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Geriatrics Responsibilities The Department of Geriatrics is seeking an academic geriatric physician to fill a full-time 12-month open-rank faculty position at a minimum rank of either Assistant or Associate Professor, dependent upon qualifications and experience. The position will involve substantial teaching and supervision of health professional students as well as assisting in the delivery of an innovative, integrated curriculum and practice in a clinical facility. The positions will include around 50% direct patient care at an affiliated primary care practice (credentialing required). The Department has research interests in the areas of geriatrics workforce enhancement and geriatric syndromes. Qualifications Applicants must have a doctoral degree (MD or DO) in an appropriate field from an accredited institution; a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service; and personal and professional goals that are consistent with the mission of the FSU College of Medicine. Applicants must have completed an approved U.S. Residency Program. Applicants must have Board Certification in Geriatric Medicine, or the ability to obtain within one year of hire and participate in maintenance of certification. Must possess or obtain a valid Florida license to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes. Ability to foster an educational environment conducive to patient-centered medical students, physician assistants and other healthcare students' education. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching healthcare students is highly desired. Relevant academic, clinical, and professional experience; excellent skills in communication and collaboration; and be passionate about the field of geriatric medicine. Contact Info Regina Scott: regina.scott@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a clinician-educator position and is not tenure-earning eligible. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
