    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=60738&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Standardized Patient Coordinator (Clinical Learning Center - Medicine)",
      "description": "Job Title Standardized Patient Coordinator (Clinical Learning Center - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 60738 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Clinical Learning Center Responsibilities Coordinates all aspects of the Standardized Patient (SP) Program in the Clinical Learning Center (CLC) to provide encounters that allow students/residents to practice and be evaluated. Oversees and assists with orientation, training, evaluation and quality improvement and assurance of the SPs by monitoring SP portrayal and documentation accuracy and counseling to improve performance. Manages data within the SP Program to include the collection and analysis of data, preparation of reports and payments, assessing SP performance and provisions of data to faculty evaluation of student performance. Maintains and prints reports as requested by the Director of the CLC. Assists in preparing for, and coordinating, the CLC and FOSCE (formative objective student clinical examination)/OSCE (objective student clinical examination) sessions, as requested by the Director of the CLC, including software programming for student and faculty evaluation. Assists with Outreach & Advising SSTRIDE Summer Camp; provides visiting groups with tours of facilities including Harvey sessions and interactions as health care providers, etc. Responsible for exam rooms being equipped with appropriate books, medical supplies and equipment and maintains sufficient inventory levels. Performs outreach marketing services to increase awareness of SP Program at FSU College of Medicine. In addition, recruits and manages the SPs. Promotes an atmosphere of teamwork in accomplishing the mission and goals of the FSU COM to include participating in the delivery of academic support services for special projects or in meeting key departmental deadlines. Other related duties as deemed by the Director of the CLC. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent experience equal to six years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Contact Info Debra Danforth (debra.danforth@med.fsu.edu) Main number (850) 644-9800 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range Low $50,000’s, commensurate with experience/education. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised as Open Until Filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63247&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Technical Research Designer, Level I (Control Room - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)",
      "description": "Job Title Technical Research Designer, Level I (Control Room - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63247 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Operate and maintain facility equipment and systems in support of the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory’s DC high magnetic field user program. Interact with and assist users, research faculty, technicians and other National High Magnetic Field Laboratory staff on the operation and maintenance of the facility. Facility Operations & System Monitoring Monitor and safely operate facility equipment and systems. Coordinate with the City of Tallahassee’s Electrical Distribution Control Room with regards to facility operations and power levels. Take the proper corrective actions in response to alarms or other indications of abnormal equipment operation. Exercise skilled independent judgement in handling facility operations as well as unexpected or emergency situations. Distributed Control System (DCS) Engineering Perform engineering functions on the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Distributed Control System (DCS) such as graphic, trend group and control group building, logic development and troubleshooting, field device integration. Use knowledge of the DCS to perform troubleshooting between the DCS and field devices. Safety & Compliance Coordinate, prepare and issue Lock, Tag, Verify procedures for facility maintenance, troubleshooting and repair in accordance with National High Magnetic Field Laboratory safety policies and procedures. Work with other National High Magnetic Field Laboratory personnel in the evaluation and development of safety policies and procedures. Take a proactive attitude and make solution-oriented contributions to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory safety program. Maintenance & System Performance Assist Facility engineers, staff and scientists with the development of preventative maintenance programs and procedures. Assist Facility engineers and staff in tracking the performance and characteristics of the water-cooled magnets. Contribute to equipment and system characterization, troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance, installation, integration and commissioning. Training & User Support Provide training to users and staff on safe magnet operations, safe overhead crane operations and other safety procedures as necessary. Engineering Support & Projects In consultation with supervisor(s) and design engineers, assist with determining changes in design and operation of plant and power equipment to improve operations, capabilities, reliability and uptime. Contribute to facility projects. Giving tours. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Minimum salary of $47,660, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Participate in on-call duties. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63230&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate – Computational Solid Mechanics at the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering",
      "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate – Computational Solid Mechanics at the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63230 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering Responsibilities The successful candidate will join a highly interdisciplinary team of engineers, computer scientists, applied mathematicians, and computational scientists to develop next-generation computational methods, publish in leading journals and conferences, mentor graduate students, and contribute to major federally funded research initiatives. Develop next-generation numerical methods for computational solid mechanics. Design and implement robust finite element algorithms for nonlinear mechanics problems. Develop AI-enabled acceleration strategies for nonlinear finite element analysis and large-scale computational mechanics. Develop novel iterative solvers, multigrid methods, Krylov subspace algorithms, learned preconditioners, and nonlinear solution strategies for large-scale mechanics problems. Develop scalable computational algorithms for large-scale engineering and biomedical simulations Advance the state of the art in computational solid mechanics, scientific computing, numerical linear algebra, and scientific machine learning. Conduct large-scale computational simulations and analyze numerical results. Publish research in leading journals and conferences in computational mechanics, scientific computing, applied mathematics, and computational engineering. Collaborate with researchers across engineering, computer science, applied mathematics, and biomedical engineering. Contribute to competitive research proposals to federal agencies and private foundations. Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Qualifications Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline. Strong background in computational solid mechanics, finite element methods, scientific computing, numerical methods, or computer graphics. Excellent programming skills in C/C++ and Python, with experience developing large-scale scientific software. Experience with object-oriented software development and modern software engineering practices. Demonstrated record of scholarly publications in high-quality conferences and peer-reviewed journals. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary research environments. Preferred Qualifications Experience with nonlinear finite element methods and computational mechanics. Experience with iterative solvers, multigrid methods, Krylov subspace methods, preconditioning techniques, and nonlinear solution algorithms. Experience developing scientific machine learning, AI-based acceleration techniques, or learned numerical methods for computational mechanics. Experience with reduced-order modeling, multiscale methods, uncertainty quantification, or high-performance scientific computing. Experience developing computational simulation, visualization, or interactive software systems. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Other Information About the College of Engineering Located in Tallahassee, Florida, the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering is the nation's only jointly operated college of engineering, combining the complementary strengths of Florida State University and Florida A&M University. The College offers an exceptionally collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with internationally recognized expertise in artificial intelligence, computational science, quantum science and engineering, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, high-performance computing, and materials research. Faculty and students benefit from close collaborations with the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Center for Advanced Power Systems, regional healthcare partners, and a growing network of federal laboratories and industry collaborators. Helpful The NexCom Laboratory (Laboratory for Next-Generation Computation) at the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate in Computational Surgery. The NexCom Laboratory develops next-generation computational methods that integrate scientific computing, artificial intelligence, and emerging computational paradigms to solve challenging problems in engineering, medicine, and science. Our research spans computational mechanics, scientific computing, computer graphics, machine learning, computational modeling, and quantum computing, with an emphasis on developing transformative computational technologies with real-world impact. Our research focuses on nonlinear computational solid mechanics, finite element methods, scientific machine learning, iterative and nonlinear solvers, multigrid methods, Krylov subspace methods, reduced-order modeling, multiscale modeling, and high-performance scientific computing. We are particularly interested in developing AI-enabled acceleration strategies that improve the convergence, efficiency, robustness, and scalability of numerical algorithms for large-scale nonlinear mechanics problems. Contact Info Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De , Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63217&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Psychiatrist, Clinical Director | FSU BehavioralHealth",
      "description": "Job Title Psychiatrist, Clinical Director | FSU BehavioralHealth Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63217 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine | Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc. FSU BehavioralHealth™ 2507 Callaway Rd. Tallahassee, FL 32303 Responsibilities Provide quality outpatient psychiatric medical care that aligns with the College of Medicine's mission, goals, and objectives, while adhering to current standards of psychiatric practice. Demonstrate clinical leadership and collaboration in support of patient care, education, and program development, with experience in academic medicine. Document patient history, mental and emotional state, diagnostic evaluation, treatment and disposition and clinically appropriate and timely coding for insurance reimbursement in the patient's Electronic Medical Record. Complete clinically appropriate and timely coding for accurate insurance reimbursement including treatment plan as required. Serves as Practice Clinical Director for FSU BehavioralHealth™, providing leadership and oversight for patient care, safety, quality improvement, clinic operations, and patient experience. Acts as a primary resource for clinicians, collaborates with Practice Managers on operational and budgetary matters, and fosters positive clinician and staff relationships. Oversees clinician meetings, performance management, supervision, coverage, and call schedules. Ensures compliance with regulatory and reimbursement requirements and supports the development of clinical protocols, policies, emergency procedures, and quality improvements initiatives. Provides comprehensive psychiatric care by evaluating patients, diagnosing mental health conditions, developing treatment plans, and coordinating referrals when needed. Collaborates with multidisciplinary healthcare teams to support patient care, monitor treatment progress, and provide patient education, counseling, and appropriate diagnostic testing. May also serve as a clinical preceptor for students and residents and provide consultation to Psychiatric Advanced Practice Registered Nurses (APRNs). Qualifications Doctoral degree (MD or DO) and completion of necessary internship, three years of psychiatric residency, and one year of post-residency in psychiatry. Valid licensure in Florida in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes; or licensed in another state with the ability to obtain FL Licensure within 30 days of hire. Valid Board Certification in Psychiatric Medicine or appropriate discipline. Current Federal DEA license. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification by certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following is required: Current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician from within the past 6 months. Physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician from within the past 6 months. Within 30 days of hire, you must provide: Documentation of vaccination for Tetanus within the last 10 years. Proof of immunization OR positive titers for Hepatitis B. Preferred Qualifications Experience in clinical leadership, especially within academic medicine settings. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63235&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Faculty I,12 month Salaried (Quantum Scientific Computing-FAMU–FSU College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Research Faculty I,12 month Salaried (Quantum Scientific Computing-FAMU–FSU College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63235 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The NexCom Laboratory (Laboratory for Next-Generation Computation) at the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering invites applications for a Research Faculty I position in Quantum Scientific Computing. Responsibilities The successful candidate will play a key role in building a nationally recognized research program in Quantum Scientific Computing. The position offers the opportunity to conduct cutting-edge interdisciplinary research, develop externally funded research programs, build collaborations across engineering, mathematics, computer science, and quantum information science, supervise graduate students and postdoctoral researchers, and help establish the NexCom Laboratory as a leader in next-generation computational science. Develop novel quantum algorithms for scientific computing and engineering applications. Investigate opportunities for quantum advantage in computational mechanics, scientific computing, and engineering simulation. Develop scalable quantum algorithms for finite element methods, linear systems, eigenvalue problems, optimization, and multiscale simulation. Develop algorithms for both NISQ and fault-tolerant quantum computing (FTQC) architectures. Advance modern quantum algorithmic frameworks, including block encoding, QSVT, and quantum linear algebra. Develop quantum machine learning (QML) and hybrid quantum-classical methods for engineering and scientific computing. Implement, benchmark, and evaluate algorithms using state-of-the-art quantum software frameworks and quantum hardware platforms. Collaborate with researchers across engineering, computer science, mathematics, physics, and quantum information science. Lead and contribute to competitive research proposals to federal agencies, industry, and private foundations. Publish research findings in leading journals and conferences. Supervise graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, and research staff. Qualifications Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Computer Science, Physics, Electrical Engineering, Computational Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in scientific computing, computational mathematics, numerical linear algebra, or computational mechanics. Demonstrated knowledge of quantum computing, quantum algorithms, or quantum information science. Strong programming skills in Python and C/C++. Experience with quantum software frameworks such as Qiskit, PennyLane, Cirq, Classiq, or similar platforms. Demonstrated record of scholarly publications in high-quality conferences and peer-reviewed journals. Demonstrated ability to develop innovative research ideas and work collaboratively in interdisciplinary research environments. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing quantum algorithms for scientific computing, computational mechanics, or engineering applications. Experience with quantum machine learning, variational quantum algorithms, hybrid quantum-classical algorithms, or quantum optimization. Background in finite element methods, computational mechanics, scientific computing, numerical linear algebra, or high-performance computing. Experience using cloud-based quantum computing platforms and current quantum hardware. Experience developing externally funded research proposals. Experience mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, or research staff. Other Information About the College of Engineering Located in Tallahassee, Florida, the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering is the nation's only jointly operated college of engineering, combining the complementary strengths of Florida State University and Florida A&M University. The College offers an exceptionally collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with internationally recognized expertise in artificial intelligence, computational science, quantum science and engineering, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, high-performance computing, and materials research. Faculty and students benefit from close collaborations with the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Center for Advanced Power Systems, regional healthcare partners, and a growing network of federal laboratories and industry collaborators. Helpful The NexCom Laboratory develops next-generation computational methods that integrate scientific computing, artificial intelligence, and emerging computational paradigms to solve challenging problems in engineering, medicine, and science. Our research spans computational mechanics, scientific computing, machine learning, computational modeling, computer graphics, and quantum computing, with an emphasis on developing transformative computational technologies with real-world impact. Quantum Scientific Computing is an emerging interdisciplinary field at the intersection of quantum computing, scientific computing, applied mathematics, and computational science. Our research seeks to discover and exploit quantum advantages for computationally intensive problems arising in engineering, physics, and data science. We investigate both Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum (NISQ) and Fault-Tolerant Quantum Computing (FTQC) paradigms, developing algorithms that deliver practical performance gains on near-term quantum hardware while laying the theoretical foundations for scalable quantum scientific computing on future fault-tolerant quantum computers. Current research focuses on quantum algorithms for finite element analysis, computational mechanics, scientific computing, linear systems, eigenvalue problems, reduced-order modeling, multiscale methods, quantum machine learning (QML), and quantum optimization. Emphasis is placed on modern quantum algorithmic frameworks, including block encoding, Quantum Singular Value Transformation (QSVT), quantum linear algebra, and hybrid quantum-classical algorithms. Our goal is to identify, develop, and demonstrate quantum algorithms that provide meaningful quantum advantages for engineering and scientific computing problems across both NISQ and FTQC architectures. Contact Info Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De, Search Committee Chair, at sde@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range This is a 12-month, permanent, non-tenure-track faculty appointment at Florida State University with a competitive salary and benefits package. The starting date for this position is negotiable. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include the following documents: A letter of interest Most current curriculum vitae A research statement The names and contact information of three references Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63236&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenure Track 9 Month Salaried (Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Florida A&M University - Florida State University College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Tenure Track 9 Month Salaried (Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Florida A&M University - Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63236 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Florida A&M University (FAMU)-Florida State University (FSU) College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in Computer Engineering in Tallahassee, Florida. Responsibilities Successful candidates are expected to develop research programs that are internationally recognized with significant and sustained funding, incorporate interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers across campus, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, supervise undergraduate, graduate and post-doctoral researchers, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in computer engineering, computer science, electrical engineering, or a closely related discipline, and demonstrate documented potential for outstanding research. Helpful The ECE Department currently has 37 faculty, 100+ graduate students, 450+ undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $20M. The two universities and outstanding research facilities in the affiliated research buildings/centers provide opportunities for collaboration with faculty in Computer Science and Scientific Computing, the Center for Advanced Power Systems (CAPS) , FAMU Center for Cyber Security , National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL ), Center for Intelligent Systems, Control and Robotics (CISCOR) , FSU Institute of Molecular Biophysics , FSU Jim Moran College of Entrepreneurship , and FSU College of Medicine . The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the college of engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources and mission from our parent organization has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home organization, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at our independent campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven (7) of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Contact Info Applications will be reviewed beginning on December 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Rodney Roberts, Search Committee Chair, at rroberts@eng.famu.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2 to 3-page research statement including research interests and plans and how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page statement on teaching and philosophy No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information We are seeking faculty members with expertise in Computer Networks Security, Data Science, AI, Computer Vision, Robotics & Autonomy, Embedded Computing, and Cyber-physical Systems Security. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63224&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate-Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering",
      "description": "Job Title Postdoctoral Research Associate-Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63224 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Responsibilities The successful candidate will work within a highly interdisciplinary team of engineers, computer scientists, surgeons, and medical educators to develop novel computational methods, publish in leading journals and conferences, mentor graduate students, and contribute to the development of major externally funded research initiatives. Develop novel AI and computer vision algorithms for objective assessment of surgical technical performance from video. Design and evaluate next-generation video foundation models for surgical skill assessment. Develop explainable AI methods that generate clinically meaningful and actionable formative feedback. Develop multimodal computational methods that integrate video, motion, and other data sources to improve assessment accuracy. Investigate longitudinal models of surgical skill acquisition and performance. Collaborate with surgeons and medical educators to validate computational methods using clinical and simulated surgical datasets. Publish research in leading journals and conferences in artificial intelligence, computer vision, biomedical engineering, and surgical education. Contribute to the preparation of competitive proposals to federal agencies and private foundations. Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong background in artificial intelligence, machine learning, computer vision, or computational science Excellent programming skills in Python and experience with modern machine learning frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn. Demonstrated record of scholarly publications in high-quality conferences and peer-reviewed journals. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary research environments. Preferred Qualifications Experience with video understanding, video foundation models, vision-language models, self-supervised learning, or explainable AI. Experience with biomedical imaging, healthcare data, or human performance analysis. Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers. Other Information About the College of Engineering Located in Tallahassee, Florida, the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering is the nation's only jointly operated college of engineering, combining the complementary strengths of Florida State University and Florida A&M University. The College offers an exceptionally collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with internationally recognized expertise in artificial intelligence, computational science, quantum science and engineering, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, high-performance computing, and materials research. Faculty and students benefit from close collaborations with the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, the Center for Advanced Power Systems, regional healthcare partners, and a growing network of federal laboratories and industry collaborators. Helpful The NexCom Laboratory (Laboratory for Next-Generation Computation) at the FAMU–FSU College of Engineering, invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate in AI for Video-Based Surgical Skill Assessment. The NexCom Laboratory develops next-generation computational methods that combine scientific computing, artificial intelligence, and emerging computational paradigms to solve challenging problems in engineering, medicine, and science. Our research spans scientific machine learning, computer vision, explainable AI, quantum computing, and computational modeling, with an emphasis on developing transformative computational technologies with real-world impact. This position offers an exceptional opportunity to help shape the future of AI-enabled surgical education. Our research seeks to fundamentally transform how surgical technical performance is assessed by developing intelligent systems that learn directly from surgical video, objectively evaluate technical skill, provide meaningful formative feedback, and support competency-based surgical training. By combining modern computer vision, video foundation models, self-supervised learning, multimodal machine learning, explainable AI, and human performance modeling, we are developing scalable computational methods that reduce reliance on subjective expert evaluation while improving the consistency, accessibility, and effectiveness of surgical training. Contact Info Questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Suvranu De , Search Committee Chair. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63207&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Project Manager, Strategic Partnerships and Innovation",
      "description": "Job Title Project Manager, Strategic Partnerships and Innovation Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63207 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Strategic Partnerships and Innovation within the Office of Research seeks to fill the Project Manager position. Responsibilities This position is responsible for developing, leading and implementing detailed Project Management Plans (PMP). Manage and lead project teams, direct the work of the activity leaders, prioritize the various lines of effort, and shift resources. Collaborate with all parties associated with projects to ensure they are working according to plan. Implement project management principles and concepts with an in-depth understanding of project controls processes/procedures and systems. Develop and implement processes for meeting deliverables and goals. Is responsible for monitoring projects to keep on track, on schedule, and within budget. Utilize tools such as Smartsheet and Trello to plan and track projects and deliverables. Gather data, conduct data analysis, and create dashboards and reports. Will require working on several projects simultaneously. Prepare regular status reports and advise on critical areas and progress toward milestones. Also will provide operational support including securing and managing resources and facilities. Support events and programs (such as Discovery Days, Industry Days or the Industry Affiliate Program), grants, SPI operations, and large projects. Schedule and facilitate meetings, which includes but is not limited to preparing agendas and meeting minutes by documenting document decisions, identify issues, and identifying action items. Other duties as it relates to the project management and the advancement and implementation of SPI events and objectives. Qualifications Bachelors degree and a minimum of four years or a high school diploma/equivalent and eight years of relevant experience facilitating projects. Preferred Qualifications Four or more years related experience. Experience with Smartsheet or other project management software. Project management certification (PMP). Experience in a research or higher education environment. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at RSCH-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63220&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - American Political Behavior",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - American Political Behavior Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63220 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Political Science - College of Social Sciences & Public Policy Responsibilities The Department of Political Science in the College of Social Sciences & Public Policy at Florida State University seeks applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position to begin in Fall 2027. We seek candidates whose research focuses on American political behavior, including, but not limited to, the political behavior of the general public, groups, or political elites, public opinion, and political psychology. Must be able to offer undergraduate and doctoral level courses in Political Behavior. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Political Science or a related discipline by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. Successful candidates are expected to add to the department’s strengths in quantitative, experimental, and/or formal methods. Contact Info Professor Andy Ballard University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit: A letter of application indicating research and teaching interests A curriculum vitae Writing samples Three letters of recommendations A graduate school transcript Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63229&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Comparative Politics",
      "description": "Job Title Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Comparative Politics Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63229 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Political Science - College of Social Sciences & Public Policy Responsibilities The Department of Political Science in the College of Social Sciences & Public Policy at Florida State University seeks applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position to begin in Fall 2027. We seek candidates whose research focuses on comparative politics. The search is open with respect to specialization within the comparative politics subfield. Must be able to offer undergraduate and doctoral level courses in Comparative Politics. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD degree in Political Science or a related discipline by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research and teaching. Successful candidates are expected to add to the department’s strengths in quantitative, experimental, and/or formal methods. Contact Info Professor Quintin Beazer University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit: A letter of application indicating research and teaching interests A curriculum vitae Writing samples Three letters of recommendations A graduate school transcript Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62492&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of NMR/MRI Program at the NHMFL",
      "description": "Job Title Director of NMR/MRI Program at the NHMFL Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62492 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry | College of Arts & Sciences | National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Responsibilities The National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL, MagLab), in partnership with Florida State University (FSU), invites applications and nominations for the Director of the NMR/MRI Program position. The successful candidate will be appointed as a tenured Full Professor in the Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry in the College of Arts & Sciences. This position offers a unique opportunity to lead a world-class magnetic resonance user facility and research program at the forefront of high-magnetic-field science. The Director will provide visionary scientific and administrative leadership for the NMR/MRI program, overseeing both: A national user facility serving a broad and growing external user community An internationally recognized research program in magnetic resonance science The incumbent will articulate and execute a strategic vision that advances high-magnetic-field instrumentation and experimental capabilities, expands the user base, and integrates emerging technologies into magnetic resonance research and applications. Main Duties Involve: Leading and managing the NMR/MRI user facility, including staff and operations Developing and sustaining a high-impact, externally funded research program Securing funding to expand instrumentation and scientific capabilities Fostering collaborations across institutions and disciplines Enhancing and supporting a broad national and international user community Driving innovation through new methodologies, instrumentation, and data-centric approaches Academic Role: The Director will also contribute to the academic mission of Florida State University through: Participating in graduate and undergraduate education and mentoring Engaging in interdisciplinary research initiatives Qualifications Requirements: A PhD in chemistry, biochemistry, physics, or a related discipline An outstanding record of scientific achievement in solid-state NMR, MRI, or related magnetic resonance techniques Demonstrated successes in leading complex research programs or user facilities Proven ability to secure external funding Preferred Qualifications Experience with national user facilities or large-scale instrumentation programs Expertise in advanced magnetic resonance techniques An established record of excellence in research, teaching, and mentorship consistent with appointment at the Full Professor level A compelling vision for advancing the field through emerging technologies, including AI and data science A demonstrated commitment to fostering a positive and collaborative workplace aligned with MagLab Values Other Information Facilities and Capabilities: The NHMFL NMR/MRI User Program operates a state-of-the-art suite of instruments, including: 1.5 GHz (36 T) Series-Connected Hybrid (SCH) magnet for solid-state NMR Ultra-wide bore 900 MHz system for solid-state NMR and imaging 600 MHz Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (DNP) systems Multiple instruments ranging from 850 MHz, 800MHz, 600MHz, and lower A defining strength of the program is its radio-frequency technology group. It comprises scientists, engineers, and technical staff who design and construct highly efficient, custom-made solid-state NMR probes and MRI coils, enabling rapid development and deployment of novel experimental capabilities. These capabilities support cutting-edge research across physics, chemistry, biology, materials science, and chemical and biochemical engineering, enabled by the MagLab's unique high-field magnet technologies. Contact Info Please direct nominations and inquiries to the Search Committee . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants should submit the following: Curriculum vitae Statement of research accomplishments and future vision Statement of leadership philosophy and vision for the NMR/MRI program Contact information for three references Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications will begin on August 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63146&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Liberty Lab Director - Research Faculty 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Job Title Liberty Lab Director - Research Faculty 12 Month Salaried (Open Rank) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63146 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University Homepage | Institute for Governance & Civics | FSU America’s Liberty Lab is a distinctive program that sets the IGC apart nationally. It uses the methods of the hard sciences and social sciences to study liberty itself. Just as traditional labs test hypotheses through experimentation and data, the Liberty Lab will investigate where and how liberty thrives-and where it does not using polling, surveys, and cognitive science. The Lab will serve as a hub for: data collection and empirical analysis across our four pillars of liberty (constitutional liberty, economic liberty, conscience liberty, and educational liberty); original survey research and public opinion polling; field and natural experiments on policy and institutional design; use of advanced cognitive research methods; and evaluation of real-world laws and regulations. Responsibilities The Institute for Governance and Civics at Florida State University seeks candidates for a Research Faculty position that is also the Lab Director for our cognitive lab, America’s Liberty Lab. We are particularly interested in researchers whose work addresses real policy outcomes. We expect research faculty to publish in academic outlets as well as write white papers and other work read by policy makers. The goal is to link topflight cognitive and academic research with nonpartisan public policy discussions. We seek candidates from a broad array of academic backgrounds, including (but not limited to): psychology, political science, economics, communications, public policy, history, religion, and more. The successful candidate also will be expected to possess sufficient managerial skills to head up the Liberty Lab. The Lab Director will assist with the initial equipping and design of the new cognitive lab facilities, coordinate with faculty over their research, ensure student access to the Lab, work with the IGC Director, the branch head for Data, Analyses, and Polling, and communications team to publicize the Lab's research, and oversee Lab practice and procedures, including IRB approvals, access to lab spaces and equipment and related matters. Applicants should have experience with EEGs, eye tracking, and biopac equipment. Qualifications Minimum Requirements: Completed Ph.D. by the date of hire. Research interests that contribute to the study of liberty and American civics. Potential for high impact publications. Commitment to the mission of enhancing civic awareness as well as a readiness to contribute to the intellectual life and programmatic development of the IGC. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree upon taking the position. Contact Info FSU, Institute for Governance and Civics if you have additional questions Lynn Woodworth jlw25c@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is commiserate upon experience, education and minimal qualifications and salary is competitive. Candidates will be considered for open rank. This appointment will initially be for one year. Renewal will be based on satisfactory performance. FSU’s research faculty positions are not tenured but do contain renewal protections. There is no expectation of teaching with a research faculty position at FSU. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63058&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research & Special Projects Librarian, 12-Month Salaried",
      "description": "Job Title Research & Special Projects Librarian, 12-Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63058 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Research Center Responsibilities Florida State University seeks a creative, enthusiastic, and innovative law librarian to serve as the Research & Special Projects Librarian. This position provides research and reference support to College of Law faculty and students and contributes to specialized library initiatives supporting the College's research, teaching, and public service mission. In addition to core research and instruction responsibilities, this librarian will have a dedicated role in developing and supporting special projects, including work on the Florida Workers' Compensation Archive and research support for the Election Law Center. These projects offer an opportunity to contribute to innovative, high-impact work involving legal research, archival and digital collections, and public-facing legal information resources. Provides reference and research support to faculty and student research, including in-depth research assistance at the reference desk, email support, and in-person consultations. Contributes to the development, organization, description, promotion, and sustainability of special projects, including the Florida Workers' Compensation Archive. Provides research, current awareness, and resource development support for the Election Law Center, in collaboration with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders. Works collaboratively on projects involving digital collections, archival materials, government information, legal history, and specialized research resources. Participates in legal research instruction via workshops, guest lectures, and other opportunities in various formats, including online, hybrid, and face-to-face instruction. Contributes to the College of Law and the profession through committee work, research, publishing, and/or participation in professional organizations. Represents the Research Center on various colleges, campus, and library system committees and at meetings and other functions. Facilitates collaborative relationships within the College of Law and with campus partners. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree from an accredited institution in library science and appropriate experience as a professional librarian consistent with university guidelines. Preferred Qualifications J.D. and Master's in library science from accredited institutions. Alternatively, substantial experience as a professional librarian or researcher that meets university guidelines may substitute for one of the degrees. Proficiency in legal research and information technologies. Excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills and the ability to work effectively and collaboratively with varied groups. Excellent organizational, project management, time-management, and analytical skills. Strong service orientation and the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to meet the Research Center's research, service, and leadership requirements. Other Information Overview: This librarian will be part of a highly collaborative, forward-thinking library that is a valued contributor to the College of Law's mission. The ideal candidate will have strong legal research skills, excellent communication and organizational abilities, the ability to thrive in a team-oriented environment and be eager to develop or apply experience in archival or special collections work. We welcome experienced and entry-level applicants, including Spring/Summer 2026 graduates. Environment: The Florida State University Legal Research Center is an innovative, exciting library with a collaborative approach to decision-making. The library serves Florida State University faculty, staff and students, students and faculty of other local colleges and universities, attorneys, and the general public. The College of Law offers an intellectually rigorous legal education in a welcoming, collegial atmosphere that is supportive of students, faculty, and staff. Florida State University is located in Tallahassee, Florida's beautiful capital city, a place that combines the atmosphere and amenities of a larger city with the charm and affordable cost of living in a smaller town. Florida has no state or local income tax. Contact Info Elizabeth Farrell Clifford University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Please include a cover letter with a complete statement of qualifications, a full resume of education and relevant experience, and the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of at least three people who are knowledgeable about your qualifications for this position. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This is a full-time, 12-month specialized faculty appointment, though we welcome applications from candidates interested in a reduced FTE arrangement (minimum .75 FTE). Relocation assistance may be available for the successful candidate. This position is being advertised as open until filled . The start date is flexible. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63053&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63053 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a robust externally funded research program, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to create and sustain an internationally recognized research program in their field of expertise, and have a strong interest in engineering education. Other Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent organizations has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing the prerequisites at their home universities, FAMU and FSU students learn, study, and research together at our independent campus, with jointly appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 150+ graduate students, ~800 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $36M. A new graduate program in Aerospace Engineering started in the fall of 2025 within the Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Department. Additional investments in aerospace include over $100M investments in our Panama City, FL campus Inspire . We expect that the candidate would join our existing Center for Intelligent Systems, Control, and Robotics (CISCOR), but outstanding opportunities exist for collaboration with a number of additional centers of excellence including: the High Performance Materials Institute (HPMI,), the Florida Center for Advanced Aero-Propulsion (FCAAP), and the Aerospace, Mechatronics and Energy Center (AME). Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit our website Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering . Contact Info The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Jonathan Clark, Search Committee Chair, at clarkj@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for tenure-track faculty positions in the field of dynamics and control in Tallahassee, Florida. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. We are interested in candidates whose robotic research is grounded in mechanical engineering, including but not limited to aerial/aquatic/space robotics, dynamics/mechanisms, soft robotics, manipulation/surgical robotics, human-robot interface, sensing and perception, Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning, and Optimal/feedback controls. Other areas of Dynamics and controls will also be considered, particularly if they complement existing program strengths. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Application review will begin on September 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63052&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor. 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering)",
      "description": "Job Title Open Rank Professor. 9 Month Salaried (Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Florida A&M University – Florida State University College of Engineering) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63052 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering at the Florida A&M University-Florida State University College of Engineering Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a robust externally funded research program, have a strong commitment to teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate courses, and participate in college and professional service. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related discipline, demonstrate the ability to create and sustain an internationally recognized research program in their field of expertise, and have a strong interest in engineering education. Other Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State universities. This unique combination of focus, resources, and mission from our parent university has created on our campus a truly innovative atmosphere that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU model with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing the prerequisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study, and research together at our independent campus, with jointly appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university and from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida and are accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Additionally, all seven of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET . Helpful The MAE Department currently has about 36 faculty, 150+ graduate students, ~800 undergraduate students, and annual research expenditures exceeding $36M. A new graduate program in Aerospace Engineering started in the fall of 2025 within the Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Department. Additional investments in aerospace include over $100M investments in our Panama City, FL campus Inspire. We expect that the candidate would join our existing Florida Center for Advanced Aero-Propulsion (FCAAP), and outstanding opportunities exist for collaboration with a number of additional centers of excellence including: the High Performance Materials Institute (HPMI), the Center for Intelligent Systems, Control, and Robotics (CISCOR), and the Aerospace, Mechatronics and Energy Center (AME). Potential applicants seeking more information are encouraged to visit Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering . Contact Info Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Chiang Shih, Search Committee Chair, at shih@eng.famu.fsu.edu . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita and include: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 2-page research statement. This statement should clearly indicate how the proposed research efforts will connect to other efforts in the department and universities. A 1-page teaching statement No more than four selected publications for review The names and contact information of four potential references Faculty Information The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering is pleased to invite applications from highly qualified individuals for tenure-track faculty positions in the field of Aerospace (Propulsion, Structures, and Space Guidance, Navigation, and Controls) in Tallahassee, Florida. This position is at the assistant level, but well-qualified candidates will be considered at a higher rank. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The appointment is anticipated to begin in August 2027. Application review will begin on September 1, 2026. Acceptance and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
